#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2042
msgid "`Add`, `Sub`, `Mul`, `Div` and `Neg` for `BallFloat` and `BallFloatDecorated`"
msgstr "`BallFloat` 和 `BallFloatDecorated` 的 `Add`、`Sub`、`Mul`、`Div` 和 `Neg`"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2044
msgid "`BallFloat` implements `Add`, `Sub`, `Mul`, `Div` and `Neg`; `BallFloatDecorated` implements `Add`, `Sub`, `Mul` and `Div`. The operators call the methods of the same name."
msgstr "`BallFloat` 实现了 `Add`、`Sub`、`Mul`、`Div` 和 `Neg`；`BallFloatDecorated` 实现了 `Add`、`Sub`、`Mul` 和 `Div`。这些运算符调用同名方法。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2062
msgid "`Show` writes an interval in an exact text form."
msgstr "`Show` 以精确的文本形式输出区间。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2076
msgid "A bounded `BallFloat` prints as `center +/- radius` with both numbers in the exact `BinFloat` notation (`3p-1` is $3 \\cdot 2^{-1}$), so the text denotes exactly the stored set (up to the far-endpoint case: endpoints more than about $2^{16}$ binary orders of magnitude apart print with a sticky surrogate for the smaller one); an unbounded one prints as `[lo, hi]`, Empty as `[empty]`. A decorated interval appends `_` and the decoration; NaI prints as `[nai]`."
msgstr "有界的 `BallFloat` 输出为 `center +/- radius`，两个数都使用精确的 `BinFloat` 记法（`3p-1` 表示 $3 \\cdot 2^{-1}$），因此文本恰好表示所存储的集合（远端点情形除外：端点在二进制数量级上相差超过约 $2^{16}$ 时，较小的端点以一个粘滞替身输出）；无界的输出为 `[lo, hi]`，Empty 输出为 `[empty]`。装饰区间会附加 `_` 及装饰；NaI 输出为 `[nai]`。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2095
msgid "These are the derived `Eq` and `Debug` methods of the structures."
msgstr "这些是各结构体派生的 `Eq` 和 `Debug` 方法。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2109
msgid "These are the derived `Eq` and `Debug` methods of the enums."
msgstr "这些是各枚举派生的 `Eq` 和 `Debug` 方法。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2120
msgid "The `Eq` implementations of `BallFloat` and `BallFloatDecorated` are the `equal` relation of IEEE 1788-2015 (12.12.9), not equality of representation: `==` compares sets, ignoring precision tags, and on decorated intervals it is false whenever one operand is NaI, so NaI is not equal to itself (as NaN is not), and decorations are ignored. `identical` is the equality of the datum. `to_repr` gives the structural `Debug` form. The `Eq` of `Decoration` and `OverlapState` is the equality of the variants."
msgstr "`BallFloat` 和 `BallFloatDecorated` 的 `Eq` 实现是 IEEE 1788-2015（12.12.9）的 `equal` 关系，而不是表示的相等：`==` 比较集合，忽略精度标记；在带装饰的区间上，只要有一个操作数是 NaI 它就为假，所以 NaI 不等于它自己（NaN 同理），并且装饰被忽略。`identical` 是数据本身的相等。`to_repr` 给出结构化的 `Debug` 形式。`Decoration` 和 `OverlapState` 的 `Eq` 是各变体的相等。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2130
msgid "`BallFloat` implements the enclosure relation traits of `Luna-Flow/arithmetic`."
msgstr "`BallFloat` 实现了 `Luna-Flow/arithmetic` 的包络关系 trait。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2140
msgid ""
"`Contains::contains(x, y)` is `y.subset(x)` (set inclusion, not the point-taking method). `Overlaps::overlaps(x, y)` is $\\underline{x} \\le \\overline{y} \\wedge \\underline{y} \\le \\overline{x}$, that is $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap \\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\emptyset$, and `MaybeEq::maybe_eq` is the same relation read as \"the two unknown points may be equal\". `DefinitelyLt::definitely_lt(x, y)` is $\\overline{x} < \\underline{y}$ and `DefinitelyLe::definitely_le(x, y)` is $\\overline{x} \\le \\underline{y}$: they hold when the order holds for every pair of points. All four are false when an operand is Empty. This differs from `disjoint`, `precedes` and `strict_precedes`, which are true for an Empty operand (IEEE 1788-2015 Table 10.4): `overlaps` is false where `disjoint` is true, and `definitely_lt` is false where `strict_precedes` is true, so a `true` answer of the traits is always backed by at least one pair of points. These are the generic interface of `Luna-Flow/arithmetic`; the interval package spells the standard relations `disjoint`, `precedes` and `strict_precedes`."
msgstr ""
"`Contains::contains(x, y)` 即 `y.subset(x)`（集合的包含，而不是接受点的那个方法）。`Overlaps::overlaps(x, y)` 为 $\\underline{x} \\le \\overline{y} \\wedge \\underline{y} \\le \\overline{x}$，即 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap \\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\emptyset$，`MaybeEq::maybe_eq` 是同一关系，读作“两个未知的点可能相等”。`DefinitelyLt::definitely_lt(x, y)` 为 $\\overline{x} < \\underline{y}$，`DefinitelyLe::definitely_le(x, y)` 为 $\\overline{x} \\le \\underline{y}$：它们在对每一对点该序都成立时成立。四者在某个操作数为 Empty 时都为假。这与 `disjoint`、`precedes` 和 `strict_precedes` 不同，后三者在操作数为 Empty 时为真（IEEE 1788-2015 表 10.4）：`overlaps` 为假之处 `disjoint` 为真，`definitely_lt` 为假之处 `strict_precedes` 为真，因此这些 trait 返回 `true` 时总有至少一对点作为依据。它们是 `Luna-Flow/arithmetic` 的通用接口；区间包用 `disjoint`、`precedes` 和 `strict_precedes` 来拼写标准关系。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2158
msgid "`BallFloat` implements `DivChecked`, `PowNatChecked` and `PowIntChecked`; their methods are promoted."
msgstr "`BallFloat` 实现了 `DivChecked`、`PowNatChecked` 和 `PowIntChecked`；它们的方法被提升为该类型的方法。"

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:2170
msgid "Only `ctx.precision` is used: the operands are re-rounded to it with `with_precision`, the operation is applied, and the result is re-rounded outward (see [`BallFloat::with_precision`](#ballfloatwith_precision)). At the operands' own precision the result is that of the plain operation; at a lower precision it can be wider. They always return `Ok`. `div_checked` follows the division rules above (a divisor containing 0 gives an unbounded result, not an error). `pow_int_checked` uses `pown`. `pow_nat_checked` uses binary powering by repeated interval multiplication, which treats the factors as independent: for an argument containing 0 its result is wider than `pown`. An Empty base gives Empty for every exponent, including 0, as `pown` does."
msgstr "只使用 `ctx.precision`：操作数先用 `with_precision` 重新舍入到该精度，再应用运算，然后将结果向外重新舍入（参见 [`BallFloat::with_precision`](#ballfloatwith_precision)）。在操作数自身的精度下，结果与普通运算相同；在更低的精度下结果可能更宽。它们总是返回 `Ok`。`div_checked` 遵循上述除法规则（除数包含 0 时给出无界结果，而不是错误）。`pow_int_checked` 使用 `pown`。`pow_nat_checked` 通过重复的区间乘法进行二进制求幂，这会把各因子视为相互独立：对于包含 0 的参数，其结果比 `pown` 更宽。与 `pown` 一样，Empty 底数对任何指数（包括 0）都给出 Empty。"

