#: manual/api/bin_float_checked.md:491
msgid "Each unary elementary function `name` has two wrapper methods. `name()` is `bind` of `BinFloat::try_name_ctx` under `BinaryContext::new(precision=x.precision())`, that is nearest-even rounding to the operand's precision with no exponent limit; `name_ctx(ctx)` uses the given context instead. A success is the correctly rounded value of `bin_float`. The flags of the step are mapped as for `div`: the invalid operation exception (a signaling NaN operand, or an argument outside the domain of IEEE 754-2019 Table 9.1) is a `DomainError`, divideByZero (a pole, §9.2) is a `DivisionByZero` error, and overflow, underflow and inexact are dropped. Besides the errors listed below, every function can report a `CertificationFailure` when `bin_float` cannot certify the rounding within its refinement budget (see [`bin_float` elementary functions](bin_float.md#elementary-functions)); the `CertificationFailureDetail` names the function. The messages of the other errors name it too: `name: invalid operation` and `name: division by zero`, so that in a chain of steps the message says which one failed. A quiet NaN operand gives a successful NaN."
msgstr "每个一元初等函数 `name` 都有两个包装方法。`name()` 是 `BinFloat::try_name_ctx` 在 `BinaryContext::new(precision=x.precision())` 下的 `bind`，即以就近舍入（偶数优先）舍入到操作数的精度，且无指数限制；`name_ctx(ctx)` 则改用给定的上下文。成功值是 `bin_float` 的正确舍入值。该步骤的标志按与 `div` 相同的方式映射：无效运算异常（信号 NaN 操作数，或超出 IEEE 754-2019 表 9.1 定义域的参数）为 `DomainError`，除以零（极点，§9.2）为 `DivisionByZero` 错误，上溢、下溢和不精确则被丢弃。除下文列出的错误外，当 `bin_float` 无法在其细化预算内认证舍入时，每个函数都可能报告 `CertificationFailure`（参见 [`bin_float` 初等函数](bin_float.md#elementary-functions)），其 `CertificationFailureDetail` 指明函数名。其他错误的消息也指明函数名：`name: invalid operation` 和 `name: division by zero`，这样在一连串步骤中，消息就能说明是哪一步失败。静默 NaN 操作数得到一个成功的 NaN。"

