msgstr "端点是具有 $p$ 位有效位的 `BinFloat` 数，因此精确的端点值必须经过舍入。记 $F_p$ 为 $p$ 位二进制数的集合，并且"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:99
msgid "Three properties follow directly from these definitions:"
msgstr "由这些定义可直接得到三条性质："

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:109
msgid "(ii) holds because the set maximized for $\\operatorname{RD}_p(b)$ contains the one for $\\operatorname{RD}_p(a)$; (iii) follows from (ii), since the minimum over $S$ is attained at $\\min S$. Hence, if $L \\le \\inf A$ and $U \\ge \\sup A$ for a set $A$,"
msgstr "(ii) 成立是因为对 $\\operatorname{RD}_p(b)$ 取最大值的集合包含对 $\\operatorname{RD}_p(a)$ 取最大值的集合；(iii) 由 (ii) 推出，因为在 $S$ 上的最小值在 $\\min S$ 处取得。因此，若对集合 $A$ 有 $L \\le \\inf A$ 且 $U \\ge \\sup A$，则"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:118
msgid "This is the only way rounding enters the package: each operation computes a lower bound $L$ and an upper bound $U$ of the exact range and stores $\\operatorname{RD}_p(L)$ and $\\operatorname{RU}_p(U)$. Property (iii) means it does not matter whether candidates are rounded before or after taking the minimum; the code rounds the extremal candidate once (`quantize_interval`)."
msgstr "这是舍入进入本包的唯一途径：每个运算计算精确值域的下界 $L$ 和上界 $U$，并存储 $\\operatorname{RD}_p(L)$ 和 $\\operatorname{RU}_p(U)$。性质 (iii) 意味着候选值在取最小值之前还是之后舍入并无区别；代码只对极值候选舍入一次（`quantize_interval`）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:124
msgid "The width added by rounding is at most one unit in the last place per endpoint. For $2^{e} \\le |a| < 2^{e+1}$ the $p$-bit numbers near $a$ are spaced $\\operatorname{ulp}_p(a) = 2^{e-p+1}$ apart, so $\\operatorname{RU}_p(a) - a < \\operatorname{ulp}_p(a) \\le 2^{1-p}|a|$, and likewise for $\\operatorname{RD}_p$. For a sum with exact range $[S_\\ell, S_u]$:"
msgstr "舍入增加的宽度在每个端点至多为一个末位单位。对于 $2^{e} \\le |a| < 2^{e+1}$，$a$ 附近的 $p$ 位数之间的间距为 $\\operatorname{ulp}_p(a) = 2^{e-p+1}$，因此 $\\operatorname{RU}_p(a) - a < \\operatorname{ulp}_p(a) \\le 2^{1-p}|a|$，$\\operatorname{RD}_p$ 同理。对于精确范围为 $[S_\\ell, S_u]$ 的和："

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:139
msgid "using $S_u - S_\\ell = w(\\boldsymbol{x}) + w(\\boldsymbol{y})$. Widths therefore grow additively through a computation, plus a relative $2^{1-p}$ per rounding. The relative bound needs $a$ inside the normal range of `BinFloat`, $2^{e_{\\min}} \\le |a| < 2^{e_{\\max}+1}$ with $e_{\\min} = -(2^{30} - 1)$ and $e_{\\max} = 2^{30} - 1$. Below $2^{e_{\\min}}$ the directed kernels round on a subnormal grid, and the error is only bounded absolutely, by $2^{e_{\\min} - p + 1}$; above the range an upper endpoint becomes $+\\infty$. Both happen only for magnitudes near $2^{\\pm 2^{30}}$."
msgstr "这里用到了 $S_u - S_\\ell = w(\\boldsymbol{x}) + w(\\boldsymbol{y})$。因此宽度在计算过程中以加法方式增长，每次舍入再加上相对量 $2^{1-p}$。该相对界要求 $a$ 位于 `BinFloat` 的正规范围之内，即 $2^{e_{\\min}} \\le |a| < 2^{e_{\\max}+1}$，其中 $e_{\\min} = -(2^{30} - 1)$，$e_{\\max} = 2^{30} - 1$。低于 $2^{e_{\\min}}$ 时，定向内核在次正规网格上舍入，误差只有绝对界 $2^{e_{\\min} - p + 1}$；超出范围时，上端点变为 $+\\infty$。两者都只在量级接近 $2^{\\pm 2^{30}}$ 时发生。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:148
msgid "Endpoint formulas"
msgstr "端点公式"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:150
msgid "`BallFloat` stores the two endpoints (see [Endpoints, not midpoint and radius](#endpoints-not-midpoint-and-radius)), so each operation is a formula in the endpoints."
msgstr "`BallFloat` 存储两个端点（参见[存储端点，而非中点与半径](#endpoints-not-midpoint-and-radius)），因此每个运算都是关于端点的公式。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:154
msgid "**Sum and difference.** $\\xi + \\eta$ is increasing in both arguments and $\\xi - \\eta$ is increasing in $\\xi$ and decreasing in $\\eta$, so the extremes over the box are at the corners that make each argument extreme in the right direction:"
msgstr "**和与差。** $\\xi + \\eta$ 对两个参数均递增，$\\xi - \\eta$ 对 $\\xi$ 递增、对 $\\eta$ 递减，因此盒子上的极值出现在使每个参数朝正确方向取极值的角点处："

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:166
msgid "**Product.** For fixed $\\eta$, $\\xi \\mapsto \\xi\\eta$ is affine, so its extrema over $\\boldsymbol{x}$ lie at $\\underline{x}$ or $\\overline{x}$; applying the same argument to $\\eta$ gives"
msgstr "**积。** 对固定的 $\\eta$，$\\xi \\mapsto \\xi\\eta$ 是仿射的，因此其在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上的极值位于 $\\underline{x}$ 或 $\\overline{x}$；对 $\\eta$ 运用同样的论证可得"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:175
msgid "The sign pattern decides which elements of $S$ can be extremal. If $\\underline{x}, \\underline{y} \\ge 0$ the product is increasing in both arguments, so the range is $[\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}, \\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y}]$; the other single-sign cases follow from $\\xi\\eta = (-\\xi)(-\\eta) = -((-\\xi)\\eta)$, which gives the table used by `multiplication_bounds`:"
msgstr "符号模式决定了 $S$ 中哪些元素可能取到极值。若 $\\underline{x}, \\underline{y} \\ge 0$，乘积对两个参数均递增，因此值域为 $[\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}, \\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y}]$；其余单一符号的情形由 $\\xi\\eta = (-\\xi)(-\\eta) = -((-\\xi)\\eta)$ 推出，由此得到 `multiplication_bounds` 所用的表格："

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:182
msgid "lower"
msgstr "下界"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:182
msgid "upper"
msgstr "上界"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:188
msgid "other (one of them has $0$ in its interior)"
msgstr "其他（其中之一的内部含有 $0$）"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:190
msgid "The first four rows cover the cases where both operands have constant sign (an operand with a zero endpoint, such as $[0, 2]$, has constant sign; when two rows apply they give the same products). The last row covers the five remaining cases, in which at least one operand straddles 0. Say $\\underline{x} < 0 < \\overline{x}$. The minimum of $S$ is $\\le 0$, because $\\underline{x}\\,\\eta$ and $\\overline{x}\\,\\eta$ have opposite signs for any $\\eta$. If it were attained at $\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y} < 0$, then $\\underline{y} > 0$, hence $\\overline{y} \\ge \\underline{y}$ gives $\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y} \\le \\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$; if at $\\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y} < 0$, then $\\overline{y} < 0$ and $\\overline{x}\\,\\underline{y} \\le \\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$. Either way the minimum is also attained at $\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$ or $\\overline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$ (and a minimum of 0 at $\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$ means $\\underline{y} = 0$, so $\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y} \\le 0$ as well). The maximum and the case where $\\boldsymbol{y}$ straddles 0 are symmetric. So two products suffice for the four single-sign rows and four for the rest."
msgstr "前四行涵盖两个操作数符号都恒定的情形（端点为零的操作数，例如 $[0, 2]$，符号恒定；当两行都适用时，它们给出相同的乘积）。最后一行涵盖其余五种情形，其中至少一个操作数跨越 0。设 $\\underline{x} < 0 < \\overline{x}$。$S$ 的最小值 $\\le 0$，因为对任意 $\\eta$，$\\underline{x}\\,\\eta$ 与 $\\overline{x}\\,\\eta$ 符号相反。若最小值在 $\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y} < 0$ 处取得，则 $\\underline{y} > 0$，于是由 $\\overline{y} \\ge \\underline{y}$ 得 $\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y} \\le \\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$；若在 $\\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y} < 0$ 处取得，则 $\\overline{y} < 0$ 且 $\\overline{x}\\,\\underline{y} \\le \\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$。无论哪种情况，最小值也在 $\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y}$ 或 $\\overline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$ 处取得（而在 $\\underline{x}\\,\\underline{y}$ 处取得的最小值 0 意味着 $\\underline{y} = 0$，因此同样有 $\\underline{x}\\,\\overline{y} \\le 0$）。最大值以及 $\\boldsymbol{y}$ 跨越 0 的情形是对称的。因此，四个单一符号的行只需两个乘积，其余情形需要四个。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:208
msgid ""
"For unbounded intervals all four products are formed with $0 \\cdot \\infty := 0$. This is the right limit for the set-based model: if $\\underline{x} = 0$ and $\\overline{y} = +\\infty$, the products $\\xi\\eta$ with $\\xi \\downarrow 0$ and $\\eta$ fixed tend to 0, while the unbounded growth is already represented by the other corners ($\\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y} = \\pm\\infty$ when $\\overline{x} \\n"
"e 0$)."
msgstr ""
"对于无界区间，四个乘积都按 $0 \\cdot \\infty := 0$ 构成。这对基于集合的模型而言是正确的极限：若 $\\underline{x} = 0$ 且 $\\overline{y} = +\\infty$，则当 $\\xi \\downarrow 0$ 而 $\\eta$ 固定时，乘积 $\\xi\\eta$ 趋于 0，而无界增长已由其他角点表示（当 $\\overline{x} \\n"
"e 0$ 时 $\\overline{x}\\,\\overline{y} = \\pm\\infty$）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:215
msgid ""
"**Division.** IEEE 1788 defines $\\boldsymbol{x}/\\boldsymbol{y} = \\operatorname{hull}\\{\\xi/\\eta : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}, \\eta \\n"
"e 0\\}$. When $0 \\n"
"otin \\boldsymbol{y}$, $1/\\eta$ is continuous and decreasing on $\\boldsymbol{y}$, so $1/\\boldsymbol{y} = [1/\\overline{y}, 1/\\underline{y}]$ and $\\boldsymbol{x}/\\boldsymbol{y} = \\boldsymbol{x} \\cdot (1/\\boldsymbol{y})$; the code evaluates the selected endpoint quotients directly with directed division instead of rounding twice. When $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{y}$:"
msgstr ""
"**除法。** IEEE 1788 定义了 $\\boldsymbol{x}/\\boldsymbol{y} = \\operatorname{hull}\\{\\xi/\\eta : \\xi \\in \\boldsymbol{x}, \\eta \\in \\boldsymbol{y}, \\eta \\n"
"e 0\\}$。当 $0 \\n"
"otin \\boldsymbol{y}$ 时，$1/\\eta$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{y}$ 上连续且递减，因此 $1/\\boldsymbol{y} = [1/\\overline{y}, 1/\\underline{y}]$ 且 $\\boldsymbol{x}/\\boldsymbol{y} = \\boldsymbol{x} \\cdot (1/\\boldsymbol{y})$；代码直接用定向除法计算所选的端点商，而不是舍入两次。当 $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{y}$ 时："

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:224
msgid "$\\boldsymbol{y} = \\{0\\}$: no admissible $\\eta$, the result is $\\emptyset$."
msgstr "$\\boldsymbol{y} = \\{0\\}$：不存在可取的 $\\eta$，结果为 $\\emptyset$。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:225
msgid ""
"$\\underline{y} < 0 < \\overline{y}$, $\\boldsymbol{x} \\n"
"e \\{0\\}$: $\\eta$ approaches 0 from both sides, so $\\xi/\\eta$ is unbounded in both directions: Entire."
msgstr ""
"$\\underline{y} < 0 < \\overline{y}$，$\\boldsymbol{x} \\n"
"e \\{0\\}$：$\\eta$ 从两侧趋于 0，因此 $\\xi/\\eta$ 在两个方向上都无界：Entire。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:228
msgid ""
"$\\boldsymbol{y} = [0, \\overline{y}]$ with $\\overline{y} > 0$ and $\\underline{x} \\ge 0$, $\\boldsymbol{x} \\n"
"e \\{0\\}$: as $\\eta \\downarrow 0$ with $\\xi = \\overline{x} > 0$, $\\xi/\\eta \\to +\\infty$, and the smallest quotient is $\\underline{x}/\\overline{y}$ (0 when $\\overline{y} = +\\infty$), so the result is $[\\underline{x}/\\overline{y}, +\\infty)$. The cases $\\overline{x} \\le 0$ and $\\boldsymbol{y} = [\\underline{y}, 0]$ are mirror images, obtained from $\\xi/\\eta = (-\\xi)/(-\\eta) = -((-\\xi)/\\eta)$. If $\\boldsymbol{x}$ straddles 0, both signs are unbounded: Entire."
msgstr ""
"$\\boldsymbol{y} = [0, \\overline{y}]$，其中 $\\overline{y} > 0$，且 $\\underline{x} \\ge 0$、$\\boldsymbol{x} \\n"
"e \\{0\\}$：取 $\\xi = \\overline{x} > 0$，当 $\\eta \\downarrow 0$ 时 $\\xi/\\eta \\to +\\infty$，而最小的商为 $\\underline{x}/\\overline{y}$（当 $\\overline{y} = +\\infty$ 时为 0），因此结果为 $[\\underline{x}/\\overline{y}, +\\infty)$。$\\overline{x} \\le 0$ 和 $\\boldsymbol{y} = [\\underline{y}, 0]$ 的情形与之镜像对称，可由 $\\xi/\\eta = (-\\xi)/(-\\eta) = -((-\\xi)/\\eta)$ 得到。若 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 跨越 0，则两侧都无界：Entire。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:236
msgid ""
"$\\boldsymbol{x} = \\{0\\}$ and $\\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\{0\\}$: every admissible quotient is 0."
msgstr ""
"$\\boldsymbol{x} = \\{0\\}$ 且 $\\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\{0\\}$：每个可取的商都为 0。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:238
msgid "An Empty operand gives Empty."
msgstr "Empty 操作数给出 Empty。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:240
msgid "From midpoint–radius to endpoints"
msgstr "从中点–半径到端点"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:242
msgid "Users often know a value as $c \\pm r$. `BallFloat::new(c, r, precision=p)` rounds the center to nearest, $\\tilde c = \\operatorname{RN}_p(c)$, and stores"
msgstr "用户常以 $c \\pm r$ 的形式了解一个值。`BallFloat::new(c, r, precision=p)` 将中心就近舍入为 $\\tilde c = \\operatorname{RN}_p(c)$，并存储"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:250
msgid "*Claim:* $[c - r, c + r] \\subseteq [\\tilde c - R, \\tilde c + R]$. For $|\\xi - c| \\le r$,"
msgstr "*断言：* $[c - r, c + r] \\subseteq [\\tilde c - R, \\tilde c + R]$。对于 $|\\xi - c| \\le r$，"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:261
msgid ""
"The endpoints $\\tilde c \\pm R$ are then formed exactly (they may have more than $p$ bits). The construction is sound but not idempotent: whenever $\\tilde c \\n"
"e c$, the displacement $|c - \\tilde c|$ is added on both sides, so rebuilding an interval whose center needs more than $p$ bits widens it (see [Tightness](#correctness-and-invariants)). `normalized` accepts that; `with_precision` does not use the construction at all. It rounds the endpoints outward directly, which encloses the input at every precision and is the tightest representable enclosure, so it has no rounding-mode argument. The converse view inside the package is exact: the center is $(\\underline{x} + \\overline{x})/2$ and the half-width $(\\overline{x} - \\underline{x})/2$, which are dyadic and need no rounding (the half-width is rounded up only if it underflows the exponent range), so $[\\text{center} - \\text{half-width}, \\text{center} + \\text{half-width}]$ is exactly the stored interval. `Show` prints this pair. The public observers are not this pair: IEEE 1788-2015 12.12.8 defines `mid` as the center rounded to the format and `rad` as the smallest number of the format with the interval inside $[m - r, m + r]$ for that rounded $m$. The half-width around the exact center is too small when the center is not representable (it was returned as `radius` before 0.12, [issue 477](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/floating/issues/477)), so `radius` measures from `midpoint`: it is the larger of $m - \\underline{x}$ and $\\overline{x} - m$, rounded up."
msgstr ""
"随后精确地构成端点 $\\tilde c \\pm R$（它们可能多于 $p$ 位）。该构造是可靠的，但不是幂等的：只要 $\\tilde c \\n"
"e c$，位移 $|c - \\tilde c|$ 就会被加到两侧，因此重建一个中心需要多于 $p$ 位的区间会使其变宽（参见[紧致性](#correctness-and-invariants)）。`normalized` 接受这一点；`with_precision` 则完全不使用该构造。它直接把端点向外取整，这在任何精度下都包含输入，并且是可表示的最紧包络，因此它没有舍入模式参数。包内的反向视图是精确的：中心为 $(\\underline{x} + \\overline{x})/2$，半宽为 $(\\overline{x} - \\underline{x})/2$，它们都是二进有理数，无需舍入（半宽仅在低于指数范围下溢时才向上舍入），因此 $[\\text{center} - \\text{half-width}, \\text{center} + \\text{half-width}]$ 恰好就是所存储的区间。`Show` 打印的正是这一对值。公开的观测量并不是这一对：IEEE 1788-2015 12.12.8 把 `mid` 定义为舍入到该格式的中心，把 `rad` 定义为满足区间位于 $[m - r, m + r]$（$m$ 为该舍入后的值）的该格式下最小的数。当中心不可表示时，精确中心处的半宽过小（0.12 之前它被作为 `radius` 返回，[issue 477](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/floating/issues/477)），所以 `radius` 从 `midpoint` 量起：它是 $m - \\underline{x}$ 与 $\\overline{x} - m$ 中较大者，向上舍入。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:283
msgid "The dependency problem"
msgstr "依赖问题"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:285
msgid "The fundamental theorem treats every occurrence of a variable as an independent point. For $\\boldsymbol{x} = [1, 2]$,"
msgstr "基本定理把变量的每次出现都视为独立的点。对于 $\\boldsymbol{x} = [1, 2]$，"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:292
msgid ""
"The result is correct (it contains 0) but not tight: interval subtraction is the extension of $(\\xi, \\eta) \\mapsto \\xi - \\eta$, and the box $\\boldsymbol{x} \\times \\boldsymbol{x}$ contains $(1, 2)$ and $(2, 1)$. In general only $f(\\boldsymbol{x}) \\subseteq F(\\boldsymbol{x})$ holds. A second theorem of Moore's gives equality, in exact arithmetic and for continuous operations, when each variable occurs at most once in the expression; the condition is sufficient, not necessary ($\\boldsymbol{x} \\cdot \\boldsymbol{x}$ is exact for $\\boldsymbol{x} = [1, 2]$). The same effect explains $\\boldsymbol{x}\\boldsymbol{x} \\supsetneq \\boldsymbol{x}^2$ for $0 \\in \\operatorname{int}\\boldsymbol{x}$ ($[-1, 2]\\cdot[-1, 2] = [-2, 4]$ but $[-1, 2]^2 = [0, 4]$) and *subdistributivity*, $\\boldsymbol{x}(\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z}) \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{x}\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{x}\\boldsymbol{z}$. For this reason the package provides single-occurrence operations — `sqr`, `pown`, `fma`, `hypot`, `cancel_minus` and the elementary functions — whose results are hulls of the true range (up to rounding) rather than products of independent factors. Interval values also do not form a group under addition: `cancel_minus` is the operation that undoes an addition, since $(\\boldsymbol{x} + \\boldsymbol{y}) - \\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\boldsymbol{x}$ in general."
msgstr ""
"结果是正确的（它包含 0），但并不紧致：区间减法是 $(\\xi, \\eta) \\mapsto \\xi - \\eta$ 的扩展，而盒子 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\times \\boldsymbol{x}$ 同时包含 $(1, 2)$ 和 $(2, 1)$。一般而言只有 $f(\\boldsymbol{x}) \\subseteq F(\\boldsymbol{x})$ 成立。Moore 的另一条定理表明：在精确算术下且对连续运算而言，当每个变量在表达式中至多出现一次时等号成立；该条件是充分的而非必要的（对 $\\boldsymbol{x} = [1, 2]$，$\\boldsymbol{x} \\cdot \\boldsymbol{x}$ 是精确的）。同样的效应解释了对 $0 \\in \\operatorname{int}\\boldsymbol{x}$ 有 $\\boldsymbol{x}\\boldsymbol{x} \\supsetneq \\boldsymbol{x}^2$（$[-1, 2]\\cdot[-1, 2] = [-2, 4]$ 但 $[-1, 2]^2 = [0, 4]$），以及*次分配律* $\\boldsymbol{x}(\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{z}) \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{x}\\boldsymbol{y} + \\boldsymbol{x}\\boldsymbol{z}$。因此本包提供单次出现的运算——`sqr`、`pown`、`fma`、`hypot`、`cancel_minus` 以及各初等函数——其结果是真实值域的凸包（至多相差舍入），而不是独立因子的乘积。区间值在加法下也不构成群：`cancel_minus` 才是撤销加法的运算，因为一般而言 $(\\boldsymbol{x} + \\boldsymbol{y}) - \\boldsymbol{y} \\n"
"e \\boldsymbol{x}$。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:312
msgid "Elementary functions: monotonicity, critical points and poles"
msgstr "初等函数：单调性、临界点与极点"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:314
msgid "For a continuous function the range over an interval is an interval, and its endpoints are attained at the endpoints of $\\boldsymbol{x}$ or at critical points inside it. The package uses three patterns."
msgstr "对于连续函数，其在区间上的值域是一个区间，值域的端点在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 的端点或其内部的临界点处取得。本包使用三种模式。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:318
msgid "**Monotone functions** (`exp`, `exp2`, `exp10`, `expm1`, `ln`, `log2`, `log10`, `log1p`, `sqrt`, `sinh`, `tanh`, `asinh`, `acosh`, `atanh`, `asin`, `atan`, and the decreasing `acos`): the range over $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap D_f$ is $[f(\\underline{x}), f(\\overline{x})]$ (swapped for decreasing $f$), so only the endpoints are evaluated, the lower one rounded down and the upper one rounded up. A domain boundary inside the interval is replaced by the limit there ($\\ln \\xi \\to -\\infty$ as $\\xi \\downarrow 0$)."
msgstr "**单调函数**（`exp`、`exp2`、`exp10`、`expm1`、`ln`、`log2`、`log10`、`log1p`、`sqrt`、`sinh`、`tanh`、`asinh`、`acosh`、`atanh`、`asin`、`atan`，以及递减的 `acos`）：在 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\cap D_f$ 上的值域为 $[f(\\underline{x}), f(\\overline{x})]$（对于递减的 $f$ 则交换），因此只需对端点求值，下端点向下舍入，上端点向上舍入。区间内部的定义域边界以该处的极限代替（$\\ln \\xi \\to -\\infty$ 当 $\\xi \\downarrow 0$）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:326
msgid "**Functions with known extrema.** `cosh` has its minimum 1 at 0. `pown` with even exponent has minimum 0 at 0. `sin` attains $+1$ at $\\xi = k\\pi/2$ with $k \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$ and $-1$ at $k \\equiv 3$; `cos` attains $+1$ at $k \\equiv 0$ and $-1$ at $k \\equiv 2$. Between two consecutive critical points both functions are monotone, so with $K = \\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z} : k\\pi/2 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$"
msgstr "**已知极值的函数。** `cosh` 在 0 处取最小值 1。偶数指数的 `pown` 在 0 处取最小值 0。`sin` 在 $\\xi = k\\pi/2$ 处取 $+1$（其中 $k \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$），在 $k \\equiv 3$ 处取 $-1$；`cos` 在 $k \\equiv 0$ 处取 $+1$，在 $k \\equiv 2$ 处取 $-1$。在两个相邻临界点之间这两个函数都是单调的，因此对 $K = \\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z} : k\\pi/2 \\in \\boldsymbol{x}\\}$ 有"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:340
msgid "The code encloses $K$ by $[\\lceil q^-(\\underline{x}) \\rceil, \\lfloor q^+(\\overline{x}) \\rfloor]$, where $q^- \\le 2\\xi/\\pi \\le q^+$ are computed from a certified enclosure $[\\pi^-, \\pi^+]$ of $\\pi$. This set can only be too large: a spurious critical point widens the result to $\\pm 1$, a missed one would break inclusion. When it has four or more elements every residue occurs. `sinpi`, `cospi` and `tanpi` use the exact critical points $k/2$, computed from the dyadic endpoints without any approximation of $\\pi$."
msgstr "代码用 $[\\lceil q^-(\\underline{x}) \\rceil, \\lfloor q^+(\\overline{x}) \\rfloor]$ 包络 $K$，其中 $q^- \\le 2\\xi/\\pi \\le q^+$ 由 $\\pi$ 的认证包络 $[\\pi^-, \\pi^+]$ 计算得到。这个集合只可能偏大：多出一个伪临界点会使结果扩大到 $\\pm 1$，而遗漏一个则会破坏包含性。当它有四个或更多元素时，所有余数都会出现。`sinpi`、`cospi` 和 `tanpi` 使用精确的临界点 $k/2$，它们由二进有理端点计算得到，不涉及对 $\\pi$ 的任何近似。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:348
msgid "**Poles.** $\\tan$ is continuous and increasing between consecutive poles $(2k+1)\\pi/2$. If $K$ contains an odd index the interval may contain a pole and the result is Entire; otherwise it is $[\\tan\\underline{x}, \\tan\\overline{x}]$. For `tanpi`, where the pole positions are exact, a pole at an endpoint gives a half-unbounded result instead. Negative powers and division handle the pole at 0 by the rules of the previous sections."
msgstr "**极点。** $\\tan$ 在相邻极点 $(2k+1)\\pi/2$ 之间连续且递增。若 $K$ 含有奇数下标，则区间可能包含极点，结果为 Entire；否则结果为 $[\\tan\\underline{x}, \\tan\\overline{x}]$。对于极点位置精确已知的 `tanpi`，位于端点上的极点改为给出半无界结果。负幂和除法按前几节的规则处理 0 处的极点。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:355
msgid "`pow(x, y)` on the domain $\\xi > 0$ (and $\\xi = 0$, $\\eta > 0$) writes $\\xi^\\eta = \\exp(\\eta u)$ with $u = \\ln \\xi$. The map $(u, \\eta) \\mapsto \\eta u$ is bilinear, so by the corner argument used for products its extrema over the box $[\\ln \\underline{x}, \\ln \\overline{x}] \\times \\boldsymbol{y}$ are at the corners, and $\\exp$ is increasing: the extrema of $\\xi^\\eta$ are among the four corner values. When $\\underline{x} = 0$, $u \\to -\\infty$ and the corner values become the limits $0$ (for $\\eta > 0$) and $+\\infty$ (for $\\eta < 0$). The code also adds the value 1 when the box crosses $\\xi = 1$ or $\\eta = 0$; such a box contains a point where $\\eta u = 0$, so $e^0 = 1$ already lies between the extreme corner values and the extra candidate is redundant but harmless."
msgstr "`pow(x, y)` 在定义域 $\\xi > 0$（以及 $\\xi = 0$、$\\eta > 0$）上写作 $\\xi^\\eta = \\exp(\\eta u)$，其中 $u = \\ln \\xi$。映射 $(u, \\eta) \\mapsto \\eta u$ 是双线性的，因此按乘积所用的角点论证，它在盒子 $[\\ln \\underline{x}, \\ln \\overline{x}] \\times \\boldsymbol{y}$ 上的极值位于角点，而 $\\exp$ 是递增的：$\\xi^\\eta$ 的极值就在四个角点值之中。当 $\\underline{x} = 0$ 时 $u \\to -\\infty$，角点值变为极限 $0$（$\\eta > 0$ 时）和 $+\\infty$（$\\eta < 0$ 时）。当盒子跨越 $\\xi = 1$ 或 $\\eta = 0$ 时，代码还会加入值 1；这样的盒子包含一个使 $\\eta u = 0$ 的点，因此 $e^0 = 1$ 已经位于极端角点值之间，这个额外的候选是多余的，但无害。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:366
msgid "`atan2` is handled the same way: the result is $[-\\pi, \\pi]$ when the box crosses the branch cut on the negative $\\xi$ axis, and otherwise the extrema over the box are at corners, as the next section shows."
msgstr "`atan2` 的处理方式相同:当盒子穿过负 $\\xi$ 轴上的分支切割时结果为 $[-\\pi, \\pi]$,否则盒子上的极值位于角点,见下一节。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:370
msgid "One evaluation per bound"
msgstr "每个端点一次求值"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:372
msgid "A bound of an interval result needs one directed evaluation, not the two (down and up) of which half used to be discarded, and often not even a second endpoint. Directed rounding is monotone: if $a \\ge b$ then $\\mathrm{RD}(a) \\ge \\mathrm{RD}(b)$ and $\\mathrm{RU}(a) \\ge \\mathrm{RU}(b)$. So the lower bound $\\min_i \\mathrm{RD}(f(c_i))$ over candidate points $c_i$ equals $\\mathrm{RD}(f(c^*))$ where $c^*$ minimises $f$ itself, and likewise for the upper bound. The results are therefore bit-identical to the evaluation of every candidate in both directions; only the argument that $c^*$ is the minimiser has to be written down, once per case."
msgstr "区间结果的一个端点只需要一次定向求值,而不是向下与向上各一次(其中一半曾被丢弃),往往甚至不需要第二个端点。定向舍入是单调的:若 $a \\ge b$,则 $\\mathrm{RD}(a) \\ge \\mathrm{RD}(b)$ 且 $\\mathrm{RU}(a) \\ge \\mathrm{RU}(b)$。因此对候选点 $c_i$ 的下界 $\\min_i \\mathrm{RD}(f(c_i))$ 等于 $\\mathrm{RD}(f(c^*))$,其中 $c^*$ 使 $f$ 本身最小;上界同理。所以结果与对每个候选点做双向求值逐位相同;每种情形只需写出一次 $c^*$ 为极小点的论证。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:382
msgid "Evaluations before"
msgstr "求值次数(之前)"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:382
msgid "After"
msgstr "之后"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:384
msgid "interval division"
msgstr "区间除法"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:384
msgid "2 (one directed quotient per bound)"
msgstr "2(每个端点一次定向商)"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:386
msgid "product, one factor straddling zero, the other sign-definite"
msgstr "乘积,一个因子跨零,另一个符号确定"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:386
msgid "4 products"
msgstr "4 次乘积"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:387
msgid "product with an unbounded factor"
msgstr "含无界因子的乘积"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:387
msgid "8 products"
msgstr "8 次乘积"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:387
msgid "4 (the coefficient product of a finite pair is shared by both directions)"
msgstr "4(有限对的系数乘积由两个方向共用)"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:388
msgid "`pown`, even exponent, negative or zero-containing interval"
msgstr "`pown`,偶指数,负区间或含零区间"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:388
msgid "4 or 3 `pown_ctx`"
msgstr "4 或 3 次 `pown_ctx`"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:389
msgid "8 to 16 `try_atan2_ctx`"
msgstr "8 到 16 次 `try_atan2_ctx`"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:390
msgid "2 (also 2 with one extremum inside, 0 with an extremum of each kind)"
msgstr "2(区间内有一种极值时同样为 2,两种极值都有时为 0)"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:391
msgid "8 exact-rational series per refinement round, plus $\\pi$ per round"
msgstr "每轮细化 8 个精确有理级数,另加每轮一次 $\\pi$"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:391
msgid "2 correctly rounded binary evaluations, and one $\\pi$ enclosure"
msgstr "2 次正确舍入的二进制求值,以及一次 $\\pi$ 包络"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:392
msgid "8 series per round, plus $\\pi$ per round"
msgstr "每轮 8 个级数,另加每轮一次 $\\pi$"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:392
msgid "2 evaluations, and one $\\pi$ enclosure"
msgstr "2 次求值,以及一次 $\\pi$ 包络"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:394
msgid "**Division and square root.** The lower bound of $\\boldsymbol{x} / \\boldsymbol{y}$ is one quotient of two endpoints (chosen by the signs, see the corner argument above) rounded down, the upper bound one quotient rounded up. The square root needs $\\sqrt{\\underline{x}}$ rounded down and $\\sqrt{\\overline{x}}$ rounded up."
msgstr "**除法与平方根。** $\\boldsymbol{x} / \\boldsymbol{y}$ 的下界是两个端点(按符号选取,见上文的角点论证)之商向下舍入,上界是一个商向上舍入。平方根需要向下舍入的 $\\sqrt{\\underline{x}}$ 和向上舍入的 $\\sqrt{\\overline{x}}$。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:400
msgid ""
"**Products.** If $\\boldsymbol{a}$ straddles zero and $\\boldsymbol{b} \\ge 0$ ($\\boldsymbol{b} \\n"
"e [0, 0]$), then $a \\mapsto ab$ is nondecreasing for each $b \\ge 0$ and $b \\mapsto ab$ is nondecreasing for $a \\ge 0$ and nonincreasing for $a \\le 0$, so the minimum is $\\underline{a}\\,\\overline{b}$ and the maximum $\\overline{a}\\,\\overline{b}$ (the other three sign cases are mirror images). Two factors that both straddle zero keep the four products."
msgstr ""
"**乘积。** 若 $\\boldsymbol{a}$ 跨零且 $\\boldsymbol{b} \\ge 0$($\\boldsymbol{b} \\n"
"e [0, 0]$),则对每个 $b \\ge 0$,$a \\mapsto ab$ 不减;对 $a \\ge 0$,$b \\mapsto ab$ 不减,对 $a \\le 0$ 不增。所以最小值是 $\\underline{a}\\,\\overline{b}$,最大值是 $\\overline{a}\\,\\overline{b}$(其余三种符号情形是镜像)。两个因子都跨零时仍保留四个乘积。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:407
msgid "**`atan2`.** Away from the origin and the branch cut, $\\partial \\theta / \\partial y = x / r^2$ and $\\partial \\theta / \\partial x = -y / r^2$. For $y \\ge 0$ the angle is nonincreasing in $x$, so the minimum has $x = \\overline{x}$ and the maximum $x = \\underline{x}$; at that $x$ the angle is nondecreasing in $y$ if $x > 0$, nonincreasing if $x < 0$, and constant ($\\pi/2$) at $x = 0$. For $y \\le 0$ (with $\\underline{y} < 0$) the angle is nondecreasing in $x$ and the same rule applies to $y$. If $\\boldsymbol{y}$ straddles zero the branch-cut case has been excluded, so $\\underline{x} \\ge 0$ and both bounds sit at $x = \\underline{x}$ (the minimum at $\\underline{y}$, the maximum at $\\overline{y}$). A zero endpoint of $\\boldsymbol{y}$ belongs to the side of the other endpoint: $\\mathrm{atan2}(+0, x < 0) = \\pi$ is the limit from $y > 0$ and $\\mathrm{atan2}(0, x > 0) = 0$ the limit from $y < 0$. Every edge of the box is therefore monotone and the extrema over a box are at corners, also when the origin is a corner or lies on an edge, since the angles seen near the origin are those of the neighbouring corners. The axis points that earlier versions added are between these two extremes. A box whose extreme corner is the origin (a degenerate box) uses the general corner hull."
msgstr "**`atan2`。** 远离原点和分支切割处,$\\partial \\theta / \\partial y = x / r^2$,$\\partial \\theta / \\partial x = -y / r^2$。当 $y \\ge 0$ 时角度关于 $x$ 不增,所以最小值在 $x = \\overline{x}$,最大值在 $x = \\underline{x}$;在该 $x$ 处,若 $x > 0$ 则角度关于 $y$ 不减,若 $x < 0$ 则不增,$x = 0$ 时为常数($\\pi/2$)。当 $y \\le 0$(且 $\\underline{y} < 0$)时角度关于 $x$ 不减,对 $y$ 适用同一规则。若 $\\boldsymbol{y}$ 跨零,则分支切割情形已被排除,故 $\\underline{x} \\ge 0$,两个界都在 $x = \\underline{x}$(最小值取 $\\underline{y}$,最大值取 $\\overline{y}$)。$\\boldsymbol{y}$ 的零端点归属于另一端点所在的一侧:$\\mathrm{atan2}(+0, x < 0) = \\pi$ 是 $y > 0$ 方向的极限,$\\mathrm{atan2}(0, x > 0) = 0$ 是 $y < 0$ 方向的极限。因此盒子的每条边都是单调的,盒子上的极值位于角点,原点是角点或落在边上时也一样,因为原点附近出现的角度就是相邻角点的角度。早先版本加入的坐标轴点位于这两个极值之间。极值角点为原点的盒子(退化盒子)使用通用的角点凸包。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:427
msgid "**`sinpi`, `cospi`, `sin`, `cos`.** With the index range $K$ of the previous section, an extremum of each kind inside gives $\\pm 1$ without evaluation. Without any extremum inside, $\\boldsymbol{x}$ lies in one arc between two consecutive extrema and the function is monotone there: sine increases through an index $\\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$ and decreases through $\\equiv 2$ (when $K$ contains an index), and otherwise the arc is $k = \\lceil q^- \\rceil - 1$, increasing for $k \\equiv 0, 3$ and decreasing for $k \\equiv 1, 2$. Cosine is sine shifted by one index. The lower bound is then the endpoint value rounded down at the lower end of the arc direction and the upper bound the other endpoint rounded up; with one extremum inside, the opposite bound is the better of the two endpoints."
msgstr "**`sinpi`、`cospi`、`sin`、`cos`。** 利用上一节的指标范围 $K$,区间内每种极值各有一个时无需求值即得 $\\pm 1$。区间内没有任何极值时,$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 位于相邻两个极值之间的一段弧内,函数在其上单调:正弦在指标 $\\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$ 处上升,在 $\\equiv 2$ 处下降($K$ 含有指标时);否则弧为 $k = \\lceil q^- \\rceil - 1$,$k \\equiv 0, 3$ 时上升,$k \\equiv 1, 2$ 时下降。余弦是平移一个指标的正弦。此时下界是弧方向上较低一端的端点值向下舍入,上界是另一端点向上舍入;区间内有一个极值时,相反方向的界取两个端点中较好的一个。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:439
msgid "**`sin`, `cos`, `tan` (`try_` forms).** Each endpoint value is the correctly rounded value of the binary kernel in the directed mode, which is the value the exact-rational series produced (it rounded an enclosure that rounded uniquely). The enclosure of $\\pi$ is needed only for the index range $K$ (the critical points and the poles); it is taken once from `certified_pi_interval` with $w + 48$ bits, where $w = p + m + 96$ is the working precision of the first refinement round ($p$ the precision of the interval, $m$ the binade of the larger endpoint). Its width, about $2^{-(w + 47)}$, is smaller than that of the rational enclosure of the old refinement loop (about $2^{-(w + 19)}$), so $K$ is contained in the first-round range of the old code. The old code decided a pole at its first round too, so `try_tan` returns the whole line only where the old code did. What is identical by construction: every endpoint value, and the result whenever the old code needed no refinement round. What is not: when the old code refined (an endpoint within about $2^{-w}$ of a multiple of $\\pi/2$) it used a narrower $K$ of a later round, and the new $K$ can then hold a spurious index, only for $|\\xi - k\\pi/2| < 2^{-(p + 140)}$ (an absolute bound that does not depend on the number of bits of the endpoint). A spurious extremum does not change a sine or cosine bound, since that close to an extremum the directed value already rounds to $\\pm 1$; a spurious pole makes the tangent the whole line, which keeps the inclusion property. The tests compare old and new bit for bit on the binary64 number closest to a multiple of $\\pi/2$ ($6381956970095103 \\cdot 2^{797}$) and on the correctly rounded $\\pi/2$ and $3\\pi/2$ with their neighbours at 24, 53 and 113 bits, and no input differs. The non-`try` `sin`, `cos` and `tan` are these `try_` forms with a fallback: they return $[-1, 1]$ (Entire for `tan`) for an argument the kernel cannot certify, which the `try_` forms report as an error."
msgstr "**`sin`、`cos`、`tan`(`try_` 形式)。** 每个端点值是二进制核在定向模式下的正确舍入值,也就是精确有理级数曾给出的值(它对一个唯一舍入的包络进行舍入)。$\\pi$ 的包络只用于指标范围 $K$(临界点与极点);它只从 `certified_pi_interval` 取一次,精度为 $w + 48$ 位,其中 $w = p + m + 96$ 是第一轮细化的工作精度($p$ 为区间精度,$m$ 为较大端点所在的二进制段)。它的宽度约为 $2^{-(w + 47)}$,小于旧细化循环中有理包络的宽度(约 $2^{-(w + 19)}$),所以 $K$ 包含于旧代码第一轮的范围。旧代码在第一轮同样判定极点,因此 `try_tan` 只在旧代码也如此时返回整条实数线。按构造相同的有:每个端点值,以及旧代码不需要细化轮时的整个结果。不相同的情形:旧代码发生细化(端点与 $\\pi/2$ 的倍数相差约 $2^{-w}$ 以内)时使用的是后一轮更窄的 $K$,而新的 $K$ 此时可能含有一个多余的指标,仅当 $|\\xi - k\\pi/2| < 2^{-(p + 140)}$(绝对界,与端点的位数无关)。多余的极值不会改变正弦或余弦的界,因为离极值这么近时定向值本来就舍入为 $\\pm 1$;多余的极点使正切成为整条实数线,这保持包含性。测试对最接近 $\\pi/2$ 倍数的 binary64 数($6381956970095103 \\cdot 2^{797}$)以及 24、53、113 位下正确舍入的 $\\pi/2$、$3\\pi/2$ 及其相邻数逐位对比新旧实现,没有任何输入不同。非 `try` 的 `sin`、`cos` 和 `tan` 就是这些带回退的 `try_` 形式：对内核无法认证的参数，它们返回 $[-1, 1]$（`tan` 为 Entire），而 `try_` 形式会报告错误。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:468
msgid "Certified evaluation of transcendental endpoints"
msgstr "超越函数端点的认证求值"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:470
msgid "$e^{\\underline{x}}$ is not a dyadic number, so an endpoint needs a directed rounding of the exact value: $\\operatorname{RD}_p(f(a))$ is a valid lower endpoint and $\\operatorname{RU}_p(f(b))$ a valid upper endpoint by property (i). This package does not implement the series itself. Each endpoint is evaluated by the certified `try_*_ctx` function of [`bin_float`](bin_float.md) in an unbounded context of the interval's precision, rounded toward $-\\infty$ for a lower bound and toward $+\\infty$ for an upper bound; those functions refine a working precision until the two directed roundings agree (a Ziv-style acceptance test[^ziv]) and report a certification failure when the work budget runs out."
msgstr "$e^{\\underline{x}}$ 不是二进制有限小数，所以端点需要对精确值做定向舍入：$\\operatorname{RD}_p(f(a))$ 是有效的下端点，$\\operatorname{RU}_p(f(b))$ 是有效的上端点（由性质 (i)）。本包自己不实现级数。每个端点由 [`bin_float`](bin_float.md) 中经过认证的 `try_*_ctx` 函数在区间精度的无界上下文中求值，下端点向 $-\\infty$ 舍入，上端点向 $+\\infty$ 舍入；这些函数不断提高工作精度，直到两个定向舍入一致（Ziv 式接受检验[^ziv]），并在工作预算耗尽时报告认证失败。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:481
msgid "What this package adds is the interval analysis around the point kernels: the domain restriction (an argument outside the domain is dropped, and the result is Empty when nothing is left, which is decided by comparisons before any kernel runs), the monotonicity and critical-point analysis of the previous section (which endpoint gives which bound, where an extremum of `sin` or a pole of `tan` lies), the handling of infinite endpoints, and the fallback range. An enclosure of $\\pi$ is needed only to locate critical points and poles of the trigonometric functions, and for the fallbacks of the inverse trigonometric functions; it comes from the cached binary-splitting constant of `bin_float` (`atan(+inf)` is $\\pi/2$ correctly rounded in each direction, and the scaling by 2 is exact)."
msgstr "本包补充的是围绕点内核的区间分析：定义域限制（定义域之外的参数被丢弃，若什么都不剩则结果为 Empty，这在任何内核运行之前通过比较就已判定）、上一节的单调性与临界点分析（哪个端点给出哪个界，`sin` 的极值或 `tan` 的极点在哪里）、对无穷端点的处理，以及回退值域。$\\pi$ 的包络只用于确定三角函数的临界点和极点，以及反三角函数的回退；它来自 `bin_float` 缓存的二分裂常数（`atan(+inf)` 在每个方向上都是正确舍入的 $\\pi/2$，乘以 2 是精确的）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:493
msgid "A. Ziv, \"Fast evaluation of elementary mathematical functions with correctly rounded last bit\", *ACM TOMS* 17(3), 1991; J.-M. Muller et al., *Handbook of Floating-Point Arithmetic*, 2nd ed., Birkhäuser, 2018, §10."
msgstr "A. Ziv，\"Fast evaluation of elementary mathematical functions with correctly rounded last bit\"，*ACM TOMS* 17(3)，1991；J.-M. Muller 等，*Handbook of Floating-Point Arithmetic*，第 2 版，Birkhäuser，2018，§10。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:497
msgid "The IEEE 1788 decoration model"
msgstr "IEEE 1788 装饰模型"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:499
msgid "A bare interval result says where the values lie, not whether the function was defined. IEEE 1788 attaches a *decoration* to each result of evaluating $f$ on a box $\\boldsymbol{x}$:"
msgstr "单纯的区间结果只说明值位于何处，而不说明函数是否有定义。IEEE 1788 为在盒子 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上对 $f$ 求值的每个结果附加一个*装饰*："

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:503
msgid "Decoration"
msgstr "装饰"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:503
msgid "Property $p_d(f, \\boldsymbol{x})$"
msgstr "性质 $p_d(f, \\boldsymbol{x})$"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:505
msgid "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ is non-empty and bounded, $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq D_f$, $f$ is continuous at each point of $\\boldsymbol{x}$, and the result is bounded"
msgstr "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 非空且有界，$\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq D_f$，$f$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 的每一点处连续，且结果有界"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:506
msgid "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ is non-empty, $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq D_f$ and $f \\vert_{\\boldsymbol{x}}$ is continuous"
msgstr "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 非空，$\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq D_f$，且 $f \\vert_{\\boldsymbol{x}}$ 连续"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:507
msgid "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ is non-empty and $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq D_f$"
msgstr "$\\boldsymbol{x}$ 非空且 $\\boldsymbol{x} \\subseteq D_f$"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:508
msgid "always true"
msgstr "恒为真"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:509
msgid "the value is NaI, not an interval"
msgstr "该值为 NaI，不是区间"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:511
msgid "The decorations are totally ordered by strength, $\\text{com} > \\text{dac} > \\text{def} > \\text{trv} > \\text{ill}$, because each property implies the next (continuity of $f$ at each point of $\\boldsymbol{x}$ implies continuity of the restriction, but not conversely: `atan2` restricted to a box lying on its branch cut from above is continuous, while `atan2` is not). A decorated operation $g$ applied to decorated inputs $(\\boldsymbol{y}_j, d_j)$ returns"
msgstr "装饰按强度全序排列，$\\text{com} > \\text{dac} > \\text{def} > \\text{trv} > \\text{ill}$，因为每条性质都蕴含下一条（$f$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 每一点处连续蕴含其限制连续，但反之不然：限制在从上方位于其分支切割上的盒子上的 `atan2` 是连续的，而 `atan2` 本身并不连续）。将装饰运算 $g$ 作用于装饰输入 $(\\boldsymbol{y}_j, d_j)$ 时返回"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:523
msgid "*Why the minimum is sound.* Suppose $\\boldsymbol{y}_j$ was produced by $f_j$ on $\\boldsymbol{x}$ with property $p_{d_j}$, and $g$ has $p_{d_g}$ on the box of the $\\boldsymbol{y}_j$. If $d \\ge \\text{def}$, each $f_j$ is defined on $\\boldsymbol{x}$ with values in $\\boldsymbol{y}_j$ (inclusion property), and $g$ is defined on those values, so $g \\circ (f_1, \\dots, f_k)$ is defined on $\\boldsymbol{x}$. If $d \\ge \\text{dac}$, the same holds for continuity, because a composition of continuous functions is continuous. Boundedness for `com` is a property of the final result and is checked on it. By induction the decoration of a whole expression is a true statement about the expression on the input box. This is what interval existence proofs need: for example, if $\\boldsymbol{x}$ is bounded and $F(\\boldsymbol{x}) \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{x}$ with decoration at least `dac`, the function is continuous on the compact non-empty interval $\\boldsymbol{x}$ and maps it into itself, so Brouwer's theorem gives a fixed point in $\\boldsymbol{x}$. Boundedness matters: $\\xi \\mapsto \\xi + 1$ maps Entire into itself, continuously, without a fixed point. Without the decoration, $\\sqrt{[-1, 4]} = [0, 2]$ would wrongly suggest that $\\sqrt{\\cdot}$ is defined on $[-1, 4]$."
msgstr "*为何取最小值是可靠的。* 假设 $\\boldsymbol{y}_j$ 由 $f_j$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上以性质 $p_{d_j}$ 产生，且 $g$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{y}_j$ 的盒子上具有 $p_{d_g}$。若 $d \\ge \\text{def}$，则每个 $f_j$ 都在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上有定义且取值于 $\\boldsymbol{y}_j$（包含性质），而 $g$ 在这些值上有定义，因此 $g \\circ (f_1, \\dots, f_k)$ 在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上有定义。若 $d \\ge \\text{dac}$，连续性同理成立，因为连续函数的复合仍是连续的。`com` 所要求的有界性是最终结果的性质，在最终结果上检查。由归纳，整个表达式的装饰是关于该表达式在输入盒子上的一个真命题。这正是区间存在性证明所需要的：例如，若 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 有界、$F(\\boldsymbol{x}) \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{x}$ 且装饰至少为 `dac`，则函数在紧的非空区间 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 上连续并将其映入自身，于是由 Brouwer 定理可知在 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 中存在不动点。有界性很重要：$\\xi \\mapsto \\xi + 1$ 连续地将 Entire 映入自身，却没有不动点。若没有装饰，$\\sqrt{[-1, 4]} = [0, 2]$ 会错误地暗示 $\\sqrt{\\cdot}$ 在 $[-1, 4]$ 上有定义。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:542
msgid "The package computes $d_g$ from the operands by the domain tests listed in the [API reference](../api/ball_float.md#decorated-intervals): division by an interval containing 0, a logarithm reaching $\\xi \\le 0$, `sqrt` below 0, a pole of `tanpi` or of a negative-degree `rootn` in the argument and so on give `trv`; `atan2` across its branch cut gives `def` (defined but discontinuous) and touching the cut from above gives `dac`. Set operations (`intersection`, `convex_hull`, `cancel_*`) are not point functions and always give `trv`. The result is made canonical: an empty result is always `trv` (the properties above require a non-empty box), and `com` on an unbounded result becomes `dac` (this is how overflow is reported). NaI, the result of an invalid decorated construction, absorbs every operation, and is distinct from $\\emptyset$, which is a valid set."
msgstr "本包通过 [API 参考](../api/ball_float.md#decorated-intervals)中列出的定义域测试，由操作数计算 $d_g$：除以包含 0 的区间、对数到达 $\\xi \\le 0$、`sqrt` 低于 0、参数中含有 `tanpi` 或负次数 `rootn` 的极点等情形给出 `trv`；`atan2` 跨越其分支切割时给出 `def`（有定义但不连续），从上方触及切割则给出 `dac`。集合运算（`intersection`、`convex_hull`、`cancel_*`）不是逐点函数，总是给出 `trv`。结果会被规范化：空结果总是 `trv`（上述性质都要求盒子非空），无界结果上的 `com` 变为 `dac`（上溢正是这样报告的）。NaI 是无效装饰构造的结果，它吸收所有运算，并且不同于 $\\emptyset$——后者是一个有效的集合。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:555
msgid "Integer functions"
msgstr "整数函数"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:557
msgid ""
"`sign`, `ceil`, `floor`, `trunc`, `roundTiesToEven` and `roundTiesToAway` (IEEE 1788-2015 Table 9.1) are nondecreasing with integer values, so the bare result is $[f(\\underline{x}), f(\\overline{x})]$ and no rounding happens. Their decoration needs one observation: a function with values in $\\mathbb{Z}$ (or $\\{-1, 0, 1\\}$) restricted to an interval is continuous exactly when it is constant on it, by the intermediate value theorem. So the strongest decoration $d_g$ of 11.2 is `def` when $f(\\underline{x}) \\n"
"e f(\\overline{x})$. When $f$ is constant, `dac` holds, and `com` holds when in addition $\\boldsymbol{x}$ is bounded and contains no point where $f$ is discontinuous on the real line. With $k = f(\\underline{x}) = f(\\overline{x})$ that last test is an endpoint comparison, because a constant box lies in a single step of the function:"
msgstr ""
"`sign`、`ceil`、`floor`、`trunc`、`roundTiesToEven` 和 `roundTiesToAway`（IEEE 1788-2015 表 9.1）都是取整数值的非递减函数，所以裸结果为 $[f(\\underline{x}), f(\\overline{x})]$，不发生舍入。它们的装饰只需一个观察：取值于 $\\mathbb{Z}$（或 $\\{-1, 0, 1\\}$）的函数限制在区间上时，由介值定理，连续当且仅当它在该区间上为常数。因此当 $f(\\underline{x}) \\n"
"e f(\\overline{x})$ 时，11.2 的最强装饰 $d_g$ 为 `def`。当 $f$ 为常数时 `dac` 成立；若 $\\boldsymbol{x}$ 还有界且不含 $f$ 在实数轴上的不连续点，则 `com` 成立。记 $k = f(\\underline{x}) = f(\\overline{x})$，最后这一判断是端点比较，因为常数盒位于函数的同一级台阶内："

