#: manual/design/ball_float.md:840
msgid "The tangent (cotangent) interval of a piece has one end per end of $\\Theta_r$: the tangent of an end of $\\boldsymbol{c}$ inside the region, or the limit at a boundary of the region: $\\pm\\infty$ at $\\pm\\pi/2$ for the tangent (at $0$ and $\\pi$ for the cotangent), 0 at $-\\pi$, 0 and $\\pi$ for the tangent. Whether an end of $\\boldsymbol{c}$ is below or above $-\\pi$, $-\\pi/2$, $0$, $\\pi/2$ or $\\pi$ is decided exactly, in seven zones (`atan2_zone`): $\\pi$ is irrational, so a float is never equal to a multiple of it, and only $0$ is an exact angle; the enclosure of $\\pi$ is refined until the float is separated. The product of the operand part with the trigonometric interval is monotone in each variable, so each extreme is the product of two ends, chosen by the signs of the ends of the trigonometric interval (no numerical comparison between corners is needed), and an end is attained only if both factors are: the limit 0 of $b^+$ (when $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{b}$) and the infinities are not attained, $\\tan 0 = 0$ and $\\tan \\pi = 0$ are, and $\\tan(-\\pi) = 0$ is not."
msgstr "每个片段的三角函数值区间对 $\\Theta_r$ 的每个端点有一个端点：区域内 $\\boldsymbol{c}$ 端点的正切（余切），或区域边界处的极限：正切在 $\\pm\\pi/2$ 处为 $\\pm\\infty$（余切在 $0$ 与 $\\pi$ 处），在 $-\\pi$ 处为 0，正切在 $0$ 与 $\\pi$ 处为 0。$\\boldsymbol{c}$ 的端点位于 $-\\pi$、$-\\pi/2$、$0$、$\\pi/2$、$\\pi$ 之下还是之上是精确判定的，共七个区段（`atan2_zone`）：$\\pi$ 是无理数，所以浮点数永远不等于它的倍数，只有 $0$ 是精确角度；$\\pi$ 的包不断细化直到把浮点数分开。操作数部分与三角函数区间的乘积对每个变量都是单调的，所以每个极值是两个端点的乘积，按三角函数区间端点的符号选取（无需在各角点之间做数值比较），且只有两个因子都取得到时端点才取得到：$b^+$ 的极限 0（当 $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{b}$ 时）与无穷取不到，$\\tan 0 = 0$ 与 $\\tan \\pi = 0$ 取得到，$\\tan(-\\pi) = 0$ 取不到。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:851
msgid ""
"*Branch cut and origin.* The angle $\\pi$ is attained and $-\\pi$ never, so $\\pi \\in \\boldsymbol{c}$ puts $y = 0$ into the Rev1 set when $b^- \\n"
"e \\emptyset$ (an end of the upper-left piece, attained) and $x_0 < 0$ into the Rev2 set when $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{a}$, while a $\\boldsymbol{c}$ with lower end $\\le -\\pi$ gives a lower-left piece whose end at $-\\pi$ (the limit of $\\tan$ at $-\\pi$) is open. The origin is excluded: for $\\boldsymbol{b} = \\{0\\}$ there are only the up and down pieces, so $y = 0$ is not reachable and $\\operatorname{atan2Rev1}(\\{0\\}, \\{0\\})$ is Empty; for $\\boldsymbol{a} = \\{0\\}$ there are only the angles $0$ and $\\pi$, so $x_0 = 0$ is not in the set."
msgstr ""
"*分支切割与原点。* 角度 $\\pi$ 取得到而 $-\\pi$ 永远取不到，所以当 $b^- \\n"
"e \\emptyset$ 时 $\\pi \\in \\boldsymbol{c}$ 把 $y = 0$ 放进 Rev1 的集合（左上片段的一个取得到的端点），当 $0 \\in \\boldsymbol{a}$ 时把 $x_0 < 0$ 放进 Rev2 的集合；而下端点 $\\le -\\pi$ 的 $\\boldsymbol{c}$ 给出一个左下片段，其在 $-\\pi$ 处的端点（$\\tan$ 在 $-\\pi$ 处的极限）是开的。原点被排除：对 $\\boldsymbol{b} = \\{0\\}$ 只有上、下片段，所以取不到 $y = 0$，$\\operatorname{atan2Rev1}(\\{0\\}, \\{0\\})$ 为 Empty；对 $\\boldsymbol{a} = \\{0\\}$ 只有角度 $0$ 与 $\\pi$，所以 $x_0 = 0$ 不在集合中。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:858
msgid "*Exactness of an end.* The exact ends are $0$ and the infinities. Every other end is $b_\\text{end} \\tan(c_\\text{end})$ (Rev1) or $a_\\text{end} / \\tan(c_\\text{end})$ (Rev2) with a nonzero float operand end and a nonzero float angle, which is irrational: $\\tan$ of a nonzero algebraic number is transcendental (Lindemann-Weierstrass) and a nonzero rational times a transcendental number is transcendental, so the end differs from every float, comparisons with a prior end are strict, and the loop of `pow_rev1` (the working precision doubles up to the cap of 12; an undecided comparison counts as met and the prior's own end is written) terminates. No integer test and no budget are involved. The first working precision is $p + 96$: the forward `tan` of a point has a relative error of about $2^{-w}$ also next to $\\pi/2$, $0$ and $\\pi$ (the argument reduction runs at the working precision), and the loop needs the value to a relative $2^{-(p+2)}$. An angle one float from $\\pi$ gives a cotangent of order $2^{p}$ (the tests check the result is two adjacent floats that contain the 200-bit reference)."
msgstr "*端点的精确性。* 精确的端点是 $0$ 和无穷。其余端点是 $b_\\text{end} \\tan(c_\\text{end})$（Rev1）或 $a_\\text{end} / \\tan(c_\\text{end})$（Rev2），其中操作数端点与角度都是非零浮点数，它们是无理数：非零代数数的正切是超越数（Lindemann-Weierstrass），非零有理数乘以超越数仍是超越数，所以端点与每个浮点数都不同，与先验端点的比较是严格的，`pow_rev1` 的循环（工作精度加倍，至多 12 次；未决的比较算作满足，写入先验区间自己的端点）会终止。这里没有整数检验，也没有预算。首个工作精度是 $p + 96$：点的前向 `tan` 即使紧挨着 $\\pi/2$、$0$ 与 $\\pi$，相对误差也约为 $2^{-w}$（自变量归约在工作精度下进行），而循环需要值的相对精度达到 $2^{-(p+2)}$。离 $\\pi$ 一个浮点数的角度给出量级为 $2^{p}$ 的余切（测试检查结果是包含 200 位参考值的两个相邻浮点数）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:869
msgid "*Evidence.* The ITF1788 corpus has no `atan2Rev` case, so the evidence is ours. `tools/itl_atan2_reverse_oracle.py` (pure Python, 260 digits, no `ball_float` code) derives the exact hull by polar rectangles (an angle interval times an operand part of one sign, with corner limits) and validates every expected hull by the forward definition of the operation, which shares nothing with the case analysis. For a fixed ordinate $y$, $\\operatorname{atan2}(y, b_0)$ is monotone and continuous in $b_0$ on each side of 0 (decreasing for $y > 0$, increasing for $y < 0$; for $y = 0$ it is 0 for $b_0 > 0$ and $\\pi$ for $b_0 < 0$), so its image over $\\boldsymbol{b}$ is an interval decided from the ends of $\\boldsymbol{b}$, and $y$ is a member iff the image meets $\\boldsymbol{c}$ (Rev2 likewise, with the ordinate part split at 0). The validation tests an attained end, three points a geometric step inside each piece end ($10^{-9}$, $10^{-15}$, $10^{-30}$ relative) and six points beyond each end of the hull, inside the prior ($10^{-30}$, $10^{-15}$, $10^{-9}$, $10^{-3}$, 1 and 100 relative). The generated file `testdata/interval/generated/atan2_rev.itl` (see its README) has 16,260 cases, run as the `atan2-reverse` phase, counted apart from the ITF1788 total. The reference test (`atan2_reverse_reference_wbtest.mbt`) evaluates membership of a float with the forward `BallFloat::atan2` of points at 200 bits (the same monotone image, with the cut treated explicitly) and checks, at precisions 24, 53 and 113, that every float certainly in the set is in the result, that a point a quarter of a float outside an end that comes from a piece is not in the set, and that the float one step inside is not certainly outside while the next one is certainly inside. The maximum working precision on the generated corpus is 149 bits (the first working precision, $p + 96$ at $p = 53$; none of the 6,813 evaluations of the loop doubled it) bits."
msgstr "*证据。* ITF1788 语料没有任何 `atan2Rev` 用例，所以证据是我们自己的。`tools/itl_atan2_reverse_oracle.py`（纯 Python，260 位，不含 `ball_float` 代码）用极坐标矩形推导精确的区间包（角度区间乘以一个符号确定的操作数部分，取角点极限），并用该运算的前向定义验证每一个期望的区间包，前向定义与情形分析没有任何共同之处。对固定的纵坐标 $y$，$\\operatorname{atan2}(y, b_0)$ 在 0 的每一侧对 $b_0$ 单调且连续（$y > 0$ 时递减，$y < 0$ 时递增；$y = 0$ 时 $b_0 > 0$ 为 0，$b_0 < 0$ 为 $\\pi$），所以它在 $\\boldsymbol{b}$ 上的像是由 $\\boldsymbol{b}$ 的端点决定的区间，$y$ 是成员当且仅当该像与 $\\boldsymbol{c}$ 相交（Rev2 同理，纵坐标部分在 0 处拆开）。验证检查一个取得到的端点、每个片段端点内侧一个几何步长的三个点（相对 $10^{-9}$、$10^{-15}$、$10^{-30}$），以及区间包每个端点之外、先验区间之内的六个点（相对 $10^{-30}$、$10^{-15}$、$10^{-9}$、$10^{-3}$、1 与 100）。生成的文件 `testdata/interval/generated/atan2_rev.itl`（见其 README）有 16,260 个用例，作为 `atan2-reverse` 阶段运行，与 ITF1788 总数分开计数。参考测试（`atan2_reverse_reference_wbtest.mbt`）用 200 位的点上的前向 `BallFloat::atan2` 判定浮点数的成员资格（同一个单调的像，切割单独处理），并在精度 24、53 与 113 下检查：每个确定属于该集合的浮点数都在结果中，片段所产生端点之外四分之一个浮点数处的点不在该集合中，向内一步的浮点数并非确定在外，而下一个则确定在内。生成语料上的最大工作精度是 149 位（首个工作精度，$p = 53$ 时为 $p + 96$；循环的 6,813 次求值没有一次把它加倍）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:887
msgid "Interval literals and text input"
msgstr "区间字面量与文本输入"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:889
msgid "`from_string` (IEEE 1788-2015 `textToInterval`, 9.7, 12.11, 12.12.7, 13.2; see the [API page](../api/ball_float.md#ballfloatfrom_string-and-ballfloatdecoratedfrom_string)) is a hand-written parser of the portable grammar (Tables 9.5 and 12.2) over the characters of the string. A number literal is read into one of four exact descriptions: an infinity, a decimal $d \\cdot 10^{e}$ (the digits without the point and the exponent minus the number of digits after the point), a hexadecimal $h \\cdot 2^{e}$ (the exponent minus four times the number of hexadecimal digits after the point), or a rational $p/q$ with $q$ positive. An exponent field is saturated at $10^{15}$ in magnitude (beyond every range). The uncertain form $m?rve$ is turned into two decimal descriptions by the definition of 9.7.3: $\\operatorname{ulp}(m) = 10^{-k}$ with $k$ the number of digits after the point of $m$, the bounds are $(M \\mp r) 10^{e-k}$ with $M$ the integer of the digits (one ulp being $10^{-k}$; for the empty radius, half an ulp, as $(10M \\mp 5) 10^{e-k-1}$), the direction $u$ or $d$ keeps one side, and the radius $?$ is unbounded; the arithmetic is on big integers, so no rounding precedes the final one."
msgstr "`from_string`（IEEE 1788-2015 `textToInterval`，9.7、12.11、12.12.7、13.2；见 [API 页面](../api/ball_float.md#ballfloatfrom_string-and-ballfloatdecoratedfrom_string)）是对字符串的字符逐个处理的、手写的可移植文法（表 9.5 与 12.2）解析器。数字面量被读成四种精确描述之一：无穷、十进制 $d \\cdot 10^{e}$（去掉小数点的数字，指数减去小数点后的位数）、十六进制 $h \\cdot 2^{e}$（指数减去小数点后十六进制位数的四倍）、或分母为正的有理数 $p/q$。指数字段在量级 $10^{15}$ 处饱和（已超出任何范围）。不确定形式 $m?rve$ 按 9.7.3 的定义变成两个十进制描述：$\\operatorname{ulp}(m) = 10^{-k}$，$k$ 是 $m$ 小数点后的位数，端点是 $(M \\mp r) 10^{e-k}$，$M$ 是这些数字的整数（空半径为半个 ulp，即 $(10M \\mp 5) 10^{e-k-1}$），方向 $u$ 或 $d$ 只保留一侧，半径 $?$ 表示无界；运算在大整数上进行，所以最后一次舍入之前没有任何舍入。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:900
msgid "*Rounding.* Each bound is rounded once, outward and exactly: a decimal and a hexadecimal description go through the correctly rounded directed conversions of `BinFloat` (`from_string_ctx`, `from_hex_ctx`, which accept any exponent), and a rational is divided by integer division to a quotient of at least $p + 3$ bits with the sticky remainder (the same rule as the exact rational ends of `pow_rev1`). A literal whose exact value is beyond the stored range is therefore decided by those conversions from the exponent without forming the value, and `1e400000000` has the lower end the largest finite float and the upper end $+\\infty$. Both converters accept an exponent field of any length (`from_hex_ctx` saturates it at $2^{60}$ like `from_string_ctx`; before issue 597 it rejected an exponent beyond $10^{12}$ and the parser clamped it). The invariants are checked: a failure of a converter or of the digit parser aborts instead of returning a bound."
msgstr "*丸め。* 各端点只舍入一次，向外且精确：十进制与十六进制描述通过 `BinFloat` 的正确舍入的定向转换（`from_string_ctx`、`from_hex_ctx`，它们接受任意指数），有理数则用整数除法得到至少 $p + 3$ 位的商并保留粘滞余数（与 `pow_rev1` 的精确有理端点规则相同）。因此超出存储范围的字面量由这些转换根据指数判定而无需构造其值，`1e400000000` 的下端点是最大有限浮点数，上端点是 $+\\infty$。两个转换函数都接受任意长度的指数字段（`from_hex_ctx` 像 `from_string_ctx` 那样把它饱和在 $2^{60}$；在 issue 597 之前它拒绝超过 $10^{12}$ 的指数，解析器曾把指数截断）。 这些不变式是被检查的：转换函数或数字解析器失败时中止，而不是返回一个端点。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:907
msgid "*The order $l \\le u$.* It is decided from the exact values, so rounding never makes a nonempty literal Empty and an empty one nonempty: two decimal bounds are compared by the adjusted exponent and then the digit strings (trailing zeros removed, the shorter padded with zeros), which needs no power of ten whatever the exponent; any other pair is first separated by roundings at 64 bits and otherwise compared by cross-multiplication of the exact numerators and denominators, a power being formed only for an exponent of magnitude at most 65,536. A pair that is neither separated nor within that limit (two bounds of different radices that agree to 64 bits and have an exponent beyond 65,536) is undecided: 12.12.7 case (b) allows it and requires the result to contain both bounds, so the result is the hull of the four roundings (a false positive, which the standard permits; a false negative is not possible)."
msgstr "*顺序 $l \\le u$。* 它由精确值判定，所以舍入不会把非空字面量变成 Empty，也不会把空字面量变非空：两个十进制端点先比较调整后的指数，再比较数字串（去掉尾部的零，较短的补零），无论指数多大都不需要十的幂；其他的对先用 64 位的舍入分开，否则用精确分子分母的交叉相乘比较，只有指数的量级不超过 65,536 时才构造幂。既不能被分开、又超出该限制的对（两个基数不同、在 64 位内相同且指数超过 65,536 的端点）是未决的：12.12.7 情形 (b) 允许这种情况并要求结果包含两个端点，所以结果是四个舍入值的区间包（这是标准允许的假阳性；假阴性不可能出现）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:916
msgid "*Rejections.* Every failed call is an `Err` of the parse kind whose message names the rule of the grammar or of 12.11 that was broken (a missing digit, the exponent field of a hexadecimal literal, the denominator of a rational, the order of the bounds, an infinite bound on the wrong side, the characters after the literal, the decoration literal, a decoration not permitted for the value by 11.4, a decoration on a bare literal). The test table asserts the reason of every rejected string. A literal longer than `interval_literal_max_length` is not parsed and gives Entire (12.11.5)."
msgstr "*拒绝。* 每个失败的调用都是解析类的 `Err`，其消息指明被违反的文法或 12.11 的规则（缺少数字、十六进制字面量的指数字段、有理数的分母、端点的顺序、错误一侧的无穷端点、字面量之后的字符、装饰字面量、11.4 不允许该值使用的装饰、裸字面量上的装饰）。测试表对每个被拒绝的字符串都断言其原因。长于 `interval_literal_max_length` 的字面量不被解析，结果为 Entire（12.11.5）。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:922
msgid "*Evidence.* The independent oracle `tools/interval_literal_oracle.py` (pure Python, no `ball_float` code) evaluates a literal from whole-string patterns (a special form, the two bound strings of an inf-sup form cut at the comma, the groups of an uncertain pattern) to an exact `Fraction`, derives the uncertain form from the definition of the ulp, and rounds each bound with integer arithmetic against the stored range (gradual underflow to the quantum $2^{e_{\\min}-p+1}$, the largest finite float $(2^p - 1) 2^{e_{\\max}-p+1}$); it also checks every one of 20,000 rational literals against the rounded ends by cross-multiplication (the rounded lower end is not above the value and the float below it is below, and likewise for the upper end). The generated table (9,919 literals: the vectors of Tables 9.4 and 12.1, the negative examples, and random decimal, hexadecimal, rational, uncertain, decorated and special literals at precisions 24, 53 and 113, bare and decorated) is compared with the parser in `interval_literal_wbtest.mbt`."
msgstr "*证据。* 独立预言机 `tools/interval_literal_oracle.py`（纯 Python，不含 `ball_float` 代码）用整串模式（特殊形式、inf-sup 形式中在逗号处切开的两个端点串、不确定形式模式的各个分组）把字面量求值为精确的 `Fraction`，由 ulp 的定义推导不确定形式，并用整数运算按存储范围舍入每个端点（逐渐下溢到量子 $2^{e_{\\min}-p+1}$，最大有限浮点数 $(2^p - 1) 2^{e_{\\max}-p+1}$）；它还对 20,000 个有理数字面量逐一用交叉相乘检查舍入后的端点（舍入后的下端点不高于该值且其下的浮点数低于它，上端点同理）。生成的表（9,919 个字面量：表 9.4 与 12.1 的向量、反例，以及精度 24、53、113 下随机的十进制、十六进制、有理数、不确定、带装饰和特殊字面量，裸版与装饰版）在 `interval_literal_wbtest.mbt` 中与解析器比较。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:930
msgid "Relations: certainly and possibly"
msgstr "关系：必然与可能"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:932
msgid "An interval stands for an unknown point, so a comparison of two intervals asks a quantified question. Two quantifiers give the useful relations:"
msgstr "区间代表一个未知的点，因此两个区间的比较是一个带量词的问题。两种量词给出有用的关系："

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:946
msgid "For the first line, \"$\\Leftarrow$\" is $\\xi \\le \\overline{x} < \\underline{y} \\le \\eta$. For \"$\\Rightarrow$\": if $\\overline{x}$ and $\\underline{y}$ are finite they are elements, so $\\overline{x} < \\underline{y}$; if $\\overline{x} = +\\infty$ or $\\underline{y} = -\\infty$, a large $\\xi$ or a small $\\eta$ violates $\\xi < \\eta$, and the endpoint test is false as well. The second line is the nonempty intersection of two intervals. \"Possibly less\" is the negation of \"certainly not less\", so the two families are dual: `DefinitelyLt::definitely_lt(x, y)` is false exactly when some pair satisfies $\\xi \\ge \\eta$. With empty operands the universal statements would be vacuously true, which would let a caller prove anything from an empty enclosure; the `DefinitelyLt` and `DefinitelyLe` relations (and `Overlaps`, `MaybeEq`) therefore return false for empty operands, whereas the IEEE 1788 relation `precedes` ($\\forall\\xi\\,\\forall\\eta: \\xi \\le \\eta$) is defined to be vacuously true."
msgstr "对于第一行，\"$\\Leftarrow$\" 即 $\\xi \\le \\overline{x} < \\underline{y} \\le \\eta$。对于 \"$\\Rightarrow$\"：若 $\\overline{x}$ 和 $\\underline{y}$ 有限，则它们是元素，因此 $\\overline{x} < \\underline{y}$；若 $\\overline{x} = +\\infty$ 或 $\\underline{y} = -\\infty$，则足够大的 $\\xi$ 或足够小的 $\\eta$ 会违反 $\\xi < \\eta$，而端点测试同样为假。第二行是两个区间的非空交集。\"可能小于\" 是 \"必然不小于\" 的否定，因此这两族关系是对偶的：`DefinitelyLt::definitely_lt(x, y)` 为假当且仅当存在某对值满足 $\\xi \\ge \\eta$。对于空操作数，全称命题会空真成立，这将使调用者能从空包络证明任何结论；因此 `DefinitelyLt` 和 `DefinitelyLe` 关系（以及 `Overlaps`、`MaybeEq`）对空操作数返回 false，而 IEEE 1788 的关系 `precedes`（$\\forall\\xi\\,\\forall\\eta: \\xi \\le \\eta$）则被定义为空真。"

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:959
msgid "The set relations (`subset`, `interior`, `disjoint`, `==`) and the IEEE 1788 orders (`less`: $\\forall\\xi\\,\\exists\\eta\\, \\xi \\le \\eta$ and $\\forall\\eta\\,\\exists\\xi\\, \\xi \\le \\eta$, which reduces to comparing both endpoint pairs) are evaluated by endpoint comparisons in the same way. None of these relations is a total order, and the trait method `@lf_arith.Contains::contains(x, y)` is set inclusion $\\boldsymbol{y} \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{x}$, matching the enclosure reading of the [`arithmetic`](https://lunaflow.cn/en/arithmetic/) traits."
msgstr "集合关系（`subset`、`interior`、`disjoint`、`==`）和 IEEE 1788 序（`less`：$\\forall\\xi\\,\\exists\\eta\\, \\xi \\le \\eta$ 与 $\\forall\\eta\\,\\exists\\xi\\, \\xi \\le \\eta$，归结为比较两对端点）同样通过端点比较求值。这些关系都不是全序，trait 方法 `@lf_arith.Contains::contains(x, y)` 是集合包含 $\\boldsymbol{y} \\subseteq \\boldsymbol{x}$，与 [`arithmetic`](https://lunaflow.cn/en/arithmetic/) trait 的包络解读一致。"

