msgid "the Ziv driver: `bounds_at(work)` returns a certified enclosure of an inexact result"
msgstr "Ziv 驱动器：`bounds_at(work)` 返回不精确结果的认证包络"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:520
msgid "an exact value, both tininess rules, overflow, subnormals"
msgstr "精确值，两种 tininess 规则、上溢、次正规数"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:521
msgid "the $p$-bit rounding with no range (for after-rounding tininess)"
msgstr "不带范围的 $p$ 位舍入（用于舍入后 tininess）"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:522
msgid "a result within $2^{scale}$ of a representable anchor, above or below it, decided by direction"
msgstr "与可表示锚点相距 $2^{scale}$ 以内的结果，在其上方或下方，由方向决定"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:523
msgid "a nonzero result below a quarter of the smallest subnormal"
msgstr "低于最小次正规数四分之一的非零结果"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:525
msgid "To add a function: (1) write the special-value table of §9.2.1 and Table 9.1 from the PDF text and quote it in the file header and the tests; (2) check a NaN first (`binary_nan_unary`), a signaling NaN before any shortcut; (3) list the exact results (by Niven-type arguments or direct algebra) and return them through `binary_round_dyadic`; (4) find the anchors and the ranges that cluster (a tiny or huge argument, an extreme ratio) and decide them with `binary_tiny_argument_result` with a proved bound on the distance; (5) write the enclosure for `binary_ziv_round`, with the working precision at least the operand precision plus 16 and the operation known to be inexact; (6) add the `try_*_ctx`, `*_ctx` and plain forms, the `BinFloatResult` wrappers and the `mpfr_expr` operation; (7) test against a model that does not use the code under test (an exact rational, an anchor table, the result at precision $p + 150$), at the subnormal limit of the implementation and of a few bounded formats, in every rounding direction and both tininess modes; (8) add the MPFR operation to `tools/generate_mpfr_random_oracle.c` as a new family appended after the existing operations (the rows of older families stay byte for byte), generate range boundary rows in `tools/range_boundary_rows.py`, run 1,000,000 native and 100,000 cases on each other backend and the boundary sweep, and add a few boundary rows to `testdata/bin_float/random-regressions.txt`; (9) document the function, its evidence and, for a defect of the oracle, the finding."
msgstr "添加函数的步骤：(1) 从 PDF 文本写出 §9.2.1 与表 9.1 的特殊值表，并在文件头和测试中引用；(2) 先检查 NaN（`binary_nan_unary`），信号 NaN 先于任何捷径；(3) 列出精确结果（通过 Niven 型论证或直接代数），经 `binary_round_dyadic` 返回；(4) 找出聚集的锚点和范围（微小或巨大的参数、极端比值），用 `binary_tiny_argument_result` 并给出距离的已证明界来判定；(5) 为 `binary_ziv_round` 写包络，工作精度至少为操作数精度加 16，且该运算已知是不精确的；(6) 添加 `try_*_ctx`、`*_ctx` 和普通形式、`BinFloatResult` 包装以及 `mpfr_expr` 运算；(7) 对照不使用被测代码的模型（精确有理数、锚点表、p + 150 位结果）测试，覆盖实现的次正规数极限和若干有界格式，所有舍入方向和两种 tininess 模式；(8) 把 MPFR 运算作为附加在现有运算之后的新族加入 `tools/generate_mpfr_random_oracle.c`（旧族的行逐字节不变），在 `tools/range_boundary_rows.py` 中生成范围边界行，运行原生 1,000,000 个、其他每个后端 100,000 个用例和边界扫描，并在 `testdata/bin_float/random-regressions.txt` 中加入少量边界行；(9) 记录该函数、其证据，以及预言缺陷时的发现。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:546
msgid "The oracle is not the specification. Findings about MPFR 4.2.2 (Homebrew bottle, arm64) made while doing this, each documented in `testdata/bin_float/README.md`: `mpfr_sqrt` returns a wrong ternary value or a result on the wrong side for some odd-exponent operands near the output precision (the generator checks every `sqrt` row with an exact product and draws again); `mpfr_compound_si` is not correctly rounded for a negative $n$ in the directed modes nor near the ends of the exponent range (the generator rounds the exact rational with `mpfr_set_q`; the library was right in every one of 2,017 rows proved by independent rational arithmetic); `mpfr_rec_sqrt(-0)` is $+\\infty$ by MPFR's own convention where §9.2.1 says $-\\infty$ (the expected value follows the standard); `mpfr_atan2pi` takes time that grows with the exponent difference of its operands (not a wrong answer: rows over 100,000 binades apart are not generated)."
msgstr "预言不是规范。以下是处理这些工作时对 MPFR 4.2.2（Homebrew 软件包，arm64）的发现，均记录在 `testdata/bin_float/README.md`：对某些奇数指数且精度接近输出精度的操作数，`mpfr_sqrt` 返回错误的三值或位于错误一侧的结果（生成器用精确乘积检查每个 `sqrt` 行并重新抽取）；`mpfr_compound_si` 在 $n$ 为负的定向舍入以及指数范围两端附近不是正确舍入（生成器用 `mpfr_set_q` 舍入精确有理数；库在经独立有理数运算证明的 2,017 行中全部正确）；`mpfr_rec_sqrt(-0)` 按 MPFR 自己的约定为 $+\\infty$，而 §9.2.1 要求 $-\\infty$（期望值遵循标准）；`mpfr_atan2pi` 的耗时随操作数的指数差增长（并非答案错误：相差超过 100,000 个二进制数量级的行不会生成）。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:560
msgid "Signed zeros and NaNs"
msgstr "带符号零与 NaN"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:562
msgid "An exact zero sum $a + b = 0$ with $a, b$ of opposite sign is $+0$ in every direction except RD, where it is $-0$; $(-0) + (-0) = -0$ (clause 6.3). Products and quotients take the exclusive-or of the signs. A NaN operand yields the first NaN operand, quieted, with its sign and payload (clause 6.2.3 allows any input NaN), and `invalid_operation` is raised exactly when an operand is a signaling NaN or the operation is invalid on its own ($\\infty - \\infty$, $0 \\cdot \\infty$, $0/0$, $\\infty/\\infty$, $\\sqrt{x<0}$, $\\operatorname{remainder}(\\infty, y)$, $\\operatorname{remainder}(x, 0)$). Flags are values: `combine` is the bitwise OR, so the flags of a computation form a commutative idempotent monoid and can be accumulated in any order, which a global sticky register cannot offer to concurrent code."
msgstr "$a, b$ 符号相反时的精确零和 $a + b = 0$ 在除 RD 以外的所有方向下均为 $+0$，在 RD 下为 $-0$；$(-0) + (-0) = -0$（第 6.3 条）。积与商取两符号的异或。NaN 操作数产生第一个 NaN 操作数经静默化后的结果，保留其符号和载荷（第 6.2.3 条允许任一输入 NaN），并且当且仅当某个操作数是信号 NaN 或该运算本身无效（$\\infty - \\infty$、$0 \\cdot \\infty$、$0/0$、$\\infty/\\infty$、$\\sqrt{x<0}$、$\\operatorname{remainder}(\\infty, y)$、$\\operatorname{remainder}(x, 0)$）时引发 `invalid_operation`。标志是值：`combine` 是按位或，因此一次计算的标志构成一个交换幂等幺半群，可以按任意顺序累积，而全局粘滞寄存器无法为并发代码提供这一点。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:575
msgid "The elementary functions take the signs of their special values from IEEE 754-2019 §9.2.1, which reads the sign of a zero operand: for example $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, -0) = \\pm\\pi$ but $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, +0) = \\pm 0$, $\\operatorname{tanpi}(n)$ has the sign of $\\operatorname{sinpi}(n)/\\operatorname{cospi}(n)$, and $(-0)^y$ and $(-\\infty)^y$ are negative exactly for an odd integral $y$."
msgstr "初等函数的特殊值符号取自 IEEE 754-2019 §9.2.1，该条款会读取零操作数的符号：例如 $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, -0) = \\pm\\pi$，但 $\\operatorname{atan2}(\\pm 0, +0) = \\pm 0$；$\\operatorname{tanpi}(n)$ 的符号与 $\\operatorname{sinpi}(n)/\\operatorname{cospi}(n)$ 相同；$(-0)^y$ 与 $(-\\infty)^y$ 恰在 $y$ 为奇整数时为负。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:582
msgid "Classes of a value"
msgstr "值的类别"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:584
msgid "IEEE 754-2019 clause 5.7.2 defines `class(x)` with ten values, which the `def` package spells as `IeeeClass`. Zeros, infinities and NaNs are read from the stored class and sign (a signaling NaN is the flag the value keeps). The normal/subnormal split is the one rule of clause 3.4: a nonzero finite $x$ is normal when $2^{e_{\\min}} \\le |x|$, that is when the exponent of its leading bit is at least $e_{\\min}$, and subnormal otherwise. A `BinFloat` stores no $e_{\\min}$ (it has only a precision), so `class_of`, `is_normal` and `is_subnormal` take the `BinaryContext`, the same way `Decimal` takes a `DecimalContext`. The leading-bit exponent is computed from the coefficient's bit length and the exponent, so the test is exact and independent of the precision; no rounding happens and no flag is raised. `is_finite`, `is_infinite` and `is_nan` need no context. `class_of` is a total function: the ten classes partition every `BinFloat`, and `Decimal::class_name` is the text of the same partition for `Decimal`."
msgstr "IEEE 754-2019 第 5.7.2 条定义了有十个值的 `class(x)`，`def` 包把它写作 `IeeeClass`。零、无穷和 NaN 由存储的类别和符号读出（signaling NaN 是值保存的那个标志）。正规与次正规的划分是第 3.4 条的那条规则：非零有限数 $x$ 在 $2^{e_{\\min}} \\le |x|$ 时是正规数，也就是最高位的指数不小于 $e_{\\min}$，否则是次正规数。`BinFloat` 不保存 $e_{\\min}$（它只有精度），所以 `class_of`、`is_normal` 和 `is_subnormal` 接受 `BinaryContext`，与 `Decimal` 接受 `DecimalContext` 的方式相同。最高位的指数由系数的位长和指数算出，所以这个判断是精确的，与精度无关；不发生舍入，也不产生标志。`is_finite`、`is_infinite` 和 `is_nan` 不需要上下文。`class_of` 是全函数：这十个类别划分了每一个 `BinFloat`，而 `Decimal::class_name` 是 `Decimal` 上同一划分的文本。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:599
msgid "Format conversion"
msgstr "格式转换"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:601
msgid "`convert_format` is `round_ctx` in the destination format's context, so the conversion inherits the one rounding step of the dyadic finalizer: a destination with at least the precision and range of the source is exact (the value needs at most $p_{\\text{source}} \\le p_{\\text{destination}}$ bits and its exponent is inside the wider range), and a narrower one rounds once, with the flags of clause 7. The only extra step is the payload of a NaN: `round_ctx` keeps the whole payload of a `BinFloat` only for a context of at least the same precision (a NaN of precision $p$ has $p - 2$ payload bits, so every operation and constructor that delivers a NaN at another precision truncates, 6.2.3), and a format holds $p - 2$ payload bits below the quiet bit, so the payload is masked to its low bits, which makes the result the value that decoding `to_interchange` returns and keeps the clause 6.2.3 round trip (narrower to wider to the same narrower format) exact. The independent oracle is Berkeley TestFloat: all twelve pairs among binary16, 32, 64 and 128 in the gate, five rounding directions and both tininess rules for the narrowing pairs; a widening pair does not round, so it is one task."
msgstr "`convert_format` 就是在目标格式的上下文里做 `round_ctx`，因此转换继承了二进制有理数终结器的唯一一次舍入：目标格式的精度和范围不小于源格式时转换是精确的（值至多需要 $p_{\\text{source}} \\le p_{\\text{destination}}$ 位，其指数落在更宽的范围内），更窄的格式则舍入一次，并按第 7 条给出标志。唯一额外的步骤是 NaN 的载荷：只有当上下文的精度不低于 NaN 自身的精度时，`round_ctx` 才保留 `BinFloat` 的全部载荷（精度为 $p$ 的 NaN 有 $p - 2$ 位载荷，所以每个在其他精度下交付 NaN 的运算和构造函数都会截断，6.2.3），而格式在 quiet 位之下只有 $p - 2$ 位载荷，所以载荷被屏蔽到低位，这使结果等于对 `to_interchange` 解码所得的值，并使第 6.2.3 条的往返（较窄格式到较宽格式再回到同一较窄格式）保持精确。独立的预言是 Berkeley TestFloat：门禁里 binary16、32、64 和 128 之间的全部十二个格式对，窄化的格式对覆盖五种舍入方向和两种 tininess 规则；扩宽的格式对不舍入，所以只有一个任务。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:618
msgid "Far-apart operands in addition"
msgstr "加法中相距很远的操作数"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:620
msgid "**Problem.** $2^{10^9} + 2^{-10^9}$ is exact as a dyadic number, but forming it needs a two-billion-bit coefficient."
msgstr "**问题。** $2^{10^9} + 2^{-10^9}$ 作为二进有理数是精确的，但构造它需要一个二十亿位的系数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:623
msgid "**Choice.** When the leading exponents differ by more than $p + 3$, the sum is formed on the grid with unit $\\upsilon = 2^{e(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$, where $e(\\text{high})$ is the exponent of the last bit of the larger operand, so $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$. The larger operand $H\\upsilon$ is exact on that grid; of the smaller operand only the integer part $L$ of its value in units $\\upsilon$ enters, and if anything below $\\upsilon$ was discarded the magnitude becomes $2(H \\pm L) + 1$ (for subtraction $2(H - L - 1) + 1$) in units of $\\upsilon/2$, that is, one sticky bit at the half unit."
msgstr "**选择。** 当两个操作数的首位指数相差超过 $p + 3$ 时，和在单位为 $\\upsilon = 2^{e(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$ 的网格上构成，其中 $e(\\text{high})$ 是较大操作数最低位的指数，因此 $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$。较大操作数 $H\\upsilon$ 在该网格上是精确的；较小操作数只有其值以 $\\upsilon$ 为单位的整数部分 $L$ 参与运算，若有任何低于 $\\upsilon$ 的部分被丢弃，则以 $\\upsilon/2$ 为单位，幅值变为 $2(H \\pm L) + 1$（减法时为 $2(H - L - 1) + 1$），即在半个单位处放置一个粘滞位。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:633
msgid "**Why it is exact for rounding.** The result has $\\operatorname{top} \\ge \\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - 1$, because the smaller operand is below $2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 2}$. The last retained bit of the rounded result therefore has position at least $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p$ (more on the subnormal grid), and its round bit at least $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 1$. The true sum and the substitute both lie strictly inside the same open interval $\\bigl((H \\pm L)\\upsilon, (H \\pm L + 1)\\upsilon\\bigr)$ (or are equal when nothing was discarded), and that interval lies between two consecutive multiples of $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$, at least two bit positions below the round bit. So $q$ and $g$ agree, and $t$ is set in both cases exactly when something nonzero was discarded. The argument does not need the larger operand to have at most $p$ bits. For subtraction, $H - (L + \\varepsilon) = (H - L - 1) + (1 - \\varepsilon)$ with $0 < 1 - \\varepsilon < 1$, so the same substitution applies to the borrowed form. The complete argument, including the subnormal shift, is in the attachment below."
msgstr "**为何对舍入而言是精确的。** 结果满足 $\\operatorname{top} \\ge \\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - 1$，因为较小操作数低于 $2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 2}$。因此舍入结果保留的最低位的位置至少为 $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p$（在次正规网格上更高），其舍入位至少为 $\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 1$。真实的和与替代值都严格位于同一个开区间 $\\bigl((H \\pm L)\\upsilon, (H \\pm L + 1)\\upsilon\\bigr)$ 之内（若没有丢弃任何内容则二者相等），而该区间位于 $\\upsilon \\le 2^{\\operatorname{top}(\\text{high}) - p - 3}$ 的两个相邻倍数之间，比舍入位至少低两个位位置。因此 $q$ 和 $g$ 一致，且在两种情况下 $t$ 都恰在丢弃了非零内容时被置位。该论证不要求较大操作数至多有 $p$ 位。对于减法，$H - (L + \\varepsilon) = (H - L - 1) + (1 - \\varepsilon)$ 且 $0 < 1 - \\varepsilon < 1$，因此同样的替换也适用于借位形式。包括次正规移位在内的完整论证见下方附件。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:651
msgid "One aligned pass for the sum of wide operands"
msgstr "宽操作数之和的一次对齐遍历"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:653
msgid "**Problem.** The plain `add` of two coefficients wider than one word aligned each operand with a shift into a new array, added or compared and subtracted into a third, and then rounded: about ten passes over arrays of the size of the sum and six allocations, although the result needs $p$ bits."
msgstr "**问题。** 两个宽于一个字的系数的普通 `add`，原先把每个操作数移位到新数组，再相加，或先比较再相减到第三个数组，最后舍入：约十次遍历、六次分配，都是和的大小的数组，而结果只需要 $p$ 位。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:655
msgid "**Choice.** Let $X$ be the operand with the larger top bit $t$ and $Y$ the other, $e_X, e_Y$ the exponents of their lowest bits, and $K = p + 3$. The sum is formed in a window of $n = \\lfloor (t - L) / 64 \\rfloor + 1$ limbs whose bit 0 has weight $2^{L}$, with"
msgstr "**选择。** 设 $X$ 为最高位 $t$ 较大的操作数，$Y$ 为另一个，$e_X, e_Y$ 为它们最低位的指数，$K = p + 3$。和在一个 $n = \\lfloor (t - L) / 64 \\rfloor + 1$ 个肢的窗口中形成，窗口第 0 位的权重为 $2^{L}$，其中"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:661
msgid "So $n \\le \\lfloor (p + 3) / 64 \\rfloor + 1$, whatever the exponent gap. One loop over the limbs reads both operands through their shifts (the word and bit shift are computed once) and writes $X \\pm Y$ once. $X$ is never cut ($e_X \\ge t - p > t - K$). When $Y$ reaches below the window, its dropped part is non-zero, because stored coefficients are odd (bit 0 of $Y$ is dropped), and that is the sticky flag; when $Y$ lies entirely below, none of its limbs is read. For a subtraction with a cut operand the loop starts with a borrow of one: $|X| - |Y| = (X - Y_t - 1) + (1 - f)$ with $Y_t$ the integer part and $0 < f < 1$, as in the previous section. The window then holds the exact result, or a truncated one with the sticky flag, which the finisher of the previous section rounds in place."
msgstr "所以不论指数差多大，$n \\le \\lfloor (p + 3) / 64 \\rfloor + 1$。一次对肢的循环通过各自的移位读取两个操作数（字移位和位移位只算一次），并把 $X \\pm Y$ 只写一次。$X$ 从不被截断（$e_X \\ge t - p > t - K$）。当 $Y$ 伸到窗口以下时，被丢弃的部分非零，因为存储的系数是奇数（$Y$ 的第 0 位被丢弃），这就是粘滞标志；当 $Y$ 完全位于窗口以下时，它的肢一个也不读。对于带截断操作数的减法，循环以借位 1 开始：$|X| - |Y| = (X - Y_t - 1) + (1 - f)$，其中 $Y_t$ 为整数部分，$0 < f < 1$，与上一节相同。窗口中于是保存精确结果，或带粘滞标志的截断结果，由上一节的收尾函数原地舍入。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:663
msgid "**Why the window is enough.** If $Y$ is cut, then $e_Y < t - K$, so its top is below $t - K + p = t - 3$ and the gap between the tops is at least $4$. Then for an addition $W \\ge 2^{K-1}$ has at least $p + 3$ bits, and for a subtraction $|X| - |Y| > 2^{t-1} - 2^{t-4} \\ge 2^{t-2}$, so $W = X - Y_t - 1$ has at least $K - 1 = p + 2$ bits. By the argument of the finisher (the discarded part is $d + \\varepsilon$ with integer $d$ and $0 < \\varepsilon < 1$), $p + 1$ bits and the sticky flag decide every rounding direction. If $Y$ is not cut the result is exact. When the tops differ by at most one, the exact difference fits the window ($\\min(e_X, e_Y) \\ge t - 1 - p$), and any number of leading limbs may cancel: the finisher scans down to the top limb. For equal tops the difference is formed as $\\text{left} - \\text{right}$ and negated in place when the final borrow is set, so no comparison pass is needed; an all-zero window is the exact zero, which the general path signs."
msgstr "**为什么窗口足够。** 若 $Y$ 被截断，则 $e_Y < t - K$，它的最高位低于 $t - K + p = t - 3$，两个最高位相差至少 $4$。于是对加法，$W \\ge 2^{K-1}$ 至少有 $p + 3$ 位；对减法，$|X| - |Y| > 2^{t-1} - 2^{t-4} \\ge 2^{t-2}$，所以 $W = X - Y_t - 1$ 至少有 $K - 1 = p + 2$ 位。按收尾函数的论证（被舍弃部分为 $d + \\varepsilon$，$d$ 为整数，$0 < \\varepsilon < 1$），$p + 1$ 位加粘滞标志即可决定每一种舍入方向。若 $Y$ 未被截断，结果是精确的。当两个最高位相差不超过 1 时，精确的差落在窗口内（$\\min(e_X, e_Y) \\ge t - 1 - p$），任意多个高位肢都可能相消：收尾函数从上往下扫描找到最高的非零肢。最高位相等时，差按“左减右”形成，并在最终借位置位时原地取负，因此不需要比较遍历；全零窗口就是精确的零，由通用路径给出符号。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:665
msgid "**Boundary.** The operands must satisfy the same range test as the other coefficient paths; the former limit on the exponent gap is gone, because a far operand costs only the sticky flag. The tests keep the previous path and compare bit for bit with it and with `add_ctx` and `sub_ctx`, in the sizes, gaps, cancellations and ties listed in the pull request."
msgstr "**边界。** 操作数必须满足与其他系数路径相同的范围检验；原先对指数差的限制取消了，因为远处的操作数只花费一个粘滞标志。测试保留之前的路径，并与它以及 `add_ctx`、`sub_ctx` 逐位比较，覆盖拉取请求中列出的大小、指数差、相消和平局。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:667
msgid "Fused multiply-add"
msgstr "融合乘加"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:669
msgid "`fma_ctx` forms the product $c_x c_y 2^{e_x + e_y}$ exactly as a value whose precision equals its own bit length, and passes it to the addition finalizer, so $x y + z$ is rounded once (clause 5.4.1). The difference from two roundings is the point of the operation: for $a = \\operatorname{RN}(0.1)$ in binary64, the rounding error $a \\cdot a - \\operatorname{RN}(a \\cdot a)$ is lost by `mul_ctx` followed by `sub_ctx` (the second operation sees two equal numbers) but `fma_ctx(a, a, -RN(a*a))` returns it exactly, $-8.33\\ldots \\cdot 10^{-19}$. That the result is exact is Dekker's theorem: the error of a rounded-to-nearest product is itself in $F$ when no underflow occurs (precisely, when $e_a + e_b \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$ for the exponents of the last bits of $a$ and $b$, so the exact product lies on the grid of $F$).[^dekker] If the product exponent leaves the `Int` range, the product either certainly overflows, or it is so small that it acts as a sticky bit next to a nonzero addend; the code places a single bit $p + 9$ positions below the addend's last bit, which by the far-operand argument above rounds identically. With a zero addend such a product is the tiny result of the underflow rule."
msgstr "`fma_ctx` 将乘积 $c_x c_y 2^{e_x + e_y}$ 精确地构造为一个精度等于其自身位长的值，并将其交给加法终结器，因此 $x y + z$ 只舍入一次（第 5.4.1 条）。与两次舍入的区别正是该运算的意义所在：对于 binary64 中的 $a = \\operatorname{RN}(0.1)$，先 `mul_ctx` 再 `sub_ctx` 会丢失舍入误差 $a \\cdot a - \\operatorname{RN}(a \\cdot a)$（第二次运算看到的是两个相等的数），而 `fma_ctx(a, a, -RN(a*a))` 精确地返回它，$-8.33\\ldots \\cdot 10^{-19}$。结果是精确的，这就是 Dekker 定理：在不发生下溢时（确切地说，当 $a$ 和 $b$ 最低位的指数满足 $e_a + e_b \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$，从而精确乘积位于 $F$ 的网格上时），就近舍入乘积的误差本身属于 $F$。[^dekker] 若乘积指数超出 `Int` 范围，则乘积要么必然上溢，要么小到相对非零加数而言只相当于一个粘滞位；代码在加数最低位以下 $p + 9$ 个位置处放置一个单独的位，根据上文关于远距操作数的论证，其舍入结果相同。当加数为零时，这样的乘积就是下溢规则下的微小结果。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:687
msgid "T. J. Dekker, \"A floating-point technique for extending the available precision\", *Numerische Mathematik* 18, 1971; Muller et al., §4.4."
msgstr "T. J. Dekker，\"A floating-point technique for extending the available precision\"，*Numerische Mathematik* 18，1971；Muller 等，§4.4。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:691
msgid "IEEE remainder is exact"
msgstr "IEEE 余数是精确的"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:693
msgid ""
"**Claim.** If $x, y \\in F$ (same precision $p$, same range) and $y \\n"
"e 0$, then $r = x - n y$ with $n = \\operatorname{RNE}_{\\mathbb{Z}}(x/y)$ lies in $F$."
msgstr ""
"**断言。** 若 $x, y \\in F$（精度 $p$ 相同，范围相同）且 $y \\n"
"e 0$，则满足 $n = \\operatorname{RNE}_{\\mathbb{Z}}(x/y)$ 的 $r = x - n y$ 属于 $F$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:697
msgid "**Proof.** Write $x = M_x 2^{q_x}$, $y = M_y 2^{q_y}$ with $|M_x|, |M_y| < 2^p$ and $q_x, q_y \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$. By the choice of $n$, $|r| \\le |y|/2$. If $n = 0$ then $r = x$. Otherwise $|x/y| \\ge \\frac12$, so $|r| \\le |y|/2 \\le |x|$. Now $r$ is an integer multiple of $2^{\\min(q_x, q_y)}$."
msgstr "**证明。** 记 $x = M_x 2^{q_x}$、$y = M_y 2^{q_y}$，其中 $|M_x|, |M_y| < 2^p$ 且 $q_x, q_y \\ge e_{\\min} - p + 1$。由 $n$ 的选取，$|r| \\le |y|/2$。若 $n = 0$ 则 $r = x$。否则 $|x/y| \\ge \\frac12$，因此 $|r| \\le |y|/2 \\le |x|$。此时 $r$ 是 $2^{\\min(q_x, q_y)}$ 的整数倍。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:703
msgid "If $q_x \\ge q_y$: $r = k 2^{q_y}$ with $|k| 2^{q_y} \\le |M_y| 2^{q_y}/2$, so $|k| < 2^{p-1}$."
msgstr "若 $q_x \\ge q_y$：$r = k 2^{q_y}$，其中 $|k| 2^{q_y} \\le |M_y| 2^{q_y}/2$，因此 $|k| < 2^{p-1}$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:705
msgid "If $q_x < q_y$: $r = k 2^{q_x}$ with $|k| 2^{q_x} \\le |x| = |M_x| 2^{q_x}$, so $|k| < 2^{p}$."
msgstr "若 $q_x < q_y$：$r = k 2^{q_x}$，其中 $|k| 2^{q_x} \\le |x| = |M_x| 2^{q_x}$，因此 $|k| < 2^{p}$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:708
msgid "In both cases $|k| < 2^p$, the exponent is at least $e_{\\min} - p + 1$, and $|r| \\le \\max(|x|, |y|) \\le \\Omega$, so $r \\in F$. $\\square$"
msgstr "两种情形下均有 $|k| < 2^p$，指数至少为 $e_{\\min} - p + 1$，且 $|r| \\le \\max(|x|, |y|) \\le \\Omega$，因此 $r \\in F$。$\\square$"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:711
msgid "The implementation never forms $n$, which can have $2^{30}$ bits. With $X = |x| 2^{-m}$, $Y = |y| 2^{-m}$, $m = \\min(q_x, q_y)$ (integers), it computes $X \\bmod 2Y$ by modular exponentiation of $2^{q_x - q_y}$ when $q_x > q_y$. Writing $X = Q (2Y) + R$, $0 \\le R < 2Y$, gives $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor = 2Q + [R \\ge Y]$, so $R$ alone yields both $X \\bmod Y$ and the parity of $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor$, which is all the ties-to-even choice of $n$ needs. The exact $r$ then goes through the usual finalizer; by the claim, no rounding happens for operands of the context's format."
msgstr "实现从不构造 $n$，它可能有 $2^{30}$ 位。设 $X = |x| 2^{-m}$、$Y = |y| 2^{-m}$、$m = \\min(q_x, q_y)$（均为整数），当 $q_x > q_y$ 时它通过 $2^{q_x - q_y}$ 的模幂计算 $X \\bmod 2Y$。记 $X = Q (2Y) + R$、$0 \\le R < 2Y$，得到 $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor = 2Q + [R \\ge Y]$，因此仅凭 $R$ 即可同时得到 $X \\bmod Y$ 和 $\\lfloor X/Y \\rfloor$ 的奇偶性，而这正是 $n$ 的偶数优先选择所需的全部信息。精确的 $r$ 随后经由通常的终结器处理；由上述断言，对上下文格式的操作数不会发生舍入。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:721
msgid "Neighbours, scaling and integral values"
msgstr "邻值、缩放与整数值"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:723
msgid "`next_up_ctx(x)` adds a positive step $2^{\\pi - 2}$ to $x$ and rounds toward $+\\infty$, where $\\pi = \\min(e_{\\min} - p,\\ e(x),\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)$. Every gap between consecutive points of $F$ next to $x$ is at least $2^{\\min(e_{\\min} - p + 1,\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)}$ and $x$ itself is a multiple of $2^{e(x)}$, so $x < x + 2^{\\pi - 2} < x^{+}$ for $x \\in F$, and by the definition of RU the result is the least point of $F$ above $x$. The same argument works for an $x$ with more than $p$ bits, which is why such operands are accepted. The flags of this internal addition are discarded, because `nextUp` is quiet (clause 5.3.1) even when it steps from $\\Omega$ to $+\\infty$."
msgstr "`next_up_ctx(x)` 将正步长 $2^{\\pi - 2}$ 加到 $x$ 上并朝 $+\\infty$ 舍入，其中 $\\pi = \\min(e_{\\min} - p,\\ e(x),\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)$。$x$ 旁 $F$ 中相邻点之间的每个间隙都至少为 $2^{\\min(e_{\\min} - p + 1,\\ \\operatorname{top}(x) - p)}$，且 $x$ 本身是 $2^{e(x)}$ 的倍数，因此对 $x \\in F$ 有 $x < x + 2^{\\pi - 2} < x^{+}$，再由 RU 的定义，结果是 $F$ 中高于 $x$ 的最小点。同样的论证对多于 $p$ 位的 $x$ 也成立，这就是此类操作数被接受的原因。这次内部加法的标志被丢弃，因为 `nextUp` 是静默的（第 5.3.1 条），即使它从 $\\Omega$ 步进到 $+\\infty$ 亦然。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:734
msgid "`scaleb_ctx(x, n)` (with `n` an integer-valued `BinFloat`) is the finalizer applied to $(c, e + n)$: exact in the normal range, correctly rounded with underflow and overflow outside it. `logb_ctx` returns $\\operatorname{top}(x)$, which is exact and correct for subnormal $x$ because $\\operatorname{top}$ is computed on the integer coefficient. The integral roundings use the same round and sticky bits with $\\sigma = -e$ (the bits below the binary point); `to_int_ctx` and its siblings round first and then compare the integer with the target range, reporting `invalid_operation` instead of returning an implementation-defined sentinel."
msgstr "`scaleb_ctx(x, n)`（`n` 为整数值的 `BinFloat`）是对 $(c, e + n)$ 应用终结器：在正规范围内精确，在范围之外以下溢和上溢正确舍入。`logb_ctx` 返回 $\\operatorname{top}(x)$，它是精确的，并且对次正规的 $x$ 也正确，因为 $\\operatorname{top}$ 是在整数系数上计算的。取整舍入使用相同的舍入位和粘滞位，取 $\\sigma = -e$（即二进制小数点以下的位）；`to_int_ctx` 及其同类先舍入，再将整数与目标范围比较，报告 `invalid_operation` 而非返回由实现定义的哨兵值。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:744
msgid "Decimal conversion"
msgstr "十进制转换"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:746
msgid ""
"**Parsing.** `from_string_ctx` reads $D \\cdot 10^{k}$ exactly ($D$ an integer without trailing zeros). For $|k|$ up to $\\max\\bigl(400, \\lfloor (3n + p)/2 \\rfloor + 64\\bigr)$ ($n$ the number of digits) it is rounded exactly: $D \\cdot 5^{k} \\cdot 2^{k}$ by the dyadic finalizer for $k \\ge 0$, and $D / 5^{|k|} \\cdot 2^{k}$ by the division finalizer for $k < 0$. Beyond that bound it uses directed enclosures $[\\operatorname{RD}_w(D)\\operatorname{RD}_w(10^k), \\operatorname{RU}_w(D)\\operatorname{RU}_w(10^k)]$ at a working precision $w$, doubled until both ends round to the same value with the same flags. The bound makes the loop terminate. The rounding breakpoints of a direction are the points of $F$ (directed modes) or the midpoints between them (nearest modes); both are dyadic with at most $p + 1$ significant bits. For $k \\ge 0$ the odd part of $D 10^{k}$ is a multiple of $5^{k}$, and $5^{k} > 2^{2.32 k} > 2^{p+2}$ beyond the bound, so the value is no breakpoint: $k > \\lfloor (3n+p)/2 \\rfloor + 64 > (p+2)/2.32$. For $k < 0$, $|k| > 1.5n$ gives $5^{|k|} > 10^{n} > D$, so $5^{|k|} \\n"
"mid D$ and $D/10^{|k|}$ is not even dyadic. The points where a flag changes (the overflow threshold, $2^{e_{\\min}}$ for tininess, the points of $F$ for inexactness) are dyadic with at most $p + 1$ significant bits as well. A value that is none of these has a positive distance to all of them, and the enclosure, whose relative width is $O(2^{-w})$, eventually lies strictly between two of them, so some $w$ certifies it; with no count limit (`BinaryContext::with_refinement_limit(None)`) the loop ends by itself once $w$ passes the work cap below. Values whose binary logarithm is certainly beyond the range, estimated with $\\log_2 10$ and a safety margin, overflow or underflow without any arithmetic, so `1e100000000` costs nothing."
msgstr ""
"**解析。** `from_string_ctx` 精确读取 $D \\cdot 10^{k}$（$D$ 为不带末尾零的整数）。对于至多 $\\max\\bigl(400, \\lfloor (3n + p)/2 \\rfloor + 64\\bigr)$ 的 $|k|$（$n$ 为数字位数），它被精确舍入：$k \\ge 0$ 时由二进有理终结器处理 $D \\cdot 5^{k} \\cdot 2^{k}$，$k < 0$ 时由除法终结器处理 $D / 5^{|k|} \\cdot 2^{k}$。超出该界后，它在工作精度 $w$ 下使用定向包络 $[\\operatorname{RD}_w(D)\\operatorname{RD}_w(10^k), \\operatorname{RU}_w(D)\\operatorname{RU}_w(10^k)]$，并将精度加倍，直到两端舍入到相同的值且标志相同。该界保证循环终止。某一方向的舍入断点是 $F$ 中的点（定向模式）或它们之间的中点（就近模式）；二者都是至多有 $p + 1$ 位有效位的二进有理数。对于 $k \\ge 0$，$D 10^{k}$ 的奇数部分是 $5^{k}$ 的倍数，且超出该界后 $5^{k} > 2^{2.32 k} > 2^{p+2}$，因此该值不是断点：$k > \\lfloor (3n+p)/2 \\rfloor + 64 > (p+2)/2.32$。对于 $k < 0$，$|k| > 1.5n$ 给出 $5^{|k|} > 10^{n} > D$，因此 $5^{|k|} \\n"
"mid D$，而 $D/10^{|k|}$ 甚至不是二进有理数。标志发生变化的点（上溢阈值、微小性的 $2^{e_{\\min}}$、不精确性的 $F$ 中的点）同样是至多有 $p + 1$ 位有效位的二进有理数。不属于其中任何一类的值到它们都有正的距离，而相对宽度为 $O(2^{-w})$ 的包络最终会严格落在其中两个点之间，因此某个 $w$ 必能完成认证；在不设次数上限（`BinaryContext::with_refinement_limit(None)`）时，循环会在 $w$ 越过下文的工作上限后自行结束。以 $\\log_2 10$ 和安全余量估计、其二进制对数必然超出范围的值，无需任何算术即直接上溢或下溢，因此 `1e100000000` 不产生任何开销。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:773
msgid "**Hexadecimal parsing.** The value of a hexSequence is the integer of its hex digits times a power of two, so it is exactly a dyadic rational and no enclosure is needed: `from_hex_ctx` parses once (the grammar function is shared with `from_hex`) and hands the integer and the binary exponent to the same dyadic finalizer as the arithmetic operations, which applies the rounding direction, the exponent range, subnormals and the tininess rule, and returns the flags. A binary exponent beyond the 32-bit range is saturated: the value is then above $2^{2^{31}-1}$ or below $2^{-2^{31}+b}$ ($b$ the number of bits of the integer), outside every exponent range, so it overflows or underflows exactly as the saturated one does. `from_hex` keeps its own range check (a parse error beyond the 32-bit range) and its results for every in-range sequence."
msgstr "**十六进制解析。** hexSequence 的值是其十六进制数字所成整数乘以 2 的幂，因此恰好是二进制有理数，不需要包络：`from_hex_ctx` 只解析一次（文法函数与 `from_hex` 共用），把整数和二进制指数交给与算术运算相同的二进制有理数终结器，由它应用舍入方向、指数范围、次正规数和 tininess 规则并返回标志。超出 32 位范围的二进制指数会被饱和：此时的值高于 $2^{2^{31}-1}$ 或低于 $2^{-2^{31}+b}$（$b$ 为该整数的位数），在任何指数范围之外，所以它的上溢或下溢与饱和后的值完全一致。`from_hex` 保留自己的范围检查（超出 32 位范围是解析错误）以及对所有范围内序列的结果。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:786
msgid "**Fixed digits.** `to_decimal_string_ctx(x, d)` needs $\\operatorname{round}(x / 10^{E - d + 1})$ with $E = \\lfloor \\log_{10}|x| \\rfloor$. $E$ starts from $\\lfloor \\operatorname{top}(x) \\log_{10} 2 \\rfloor$, which is within one of the answer, and is corrected by comparing $|x|$ with $10^{E+1}$, first through directed bounds of the power and, when they straddle, exactly. The quotient is formed exactly as an integer division when its operands have at most $2^{20}$ bits, so ties and exact results are recognised; otherwise directed enclosures are widened until both ends round to the same integer, which terminates because such a quotient is neither an integer nor a half-integer. A carry into a new leading digit ($9.99 \\to 10.0$) increments $E$ and repeats."
msgstr "**定点位数。** `to_decimal_string_ctx(x, d)` 需要满足 $E = \\lfloor \\log_{10}|x| \\rfloor$ 的 $\\operatorname{round}(x / 10^{E - d + 1})$。$E$ 从 $\\lfloor \\operatorname{top}(x) \\log_{10} 2 \\rfloor$ 开始，它与答案相差不超过一，再通过比较 $|x|$ 与 $10^{E+1}$ 加以校正，先使用幂的定向界，当它们跨越边界时再精确比较。当操作数至多有 $2^{20}$ 位时，商以整数除法精确构成，因此能识别平局和精确结果；否则就加宽定向包络，直到两端舍入到同一个整数，由于这样的商既不是整数也不是半整数，该过程必然终止。进位产生新的最高位数字（$9.99 \\to 10.0$）时，$E$ 加一并重复。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:798
msgid "**Shortest output.** Let $I(x)$ be the set of reals that round to $x$ under RNE in the context; it is an interval containing $x$. For each digit count $n$, the two $n$-digit decimals next to $x$ (truncated and rounded away from zero) are candidates, and a candidate is accepted when parsing it returns $x$, that is when it lies in $I(x)$. Acceptance is monotone in $n$: if the $n$-digit truncation $d_n$ lies in $I(x)$, the $(n+1)$-digit truncation satisfies $d_n \\le d_{n+1} \\le x$ (in magnitude), so it lies in the interval too, and likewise for the upper neighbour. So the least accepted $n$ is found by bisection on $[1, \\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 2]$, an upper bound at which a candidate is always accepted.[^shortest] If both candidates are accepted, the nearer one is chosen, then the even one, which is the nearest decimal of that length. For binary64 this reproduces the host formatter on every value tested."
msgstr "**最短输出。** 设 $I(x)$ 为在该上下文中以 RNE 舍入到 $x$ 的实数集合；它是一个包含 $x$ 的区间。对每个位数 $n$，$x$ 旁的两个 $n$ 位十进制数（截断的和远离零舍入的）是候选值，若解析某候选值返回 $x$，即它位于 $I(x)$ 中，则接受该候选值。接受性关于 $n$ 是单调的：若 $n$ 位截断 $d_n$ 位于 $I(x)$ 中，则 $(n+1)$ 位截断满足 $d_n \\le d_{n+1} \\le x$（按绝对值），因此它也位于该区间内，上侧邻值同理。所以最小的可接受 $n$ 可以通过在 $[1, \\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 2]$（一个候选值总能被接受的上界）上二分查找得到。[^shortest] 若两个候选值都被接受，则选择较近的那个，再选偶数的那个，这就是该长度下最接近的十进制数。对于 binary64，在所有测试过的值上它都与宿主格式化器的输出一致。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:812
msgid "The digit count $\\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 1$ suffices for round trip (Matula 1968; Goldberg 1991, Theorem 15); the extra digit is a margin for the bisection's upper end."
msgstr "位数 $\\lceil p \\log_{10} 2 \\rceil + 1$ 足以保证往返转换（Matula 1968；Goldberg 1991，定理 15）；多出的一位是为二分查找上端留的余量。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:818
msgid "**Problem.** For $f = \\exp, \\ln, \\sin, \\ldots$ the value $f(x)$ is transcendental and must be rounded correctly without knowing it."
msgstr "**问题。** 对于 $f = \\exp, \\ln, \\sin, \\ldots$，值 $f(x)$ 是超越数，必须在不知道其值的情况下正确舍入。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:821
msgid "**Options.** Fixed polynomial approximations with a proven error bound (fast, but tied to one precision); Ziv's strategy of evaluating with an a priori error bound and retrying at a higher precision when the rounding is ambiguous;[^ziv] or interval evaluation."
msgstr "**可选方案。** 具有已证明误差界的固定多项式逼近（速度快，但绑定于单一精度）；Ziv 策略，即以先验误差界求值，在舍入有歧义时以更高精度重试；[^ziv] 或区间求值。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:826
msgid ""
"**Choice.** A Ziv loop whose error bound is not estimated but computed: every elementary function evaluates an enclosure $[L, U] \\n"
"i f(x)$ in which every internal operation is rounded downward for $L$ and upward for $U$ at a working precision $w$. If"
msgstr ""
"**选择。** 采用误差界经计算而非估计的 Ziv 循环：每个初等函数在工作精度 $w$ 下求出一个包络 $[L, U] \\n"
"i f(x)$，其中每个内部运算对 $L$ 向下舍入，对 $U$ 向上舍入。若"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:835
msgid "the common value is returned, otherwise $w$ grows. **The value is sound by (R2):** $L \\le f(x) \\le U$ implies $\\circ(L) \\le \\circ(f(x)) \\le \\circ(U)$, so equal ends force $\\circ(f(x)) = \\circ(L)$."
msgstr "则返回该公共值，否则增大 $w$。**由 (R2) 可知该值是可靠的：** $L \\le f(x) \\le U$ 蕴含 $\\circ(L) \\le \\circ(f(x)) \\le \\circ(U)$，因此两端相等必然得到 $\\circ(f(x)) = \\circ(L)$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:839
msgid "The flags need a separate argument. Overflow and tininess (under either rule) depend only on $|r|$ through a threshold, so on one side of zero they are monotone: if $L$ and $U$ (which have the same sign once they round to the same nonzero value) agree, every $r \\in [L, U]$ agrees with them. Inexactness is not monotone: it is false exactly on $F$. If $L < U$ round to the same value $v$ with `inexact`, then $f(x)$ is inexact *unless* $f(x) = v \\in F$. The loop cannot tell these apart, so the flags are right only if every input whose exact result lies in $F$ is caught before the loop. That is why the exact cases below are filtered, and why an exact case that is missed shows up as a spurious `inexact` (nearest rounding) or as a budget failure (directed rounding, where $L$ and $U$ round to different neighbours of $v$)."
msgstr "标志需要单独论证。上溢和微小性（无论采用哪种规则）只通过某个阈值依赖于 $|r|$，因此在零的同一侧它们是单调的：若 $L$ 和 $U$（一旦舍入到同一个非零值，它们就同号）一致，则每个 $r \\in [L, U]$ 都与它们一致。不精确性不是单调的：它恰在 $F$ 上为假。若 $L < U$ 带 `inexact` 舍入到同一个值 $v$，则 $f(x)$ 是不精确的，*除非* $f(x) = v \\in F$。循环无法区分这两种情况，因此只有当每个精确结果位于 $F$ 中的输入都在循环之前被捕获时，标志才是正确的。这就是下文的精确情形要被过滤的原因，也是漏掉的精确情形会表现为虚假的 `inexact`（就近舍入）或预算失败（定向舍入，此时 $L$ 和 $U$ 舍入到 $v$ 的不同相邻值）的原因。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:852
msgid "The enclosures come from series with rigorous tails and from monotone reductions. For $\\exp$ on $[0, 1/8]$, the terms $t_k = x^k/k!$ satisfy $t_{k+1}/t_k = x/(k+1) \\le 1/8$, so after the last summed term $t_n$"
msgstr "包络来自具有严格尾项界的级数以及单调的约简。对于 $[0, 1/8]$ 上的 $\\exp$，各项 $t_k = x^k/k!$ 满足 $t_{k+1}/t_k = x/(k+1) \\le 1/8$，因此在最后一个求和项 $t_n$ 之后"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:860
msgid "and the code stops once $t_n < 2^{-(w+8)}$ and adds $2 t_n$ (rounded upward) to the upper sum; the lower sum of positive terms is already a lower bound. Larger arguments are halved $r$ times and the result squared $r$ times, which is monotone on positive numbers and therefore keeps the enclosure; $e^{-x} = 1/e^{x}$ handles negative arguments. For $\\ln v$ with $v \\in [1, 2]$ the series is"
msgstr "一旦 $t_n < 2^{-(w+8)}$，代码即停止，并将 $2 t_n$（向上舍入）加到上和中；正项的下和本身已是下界。较大的参数先减半 $r$ 次，结果再平方 $r$ 次，平方在正数上是单调的，因此保持包络；$e^{-x} = 1/e^{x}$ 处理负参数。对于满足 $v \\in [1, 2]$ 的 $\\ln v$，级数为"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:871
msgid "with tail $\\sum_{k \\ge m} z^{2k+1}/(2k+1) \\le \\frac{z^{2m+1}}{2m+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - z^2}$, the bound the code adds. The trigonometric functions reduce $x$ by an enclosure of $\\pi/2$ (the cached binary-splitting $\\pi$, see \"Where $\\pi$ comes from\" below) at $w \\ge p + \\max(0, \\operatorname{top}(x) + 1) + 96$ bits, so the quadrant $k = \\operatorname{round}(x / (\\pi/2))$ is the same integer at both ends of the enclosure; otherwise the attempt is repeated at a higher precision. This is the Payne–Hanek idea realised by brute precision instead of a stored table of $2/\\pi$; its cost grows with $\\log_2|x|$, so inputs needing more than $10^6$ bits are refused with `ResourceLimit` rather than run for minutes."
msgstr "其尾项为 $\\sum_{k \\ge m} z^{2k+1}/(2k+1) \\le \\frac{z^{2m+1}}{2m+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - z^2}$，即代码所加的界。三角函数在 $w \\ge p + \\max(0, \\operatorname{top}(x) + 1) + 96$ 位下用 $\\pi/2$ 的包络（已缓存的二分拆分 $\\pi$，见下文“$\\pi$ 的来源”）约简 $x$，使象限 $k = \\operatorname{round}(x / (\\pi/2))$ 在包络两端是同一个整数；否则以更高精度重试。这是以暴力提高精度而非存储 $2/\\pi$ 表格的方式实现的 Payne–Hanek 思想；其代价随 $\\log_2|x|$ 增长，因此需要超过 $10^6$ 位的输入会以 `ResourceLimit` 被拒绝，而不是运行数分钟。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:882
msgid "**Budget.** The loop starts at $w_0 = p + 64$ (for some functions at the operand precision plus 16 when that is larger) and steps $w_{i+1} = w_i + \\max(32, \\lfloor w_i/2 \\rfloor)$, at most $L$ attempts, where $L$ is the refinement limit of the context (`BinaryContext::refinement_limit`, default $12$; a value below $1$ counts as $1$). For binary64 and $L = 12$ the sequence is $117, 175, 262, \\ldots, 10053$ bits, and a hard-to-round input that needs more than that fails with a `CertificationFailure` carrying the refinement count; `Some(n)` with a larger $n$ certifies it."
msgstr "**预算。** 循环从 $w_0 = p + 64$ 开始（对某些函数，若操作数精度加 16 更大则取后者），按 $w_{i+1} = w_i + \\max(32, \\lfloor w_i/2 \\rfloor)$ 递增，至多尝试 $L$ 次，其中 $L$ 是上下文的细化限制（`BinaryContext::refinement_limit`，默认 $12$；小于 $1$ 的值按 $1$ 计）。对于 binary64 且 $L = 12$，该序列为 $117, 175, 262, \\ldots, 10053$ 位；需要更多位的难舍入输入会以带细化次数的 `CertificationFailure` 失败，而更大的 `Some(n)` 可以认证它。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:891
msgid "With $L$ = `None` the count is unbounded, but the loop is not: it stops, with the same `CertificationFailure`, when $w$ exceeds $\\max(8\\,000\\,000,\\ 256\\,w_0)$ bits (capped at $10^9$ so $w$ fits `Int32`), and a trigonometric argument that needs more than $8\\,000\\,000$ bits for its reduction is still refused with `ResourceLimit` whatever the limit. So `None` cannot allocate without bound: each step costs $O(M(w))$ for the working precision $w \\le$ the cap, and the number of steps is at most $\\log_{1.5}(\\text{cap}/w_0)$. A result that sits at distance $\\delta$ from a breakpoint needs $w \\approx \\log_2(1/\\delta)$, so the default $L = 12$ decides everything farther than about $2^{-10000}$ from a breakpoint at binary64 and `None` extends that to the cap. Functions without a context argument (the `BallFloat` enclosures) keep $12$. The exact fallback of the integer power `pown` (12 Ziv rounds, then an exact product) cannot fail and is not governed by the limit."
msgstr "当 $L$ = `None` 时，次数没有上界，但循环仍有上界：当 $w$ 超过 $\\max(8\\,000\\,000,\\ 256\\,w_0)$ 位（上限为 $10^9$，以使 $w$ 容纳于 `Int32`）时，它以同样的 `CertificationFailure` 停止；而归约所需位数超过 $8\\,000\\,000$ 的三角函数参数，无论限制为何，仍会被 `ResourceLimit` 拒绝。因此 `None` 不会无限分配：每一步的代价为 $O(M(w))$，其中工作精度 $w \\le$ 上限，步数至多为 $\\log_{1.5}(\\text{cap}/w_0)$。距断点 $\\delta$ 的结果需要 $w \\approx \\log_2(1/\\delta)$，所以在 binary64 下默认的 $L = 12$ 能判定距断点远于约 $2^{-10000}$ 的一切，`None` 则把范围扩展到上限。没有上下文参数的函数（`BallFloat` 包络）保持 $12$。整数幂 `pown` 的精确回退（12 轮 Ziv，然后精确乘积）不会失败，不受该限制约束。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:906
msgid ""
"**Termination.** Ziv's argument has two parts. First, $f(x)$ must not be a breakpoint of $\\circ$ (a point of $F$, a midpoint, or a flag threshold), all of which are dyadic. For a nonzero dyadic $x$, $e^{x}$, $\\sin x$, $\\cos x$, $\\tan x$, the hyperbolic functions, their inverses and $\\ln x$ ($x \\n"
"e 1$) are transcendental by Lindemann–Weierstrass. For $2^x$, $10^x$, $\\log_2 x$ and $\\log_{10} x$ irrationality is enough and elementary: $2^{a/b}$ with $b \\n"
"mid a$ is irrational, so $2^x$ is dyadic only for integral $x$, and $\\log_2 x = a/b$ forces $x = 2^{a/b}$, a power of two; likewise $10^x$ and $\\log_{10} x$ are dyadic only at integral $x \\ge 0$ and at $x = 10^k$. For the $\\pi$-scaled functions Niven's theorem shows that integral, half-integral and (for `tanpi`) quarter-integral arguments are the only dyadic exceptions.[^niven] For `pow` and `rootn` the exceptions are characterised under *Exact powers and roots* below. The exceptions are filtered before the loop: $e^0 = 1$, $\\ln 1 = 0$, $\\log_2 2^k = k$, $2^n$ for integral $|n| < 2^{31}$, $\\sin(\\pm 0)$, the $\\pi$-scaled cases, $10^n$ for integral $0 \\le n \\le \\max(4096, p)$ (beyond that the odd part $5^n$ has more than $p + 1$ bits, so $10^n$ is not a breakpoint), $\\log_{10} 10^n$ for every $n \\ge 1$, dyadic powers and exact roots, and so on."
msgstr ""
"**终止性。** Ziv 的论证分为两部分。第一，$f(x)$ 不能是 $\\circ$ 的断点（$F$ 中的点、中点或标志阈值），而这些都是二进有理数。对于非零二进有理数 $x$，由 Lindemann–Weierstrass 定理，$e^{x}$、$\\sin x$、$\\cos x$、$\\tan x$、双曲函数、它们的反函数以及 $\\ln x$（$x \\n"
"e 1$）都是超越数。对于 $2^x$、$10^x$、$\\log_2 x$ 和 $\\log_{10} x$，无理性就足够了，而且论证是初等的：当 $b \\n"
"mid a$ 时 $2^{a/b}$ 是无理数，因此 $2^x$ 仅在 $x$ 为整数时是二进有理数，而 $\\log_2 x = a/b$ 迫使 $x = 2^{a/b}$ 为 2 的幂；同理，$10^x$ 和 $\\log_{10} x$ 仅在整数 $x \\ge 0$ 和 $x = 10^k$ 处是二进有理数。对于以 $\\pi$ 缩放的函数，Niven 定理表明整数、半整数以及（对 `tanpi`）四分之一整数参数是仅有的二进有理例外。[^niven] 对于 `pow` 和 `rootn`，例外情形在下文*精确幂与根*中刻画。这些例外在循环之前被过滤：$e^0 = 1$、$\\ln 1 = 0$、$\\log_2 2^k = k$、整数 $|n| < 2^{31}$ 的 $2^n$、$\\sin(\\pm 0)$、以 $\\pi$ 缩放的情形、整数 $0 \\le n \\le \\max(4096, p)$ 时的 $10^n$（超出此范围时奇数部分 $5^n$ 多于 $p + 1$ 位，因此 $10^n$ 不是断点）、每个 $n \\ge 1$ 的 $\\log_{10} 10^n$、二进有理数幂和精确根，等等。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:925
msgid "Second, the enclosure must shrink onto $f(x)$ fast enough. The series stop when the next term is below $2^{-(w+8)}$ or $2^{-(w+12)}$ in *absolute* value, which is fine for arguments of moderate size; the width then is $O(2^{-w})$ relative to $f(x)$, a non-breakpoint has a positive distance to every breakpoint, and some $w$ certifies it. Tiny arguments need the two measures under *Tiny arguments* below. How large $w$ must be is the table maker's dilemma: no useful a priori bound is known for arbitrary $p$, so the budget is a resource limit, not a correctness condition. When it runs out the `try_*` form reports a `CertificationFailure` with the stage, the reason and the last $w$, and the total forms return a quiet NaN with `invalid_operation`; neither returns an uncertified value. The pinned MPFR corpus never exhausts it."
msgstr "第二，包络必须足够快地收缩到 $f(x)$ 上。当下一项的*绝对*值低于 $2^{-(w+8)}$ 或 $2^{-(w+12)}$ 时级数停止，这对中等大小的参数没有问题；此时宽度相对于 $f(x)$ 为 $O(2^{-w})$，非断点到每个断点都有正的距离，因此某个 $w$ 能完成认证。微小参数需要下文*微小参数*中的两项措施。$w$ 必须多大，就是制表者困境：对任意 $p$ 都没有已知有用的先验界，因此预算是资源限制，而不是正确性条件。预算耗尽时，`try_*` 形式报告一个 `CertificationFailure`，包含阶段、原因和最后的 $w$，全函数形式则返回带 `invalid_operation` 的静默 NaN；两者都不会返回未经认证的值。固定的 MPFR 语料从未耗尽预算。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:938
msgid "**Exact powers and roots.** An integral exponent with $|y| < 2^{31}$ goes to `pown`. A larger integral $y$ needs no filter: for $x = c \\cdot 2^e$ with $c > 1$ odd, $c^{|y|}$ has more than $2^{31} > p + 1$ bits, and a power of two $2^{ey}$ lies outside every exponent range, so neither is a breakpoint. Every other exponent is $y = m / 2^k$ with $m$ odd and $k \\ge 1$. If $x^y$ is rational, so is $q = x^{|y|}$, and $x^{|m|} = q^{2^k}$; comparing the exponents of $2$ and of each odd prime gives $q = a \\cdot 2^f$ with $a$ odd, $e|m| = f \\cdot 2^k$ and $c^{|m|} = a^{2^k}$. Since $|m|$ is odd, $2^k \\mid e$ and every prime exponent of $c$ is divisible by $2^k$, so $c = r^{2^k}$ and $q = r^{|m|} \\cdot 2^{e|m|/2^k}$. Conversely these values are exact. So a rational `pow` result exists exactly under these two divisibility conditions; for $m > 0$ it is the dyadic $q$, and for $m < 0$ it is $1/q$, which is dyadic only when $r = 1$. Every other `pow` result is irrational. `binary_pow_exact_dyadic` computes the dyadic results and rounds them once, unless the odd part $r^m$ would need more than $2p + 64$ bits (then it has more than $p + 1$ significant bits and is not a breakpoint). The same argument with $1/|n|$ in place of $|y|$ shows that $\\operatorname{rootn}(x, n)$ is rational exactly when $|n| \\mid e$ and $c = r^{|n|}$; `rootn` returns $\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|}$ rounded once for $n > 0$, and for $n < 0$ the correctly rounded quotient $1 / (\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|})$, which division decides with the right `inexact` flag although it need not be dyadic. The perfect-power test has no size limit. It first takes square roots with remainder for every factor $2$ of the degree, stopping at the first nonzero remainder, and then the floor of the remaining odd root: by bisection while the root has at most 64 bits, otherwise by integer Newton steps $r \\leftarrow \\lfloor ((d-1) r + \\lfloor c / r^{d-1} \\rfloor) / d \\rfloor$ started just above the root, which decrease monotonically to $\\lfloor c^{1/d} \\rfloor$; one power $r^d$ then decides exactness. A coefficient with at most $d$ bits other than $1$ is rejected at once, because $r \\ge 2$ gives $r^d \\ge 2^d$."
msgstr "**精确幂与根。** $|y| < 2^{31}$ 的整数指数交给 `pown` 处理。更大的整数 $y$ 无需过滤：对 $x = c \\cdot 2^e$（$c > 1$ 为奇数），$c^{|y|}$ 多于 $2^{31} > p + 1$ 位，而 2 的幂 $2^{ey}$ 位于任何指数范围之外，因此两者都不是断点。其余每个指数都可写成 $y = m / 2^k$，其中 $m$ 为奇数且 $k \\ge 1$。若 $x^y$ 是有理数，则 $q = x^{|y|}$ 也是，并且 $x^{|m|} = q^{2^k}$；比较 $2$ 及每个奇素数的指数可得 $q = a \\cdot 2^f$，其中 $a$ 为奇数，$e|m| = f \\cdot 2^k$ 且 $c^{|m|} = a^{2^k}$。由于 $|m|$ 是奇数，$2^k \\mid e$，且 $c$ 的每个素数指数都能被 $2^k$ 整除，因此 $c = r^{2^k}$ 且 $q = r^{|m|} \\cdot 2^{e|m|/2^k}$。反之，这些值都是精确的。所以有理的 `pow` 结果恰在这两个整除条件下存在；当 $m > 0$ 时它是二进有理数 $q$，当 $m < 0$ 时它是 $1/q$，后者仅在 $r = 1$ 时是二进有理数。其余每个 `pow` 结果都是无理数。`binary_pow_exact_dyadic` 计算这些二进有理结果并只舍入一次，除非奇数部分 $r^m$ 需要多于 $2p + 64$ 位（此时它有多于 $p + 1$ 个有效位，不是断点）。用 $1/|n|$ 代替 $|y|$ 作同样的论证可知，$\\operatorname{rootn}(x, n)$ 恰在 $|n| \\mid e$ 且 $c = r^{|n|}$ 时是有理数；对 $n > 0$，`rootn` 返回只舍入一次的 $\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|}$，对 $n < 0$ 则返回正确舍入的商 $1 / (\\pm r \\cdot 2^{e/|n|})$——该商未必是二进有理数，但除法会以正确的 `inexact` 标志判定它。完全幂检测没有大小限制。它先对次数中的每个因子 $2$ 求带余数的平方根，遇到第一个非零余数即停止，然后求剩余奇数次根的下取整：根至多 64 位时用二分法，否则用从略高于根处开始的整数牛顿迭代 $r \\leftarrow \\lfloor ((d-1) r + \\lfloor c / r^{d-1} \\rfloor) / d \\rfloor$，它单调递减到 $\\lfloor c^{1/d} \\rfloor$；随后由一次幂运算 $r^d$ 判定是否精确。除 $1$ 之外至多 $d$ 位的系数会被立即拒绝，因为 $r \\ge 2$ 给出 $r^d \\ge 2^d$。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:968
msgid "A negative base with an integral exponent beyond the `pown` range is evaluated as $\\pm|x|^y$. Negation is an exact symmetry of $\\circ$ that swaps the two directed modes, $\\circ_{\\mathrm{RD}}(-v) = -\\circ_{\\mathrm{RU}}(v)$, so for an odd $y$ the code rounds $|x|^y$ with RD and RU exchanged and negates."
msgstr "底数为负、整数指数超出 `pown` 范围时，按 $\\pm|x|^y$ 求值。取负是 $\\circ$ 的一个精确对称，它交换两种定向模式：$\\circ_{\\mathrm{RD}}(-v) = -\\circ_{\\mathrm{RU}}(v)$，因此对奇数 $y$，代码交换 RD 与 RU 来舍入 $|x|^y$，再取负。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:973
msgid "**Tiny arguments.** For small enough $|x|$ (about $2^{-p/2}$ for the odd functions, $2^{-p}$ for $e^x$) the result lies closer to a representable number $a$ than the target spacing: $a = x$ for the odd functions, $a = 1$ for $e^x$, $\\cos$, $\\cosh$. An enclosure whose series stops after its first term then has $a$ itself as one end ($U = x$ for $\\sin$, $L = 1$ for $e^x$), and that end rounds without `inexact` while the other end rounds with it, so the acceptance test alone would only pass once $w$ separates $f(x)$ from $a$, at $w \\approx \\log_2(1/|x|)$ or more. Two measures remove the dependence on $|x|$."
msgstr "**微小参数。** 对足够小的 $|x|$（奇函数约为 $2^{-p/2}$，$e^x$ 约为 $2^{-p}$），结果到某个可表示数 $a$ 的距离小于目标间距：对奇函数 $a = x$，对 $e^x$、$\\cos$、$\\cosh$ 则 $a = 1$。级数在第一项后即停止的包络于是以 $a$ 本身为一端（对 $\\sin$ 为 $U = x$，对 $e^x$ 为 $L = 1$），该端舍入时不带 `inexact`，而另一端舍入时带有它，因此仅靠接受测试，要等到 $w$ 把 $f(x)$ 与 $a$ 区分开时才能通过，即 $w \\approx \\log_2(1/|x|)$ 或更大。两项措施消除了对 $|x|$ 的依赖。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:982
msgid ""
"*Inner endpoints.* Every result that reaches the loop is known not to be a breakpoint. For every function other than `pow` and `rootn`, `binary_certified_inexact_target_rounding` replaces an end $E$ that could be a breakpoint (an odd coefficient of at most $p + 1$ bits) by $E' = E \\pm 2^{e_E - s}$ toward the inside of the enclosure, with $s = \\max(1, p + 3 - \\operatorname{bits}(c_E))$. If the leading bit of $E$ is $2^t$, breakpoints near $E$ are at least $2^{t - p - 1}$ apart and the offset is at most $2^{t - p - 2}$, so no breakpoint lies in $(E, E']$. Since $f(x) \\n"
"e E$, either $f(x)$ lies beyond $E'$ or between $E$ and $E'$, and in the second case it shares the open cell between breakpoints with $E'$ and rounds like it. So $\\circ(E') = \\circ(U')$ with equal flags still forces $\\circ(f(x))$ and its flags, and the test passes as soon as the enclosure is narrower than the spacing, independently of $|x|$. `pow` uses inner endpoints whenever its exactness test (above) has shown that the result is irrational, not dyadic, or wider than $p + 1$ bits, so a tiny exponent with $x^y$ closer to $1$ than the target spacing is certified too ($2^{2^{-16000}}$ in binary128 is $1$ with `inexact`). The test leaves a few cases with a power-of-two base undecided (an exponent of magnitude at least $2^{31}$, or a scale outside the 32-bit range); those keep the plain acceptance test."
msgstr ""
"*内端点。* 每个进入循环的结果都已知不是断点。对除 `pow` 和 `rootn` 之外的每个函数，`binary_certified_inexact_target_rounding` 把可能是断点的端点 $E$（至多 $p + 1$ 位的奇数系数）替换为朝包络内侧移动的 $E' = E \\pm 2^{e_E - s}$，其中 $s = \\max(1, p + 3 - \\operatorname{bits}(c_E))$。若 $E$ 的最高位为 $2^t$，则 $E$ 附近的断点间隔至少为 $2^{t - p - 1}$，而偏移至多为 $2^{t - p - 2}$，因此 $(E, E']$ 中没有断点。由于 $f(x) \\n"
"e E$，$f(x)$ 要么位于 $E'$ 之外，要么位于 $E$ 与 $E'$ 之间；在后一种情况下，它与 $E'$ 处于断点之间的同一开单元中，舍入结果与之相同。所以标志相同的 $\\circ(E') = \\circ(U')$ 仍然确定 $\\circ(f(x))$ 及其标志，并且只要包络窄于间距测试就会通过，与 $|x|$ 无关。只要 `pow` 的精确性检测（见上文）已表明结果是无理数、不是二进有理数或宽于 $p + 1$ 位，`pow` 就使用内端点，因此 $x^y$ 距 $1$ 比目标间距还近的极小指数也能得到认证（binary128 中的 $2^{2^{-16000}}$ 为 $1$ 并触发 `inexact`）。该检测会留下少数底数为 2 的幂的情形无法判定（指数的绝对值至少为 $2^{31}$，或缩放超出 32 位范围）；这些情形保留普通的接受测试。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1003
msgid "*Tiny-argument bounds.* Some enclosures (for $\\sinh$, $\\tanh$ via $e^x - e^{-x}$, and for $\\operatorname{asinh}$, $\\operatorname{atanh}$, $\\operatorname{asin}$, $\\tan$, `expm1`, `log1p`) straddle the neighbour of $a$ until $w \\approx 3\\log_2(1/|x|)$. For $|x| \\le 1/2$ the series give one-sided bounds with a known side: $0 < x - \\sin x$, $0 < \\tan x - x$, $0 < \\operatorname{asin} x - x$, $0 < \\sinh x - x$, $0 < x - \\tanh x$, $0 < x - \\operatorname{asinh} x$, $0 < \\operatorname{atanh} x - x$, each at most $|x|^3$ (for $x > 0$, mirrored for $x < 0$), and $0 < 1 - \\cos x$, $0 < \\cosh x - 1$, $0 < \\operatorname{expm1}(x) - x$, $0 < x - \\operatorname{log1p}(x)$, each at most $x^2$. With $|x| < 2^T$, `binary_tiny_argument_result` uses the enclosure $[a, a + 2^{\\sigma}]$ or $[a - 2^{\\sigma}, a]$ with $\\sigma = 3T$ (respectively $2T$), raised to at least $t_a - p - 8$, when $\\sigma < t_a - p - 3$ ($2^{t_a}$ the leading bit of $a$), and rounds it with inner endpoints. The condition implies $|x| < 2^{-(p+3)/2} \\le 1/2$, so the bounds apply, and the enclosure is at most a quarter of the breakpoint spacing at $a$ wide. When $a$ is a breakpoint, both ends lie in the cell next to $a$ and the result is decided before the loop; otherwise (an argument wider than $p + 1$ bits) the loop runs as usual. With both measures `sin` and `atan` of $2^{-6000}$ at 53 bits and $e^{2^{-20000}}$ are certified in every rounding mode."
msgstr "*微小参数界。* 某些包络（$\\sinh$、经由 $e^x - e^{-x}$ 的 $\\tanh$，以及 $\\operatorname{asinh}$、$\\operatorname{atanh}$、$\\operatorname{asin}$、$\\tan$、`expm1`、`log1p`）在 $w \\approx 3\\log_2(1/|x|)$ 之前会跨越 $a$ 的相邻值。对 $|x| \\le 1/2$，级数给出方向已知的单侧界：$0 < x - \\sin x$、$0 < \\tan x - x$、$0 < \\operatorname{asin} x - x$、$0 < \\sinh x - x$、$0 < x - \\tanh x$、$0 < x - \\operatorname{asinh} x$、$0 < \\operatorname{atanh} x - x$，各自至多为 $|x|^3$（对 $x > 0$；$x < 0$ 时对称），以及 $0 < 1 - \\cos x$、$0 < \\cosh x - 1$、$0 < \\operatorname{expm1}(x) - x$、$0 < x - \\operatorname{log1p}(x)$，各自至多为 $x^2$。设 $|x| < 2^T$，当 $\\sigma < t_a - p - 3$（$2^{t_a}$ 为 $a$ 的最高位）时，`binary_tiny_argument_result` 使用包络 $[a, a + 2^{\\sigma}]$ 或 $[a - 2^{\\sigma}, a]$，其中 $\\sigma = 3T$（相应地为 $2T$），并提升到至少 $t_a - p - 8$，再用内端点对其舍入。该条件蕴含 $|x| < 2^{-(p+3)/2} \\le 1/2$，因此上述界适用，并且包络宽度至多为 $a$ 处断点间距的四分之一。当 $a$ 是断点时，两端都位于紧邻 $a$ 的单元中，结果在循环之前即已确定；否则（参数宽于 $p + 1$ 位）循环照常运行。借助这两项措施，53 位下 $2^{-6000}$ 的 `sin` 与 `atan` 以及 $e^{2^{-20000}}$ 在每种舍入模式下都能得到认证。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1024
msgid ""
"`rootn` keeps the plain test, and `pow` uses it only for the few results its exactness test cannot classify. For `rootn` it suffices: its enclosure is $e^{\\ln(x)/n}$ at a working precision above the operand precision $q$, and $|\\ln x| / |n| > 2^{-(q + 31)}$ for $x \\n"
"e 1$ and $|n| \\le 10^9$, so an end at $1$ disappears after an attempt or two. `pow` evaluates $e^{y \\ln x}$, where $y$ can be arbitrarily small: an exponent so small that $x^y$ lies closer to $1$ than the target spacing gives an enclosure with $L = 1$ at every affordable $w$. That is why `pow` moves such an end inward once its exactness test has excluded a breakpoint, as described under inner endpoints; for example $2^{2^{-16000}}$ in binary128 is then $1$ with `inexact`."
msgstr ""
"`rootn` 保留普通测试，`pow` 仅对其精确性检测无法分类的少数结果使用普通测试。对 `rootn` 这已足够：其包络是以高于操作数精度 $q$ 的工作精度计算的 $e^{\\ln(x)/n}$，而对 $x \\n"
"e 1$ 和 $|n| \\le 10^9$ 有 $|\\ln x| / |n| > 2^{-(q + 31)}$，因此位于 $1$ 的端点在一两次尝试后就会消失。`pow` 计算 $e^{y \\ln x}$，其中 $y$ 可以任意小：当指数小到使 $x^y$ 到 $1$ 的距离小于目标间距时，在任何可承受的 $w$ 下包络都有 $L = 1$。正因如此，如内端点部分所述，`pow` 在其精确性检测排除断点之后会把这样的端点向内移动；例如 binary128 中的 $2^{2^{-16000}}$ 由此为 $1$ 并触发 `inexact`。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1035
msgid "I. Niven, *Irrational Numbers*, 1956, Corollary 3.12: if $r$ is rational and $\\sin(\\pi r)$ is rational, then $\\sin(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm\\frac12, \\pm 1\\}$; similarly for $\\cos$, and $\\tan(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm 1\\}$. The value $\\pm\\frac12$ needs $r$ with denominator 6 or 3, which is not dyadic."
msgstr "I. Niven，*Irrational Numbers*，1956，推论 3.12：若 $r$ 为有理数且 $\\sin(\\pi r)$ 为有理数，则 $\\sin(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm\\frac12, \\pm 1\\}$；$\\cos$ 同理，以及 $\\tan(\\pi r) \\in \\{0, \\pm 1\\}$。值 $\\pm\\frac12$ 需要分母为 6 或 3 的 $r$，而这不是二进有理数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1041
msgid "A. Ziv, \"Fast evaluation of elementary mathematical functions with correctly rounded last bit\", *ACM TOMS* 17(3), 1991; for interval evaluation see W. Tucker, *Validated Numerics*, Princeton 2011, and F. Johansson, \"Arb: efficient arbitrary-precision midpoint-radius interval arithmetic\", *IEEE Trans. Computers* 66(8), 2017."
msgstr "A. Ziv，\"Fast evaluation of elementary mathematical functions with correctly rounded last bit\"，*ACM TOMS* 17(3)，1991；区间求值参见 W. Tucker，*Validated Numerics*，Princeton 2011，以及 F. Johansson，\"Arb: efficient arbitrary-precision midpoint-radius interval arithmetic\"，*IEEE Trans. Computers* 66(8)，2017。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1047
msgid "**Integer powers.** `pown_ctx` computes $x^n$ by an addition chain at $w = p + \\operatorname{bits}(n) + \\operatorname{bits}(p) + 4$ bits with round-to-nearest. Each chain step $a_k = a_i + a_j$ multiplies two approximations; if $x^{a} \\prod (1 + \\delta)^{E(a)}$ describes the error structure, then $E(a_k) = E(a_i) + E(a_j) + 1$ and $E(1) = 0$, so by induction $E(a) \\le a - 1$. The computed value is therefore $x^n (1 + \\theta)$ with $|\\theta| \\le \\gamma_{n-1} = (n-1)u_w/(1 - (n-1)u_w)$ in Higham's notation, which is below $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n)}$ units in the last place of the $w$-bit result. The code uses the radius $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n) + 2}$ units (one more factor of two for a negative power, whose reciprocal adds $n$ further factors), builds the interval, and accepts when both ends round alike, by the same (R2) argument. When 12 attempts (with $w$ doubled between them) do not certify, the exact power $c^n 2^{ne}$ is formed and rounded, so the result is correctly rounded in every case. A power certainly outside the range is decided first from certified $\\log_2$ bounds; powers of two and powers whose exact value fits in $p$ bits are computed exactly. The Ziv path therefore only sees $c^n$ with $c > 1$ odd and more than $p$ bits, or $1/c^n$, which is not dyadic: neither is in $F$, so the `inexact` it reports is right (the flag argument above). A $c^n$ with exactly $p + 1$ bits is a midpoint; the enclosure then never certifies under nearest rounding and the exact fallback decides it."
msgstr "**整数幂。** `pown_ctx` 在 $w = p + \\operatorname{bits}(n) + \\operatorname{bits}(p) + 4$ 位下以就近舍入通过加法链计算 $x^n$。每个链步 $a_k = a_i + a_j$ 将两个近似值相乘；若 $x^{a} \\prod (1 + \\delta)^{E(a)}$ 描述了误差结构，则 $E(a_k) = E(a_i) + E(a_j) + 1$ 且 $E(1) = 0$，由归纳得 $E(a) \\le a - 1$。因此计算值为 $x^n (1 + \\theta)$，用 Higham 的记号即 $|\\theta| \\le \\gamma_{n-1} = (n-1)u_w/(1 - (n-1)u_w)$，它小于 $w$ 位结果的 $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n)}$ 个末位单位。代码使用半径 $2^{\\operatorname{bits}(n) + 2}$ 个单位（对负幂再多一个因子 2，其倒数还会再增加 $n$ 个因子），构建区间，并在两端舍入相同时接受，依据同样的 (R2) 论证。若 12 次尝试（每次之间 $w$ 加倍）仍无法认证，则构造精确幂 $c^n 2^{ne}$ 并舍入，因此结果在任何情况下都是正确舍入的。必然超出范围的幂会先依据经认证的 $\\log_2$ 界判定；2 的幂以及精确值能放入 $p$ 位的幂会被精确计算。因此 Ziv 路径只会遇到 $c > 1$ 为奇数且多于 $p$ 位的 $c^n$，或者不是二进有理数的 $1/c^n$：两者都不在 $F$ 中，所以它报告的 `inexact` 是正确的（见上文关于标志的论证）。恰好有 $p + 1$ 位的 $c^n$ 是中点；此时包络在就近舍入下永远无法完成认证，由精确回退来判定。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1069
msgid "**hypot.** `hypot` forms $a^2 + b^2$ exactly from the coefficients and takes one correctly rounded square root, so it needs no loop; the cost is the alignment shift between the two squares. For $|a| \\ge |b| > 0$, $|a| < \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} \\le |a| + b^2 / (2|a|)$. Write $|a| = c \\cdot 2^e$ with leading bit $2^t$ and $g = 2^{\\min(e,\\, t - p - 1)}$: $|a|$ and every rounding breakpoint near it are multiples of $g$, so when $b^2 < 2|a|g$ no breakpoint lies in $(|a|, |a| + b^2/(2|a|)]$ and every such $b$ gives the same rounded result and flags. $|b| < g/8$ is enough, and `binary_hypot_negligible_operand` then replaces $b$ by $g/8$, which keeps the shift at about twice the operand and target precisions however far apart the exponents are ($\\operatorname{hypot}(1, 2^{-600000}) = 1$ with `inexact`). A shift above $10^6$ bits is still refused as a `certification_failure`; after the replacement it needs a precision near $500\\,000$ bits."
msgstr "**hypot。** `hypot` 由系数精确构成 $a^2 + b^2$，并做一次正确舍入的平方根，因此不需要循环；代价是两个平方之间的对齐移位。对 $|a| \\ge |b| > 0$，有 $|a| < \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} \\le |a| + b^2 / (2|a|)$。记 $|a| = c \\cdot 2^e$，其最高位为 $2^t$，并令 $g = 2^{\\min(e,\\, t - p - 1)}$：$|a|$ 及其附近的每个舍入断点都是 $g$ 的倍数，因此当 $b^2 < 2|a|g$ 时，$(|a|, |a| + b^2/(2|a|)]$ 中没有断点，每个这样的 $b$ 都给出相同的舍入结果和标志。$|b| < g/8$ 就足够了，此时 `binary_hypot_negligible_operand` 将 $b$ 替换为 $g/8$，这样无论两个指数相距多远，移位都保持在操作数精度与目标精度的约两倍（$\\operatorname{hypot}(1, 2^{-600000}) = 1$，带 `inexact`）。超过 $10^6$ 位的移位仍会作为 `certification_failure` 被拒绝；替换之后，这需要接近 $500\\,000$ 位的精度。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1083
msgid ""
"**`atan`, `asin`, `acos` and `atan2`: one evaluation chain for the pair.** The enclosure of $\\operatorname{atan}$ over a pair $[a, b]$ is computed by one chain, not by one chain per endpoint. $\\operatorname{atan}$ is odd and increasing, so $L = \\operatorname{lower}(\\operatorname{atan}\\,a)$ and $U = \\operatorname{upper}(\\operatorname{atan}\\,b)$ enclose $\\operatorname{atan}$ on the whole pair. For $0 \\le a \\le b$ and $b > 1/2$ the reduction is $\\operatorname{atan}\\,x = 2 \\operatorname{atan}\\, r(x)$ with $r(x) = x / (1 + \\sqrt{1 + x^2}) = \\tan(\\operatorname{atan}(x)/2)$, which is increasing on $x \\ge 0$ (it is a composition of increasing maps). Hence $[r^-(a), r^+(b)] \\n"
"i r(x)$ for every $x \\in [a, b]$, where $r^-(a)$ divides $a$ rounded down by an upper bound of $1 + \\sqrt{1 + a^2}$ and $r^+(b)$ divides $b$ rounded up by a lower bound of $1 + \\sqrt{1 + b^2}$; the bounds of the denominator are directed squares, sums and square roots, each monotone on nonnegative numbers. The reduced pair is again nonnegative and ordered, so the recursion is a chain (two levels at most, because $r(x) < 1$ and $r(1) < 1/2$), and the Taylor series runs once, with its lower track on the lower end and its upper track on the upper end. A negative pair $[a, b]$ is $-[-b, -a]$; a pair that contains zero is widened to $[-m, m]$ with $m = \\max(-a, b)$, which contains it. The old code evaluated the series once for $|x| \\le 1/2$, twice up to $4/3$ and four times above (a lower and an upper call per reduction level); a point argument now costs one series at every size."
msgstr ""
"**`atan`、`asin`、`acos` 与 `atan2`：对区间对只做一条求值链。** $\\operatorname{atan}$ 在区间 $[a, b]$ 上的包络用一条链计算，而不是每个端点各一条。$\\operatorname{atan}$ 是奇函数且递增，所以 $L = \\operatorname{lower}(\\operatorname{atan}\\,a)$ 与 $U = \\operatorname{upper}(\\operatorname{atan}\\,b)$ 包络整个区间上的 $\\operatorname{atan}$。对 $0 \\le a \\le b$ 且 $b > 1/2$，约简为 $\\operatorname{atan}\\,x = 2 \\operatorname{atan}\\, r(x)$，其中 $r(x) = x / (1 + \\sqrt{1 + x^2}) = \\tan(\\operatorname{atan}(x)/2)$，它在 $x \\ge 0$ 上递增（是递增映射的复合）。因此对每个 $x \\in [a, b]$ 有 $[r^-(a), r^+(b)] \\n"
"i r(x)$，其中 $r^-(a)$ 用 $1 + \\sqrt{1 + a^2}$ 的一个上界去除向下舍入的 $a$，$r^+(b)$ 用 $1 + \\sqrt{1 + b^2}$ 的一个下界去除向上舍入的 $b$；分母的界由带方向的平方、和与平方根给出，它们在非负数上都单调。约简后的区间对仍然非负且有序，所以递归是一条链（最多两层，因为 $r(x) < 1$ 且 $r(1) < 1/2$），Taylor 级数只运行一次，下轨道作用在下端点，上轨道作用在上端点。负区间 $[a, b]$ 即 $-[-b, -a]$；包含零的区间被放宽为 $[-m, m]$，其中 $m = \\max(-a, b)$，它包含原区间。旧代码对 $|x| \\le 1/2$ 求一次级数，到 $4/3$ 求两次，再大求四次（每个约简层各一次下界调用和一次上界调用）；现在一个点参数在任何大小下都只需一次级数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1106
msgid "**Large arguments.** The square $x^2$ of the reduction leaves the exponent range for $|x| \\ge 2^{2^{29}}$, so for a leading bit of $x$ of at least $2w + 2$ the reduction is formed without it: with $y = 1/x$, $r(x) = 1 / (y + \\sqrt{1 + y^2})$ and $1 + y \\le y + \\sqrt{1 + y^2} \\le 1 + y + y^2$, hence $1/(1 + y + y^2) \\le r(x) \\le 1/(1 + y)$, evaluated with directed reciprocals of $x$; the relative gap is below $2y \\le 2^{-2w-1}$. An infinite end of a pair (a quotient of `atan2` that overflowed) is bounded by $\\pi/2$ rounded in the matching direction. The test `atan_single_evaluation_wbtest.mbt` covers $3 \\cdot 2^e$ for $e$ on both sides of $2^{29}$ and near $2^{30}$, both signs and three rounding directions, against $\\pi/2$ from the cached constant; the public results equal those of the previous code there."
msgstr "**大参数。** 约简中的平方 $x^2$ 在 $|x| \\ge 2^{2^{29}}$ 时会超出指数范围，因此当 $x$ 的最高位不低于 $2w + 2$ 时，约简不再形成平方：令 $y = 1/x$，则 $r(x) = 1 / (y + \\sqrt{1 + y^2})$ 且 $1 + y \\le y + \\sqrt{1 + y^2} \\le 1 + y + y^2$，于是 $1/(1 + y + y^2) \\le r(x) \\le 1/(1 + y)$，用带方向的 $x$ 的倒数求值；相对间隙小于 $2y \\le 2^{-2w-1}$。区间对中的无穷端点（`atan2` 中溢出的商）用向对应方向舍入的 $\\pi/2$ 界定。测试 `atan_single_evaluation_wbtest.mbt` 覆盖 $3 \\cdot 2^e$，其中 $e$ 位于 $2^{29}$ 两侧及接近 $2^{30}$，正负号及三种舍入方向，对照缓存常数给出的 $\\pi/2$；公开结果与此前的代码一致。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1119
msgid "For $\\operatorname{asin}$ the pair is the ratio $f(x) = x / \\sqrt{1 - x^2}$, increasing on $(-1, 1)$. With $\\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\in [\\rho^-, \\rho^+]$ on the operand pair (directed roots of directed $1 - x^2$), the lower end is $a / \\rho^-$ if $a < 0$ and $a / \\rho^+$ if $a \\ge 0$, the upper end is $b / \\rho^-$ if $b \\ge 0$ and $b / \\rho^+$ if $b < 0$, which replaces the eight directed quotients and the search for their minimum and maximum. For $\\operatorname{atan2}$ and $\\operatorname{atan2Pi}$ the ratio $y / x$ of a rectangle with $x$ of one strict sign takes its extremes at the corners selected by the signs of the ends of $y$ (four directed divisions replace the eight of the previous search). The soundness of the new evaluation is tested against the previous functions, kept as test-only copies, evaluated at 128 more bits (`atan_single_evaluation_wbtest.mbt`); the Ziv loops take the same number of attempts on that corpus. A pair that is wide because the operand is (`asin` close to $1$) can come out up to about 1.4 times wider than before, because the alternating-series bracket pairs the lower track with the terms of the other end; narrow pairs differ by a few units in the last place."
msgstr "对 $\\operatorname{asin}$，区间对是比值 $f(x) = x / \\sqrt{1 - x^2}$，它在 $(-1, 1)$ 上递增。设操作数区间上 $\\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\in [\\rho^-, \\rho^+]$（带方向的 $1 - x^2$ 的带方向平方根），则下端为：$a < 0$ 时取 $a / \\rho^-$，$a \\ge 0$ 时取 $a / \\rho^+$；上端为：$b \\ge 0$ 时取 $b / \\rho^-$，$b < 0$ 时取 $b / \\rho^+$，这取代了八次带方向除法以及对其最小值和最大值的搜索。对 $\\operatorname{atan2}$ 与 $\\operatorname{atan2Pi}$，当 $x$ 的符号严格唯一时，矩形上的比值 $y / x$ 在由 $y$ 两端符号选定的角点取极值（四次带方向除法取代此前搜索中的八次）。新求值的可靠性对照此前的函数进行测试，这些旧函数作为仅测试用的副本保留，并以多 128 位求值（`atan_single_evaluation_wbtest.mbt`）；在该语料上 Ziv 循环所需的尝试次数相同。当操作数本身就很宽时（`asin` 接近 $1$），区间对可能比以前宽至约 1.4 倍，原因是交错级数的括号把下轨道与区间对另一端的项配对；窄区间对只相差若干个末位单位。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1136
msgid "**The arctangent leaf in fixed point.** On $[0, \\tfrac12]$ the series is evaluated as $\\arctan x = x - R(x)$ with $R(x) = x^3/3 - x^5/5 + x^7/7 - \\cdots$, increasing in $x$, so on a pair $[a, b]$ the enclosure is $[\\,a - R^{+},\\ b - R^{-}\\,]$ with $R^{-} \\le R(a)$ and $R(b) \\le R^{+}$. $R$ is computed with integers of $F = w + q + 20 + \\operatorname{bits}(w)$ fractional bits, where $q = -\\operatorname{top}(b)$: a lower chain $P^{-}_k \\le a^{2k+1} 2^F$ by floors and an upper chain $P^{+}_k \\ge b^{2k+1} 2^F$ by ceilings (each step multiplies by a floor or ceiling of the square and shifts, and a floor of a product of lower bounds, or a ceiling of a product of upper bounds, keeps the bound), then $T^{-}_k = \\lfloor P^{-}_k / (2k+1) \\rfloor$ and $T^{+}_k = \\lceil P^{+}_k / (2k+1) \\rceil$ by a division by a single word. For terms decreasing in size the partial sum after an odd number of terms is at least $R$ and after an even number at most $R$; with $A = \\sum_{k \\text{ odd}} T^{+}_k$, $B = \\sum_{k \\text{ even}} T^{-}_k$, $C = \\sum_{k \\text{ odd}} T^{-}_k$ and $D = \\sum_{k \\text{ even}} T^{+}_k$ this gives $R^{+} = A - B$ (odd partial sum, upper terms added, lower terms subtracted) and $R^{-} = C' - D$ (even partial sum, $C'$ without the last odd term), and the loop stops at an odd $k$ whose $T^{+}_k$ is below two units. Every floor or ceiling loses at most one unit and $x^2 \\le \\tfrac14$, so the chain errors stay below two units, each term is within three, and the whole enclosure within $1.5 F$ units of $2^{-F}$, which the 20 and $\\operatorname{bits}(w)$ guard bits cover relative to $x \\ge 2^{-q}$. For $q \\ge w/2 + 8$ the series is not run: $0 \\le R(x) \\le x^3/3$ and $x^3/3 < x\\, 2^{-w-14}$, so the enclosure is $[\\,a - b^3/3,\\ b\\,]$. Where the previous floating-point leaf ran four rounded `BinFloat` operations per term, a term is now two integer products and two single-word divisions: instructions retired for `atan`, `asin`, `acos` and `atan2` fall by 2.1 to 2.5 times at 53, 128 and 512 bits. The tests keep the floating-point leaf as a copy and check that the new enclosure contains the old one at 128 more bits (points, neighbouring and wide pairs, a pair starting at zero) and at both sides of the threshold $q = w/2 + 8$."
msgstr "**定点实现的反正切叶子。** 在 $[0, \\tfrac12]$ 上，级数按 $\\arctan x = x - R(x)$ 求值，其中 $R(x) = x^3/3 - x^5/5 + x^7/7 - \\cdots$ 对 $x$ 递增，所以在区间 $[a, b]$ 上包络为 $[\\,a - R^{+},\\ b - R^{-}\\,]$，其中 $R^{-} \\le R(a)$，$R(b) \\le R^{+}$。$R$ 用带 $F = w + q + 20 + \\operatorname{bits}(w)$ 位小数的整数计算，其中 $q = -\\operatorname{top}(b)$：下链 $P^{-}_k \\le a^{2k+1} 2^F$ 用向下取整，上链 $P^{+}_k \\ge b^{2k+1} 2^F$ 用向上取整（每步乘以平方的向下或向上取整值并移位，下界之积的向下取整、上界之积的向上取整都保持界），然后 $T^{-}_k = \\lfloor P^{-}_k / (2k+1) \\rfloor$ 与 $T^{+}_k = \\lceil P^{+}_k / (2k+1) \\rceil$ 用单字除法求得。对于逐项递减的项，奇数项之后的部分和不小于 $R$，偶数项之后的部分和不大于 $R$；记 $A = \\sum_{k \\text{ odd}} T^{+}_k$、$B = \\sum_{k \\text{ even}} T^{-}_k$、$C = \\sum_{k \\text{ odd}} T^{-}_k$、$D = \\sum_{k \\text{ even}} T^{+}_k$，得 $R^{+} = A - B$（奇数项部分和，加上界项、减下界项）与 $R^{-} = C' - D$（偶数项部分和，$C'$ 不含最后一个奇数项），循环在 $T^{+}_k$ 小于两个单位的奇数 $k$ 处停止。每次向下或向上取整至多损失一个单位，且 $x^2 \\le \\tfrac14$，所以链的误差保持在两个单位以内，每项在三个单位以内，整个包络在 $2^{-F}$ 的 $1.5 F$ 个单位以内，相对于 $x \\ge 2^{-q}$，由 20 位与 $\\operatorname{bits}(w)$ 位保护位覆盖。当 $q \\ge w/2 + 8$ 时不运行级数：$0 \\le R(x) \\le x^3/3$ 且 $x^3/3 < x\\, 2^{-w-14}$，所以包络为 $[\\,a - b^3/3,\\ b\\,]$。此前的浮点叶子每项做四次舍入的 `BinFloat` 运算，现在每项是两次整数乘法和两次单字除法：`atan`、`asin`、`acos` 与 `atan2` 在 53、128 和 512 位的指令数减少 2.1 到 2.5 倍。测试保留浮点叶子的副本，检查新包络在多 128 位的精度下包含旧包络（点、相邻点对、宽区间对、从零开始的区间对），以及阈值 $q = w/2 + 8$ 的两侧。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1138
msgid "**Where $\\pi$ comes from.** The binary-splitting $\\pi$ of this package is cached per working precision. `BinFloat` $+\\infty$ `.try_atan_ctx` returns the correctly rounded $\\pi/2$ from that cache, so `decimal` and `ball_float` obtain $[\\operatorname{RD}(\\pi), \\operatorname{RU}(\\pi)]$ from two calls (rounding downward and upward) and a scaling by $2$, which is exact: the same interval, bit for bit, as $4\\,[\\operatorname{RD}(\\operatorname{atan} 1), \\operatorname{RU}(\\operatorname{atan} 1)]$, since scaling by a power of two commutes with directed rounding. No public function was added for it."
msgstr "**$\\pi$ 的来源。** 本包的二分拆分 $\\pi$ 按工作精度缓存。`BinFloat` $+\\infty$ 的 `.try_atan_ctx` 从该缓存返回正确舍入的 $\\pi/2$，因此 `decimal` 与 `ball_float` 通过两次调用（分别向下和向上舍入）再乘以精确的 $2$ 得到 $[\\operatorname{RD}(\\pi), \\operatorname{RU}(\\pi)]$：它与 $4\\,[\\operatorname{RD}(\\operatorname{atan} 1), \\operatorname{RU}(\\operatorname{atan} 1)]$ 是逐位相同的区间，因为按 2 的幂缩放与带方向的舍入可交换。为此没有新增任何公开函数。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1147
msgid ""
"**`sinh`, `cosh` and `tanh` from one `exp`.** With $[L, U] \\n"
"i e^{x}$ from one kernel call and $0 < L$, the enclosure of $e^{-x}$ is $[1/U, 1/L]$ with directed divisions (the reciprocal is decreasing); if $L$ is not positive (an underflowed enclosure) the kernel is called on $-x$ as before. $\\sinh$ and $\\cosh$ then combine the four ends as before. For $\\tanh = s / c$ with $0 < c_0 \\le c \\le c_1$ and $s \\in [s_0, s_1]$ the quotient is increasing in $s$ and, for $s \\ge 0$, decreasing in $c$ (the reverse for $s < 0$), so the extremes are $s_0 / c_1$ if $s_0 \\ge 0$ and $s_0 / c_0$ otherwise (lower end), $s_1 / c_0$ if $s_1 \\ge 0$ and $s_1 / c_1$ otherwise (upper end): two divisions instead of eight. At arguments where $e^{|x|}$ leaves the exponent range the enclosures are the same as before ($\\sinh$, $\\cosh$) or $[0, \\infty]$ instead of a NaN end ($\\tanh$), and the public results did not change in the tests at those arguments."
msgstr ""
"**由一次 `exp` 得到 `sinh`、`cosh` 与 `tanh`。** 一次内核调用得到 $[L, U] \\n"
"i e^{x}$ 且 $0 < L$ 时，$e^{-x}$ 的包络为 $[1/U, 1/L]$，用带方向的除法求得（倒数是递减的）；若 $L$ 不为正（包络下溢），则像以前一样对 $-x$ 调用内核。$\\sinh$ 与 $\\cosh$ 随后仍用四个端点组合。对 $\\tanh = s / c$，设 $0 < c_0 \\le c \\le c_1$，$s \\in [s_0, s_1]$，商对 $s$ 递增，且当 $s \\ge 0$ 时对 $c$ 递减（$s < 0$ 时相反），所以极值为：下端当 $s_0 \\ge 0$ 时取 $s_0 / c_1$，否则取 $s_0 / c_0$；上端当 $s_1 \\ge 0$ 时取 $s_1 / c_0$，否则取 $s_1 / c_1$：两次除法代替八次。在 $e^{|x|}$ 超出指数范围的参数处，包络与以前相同（$\\sinh$、$\\cosh$），或为 $[0, \\infty]$ 而不是带 NaN 的端点（$\\tanh$），测试表明这些参数处的公开结果没有变化。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1149
msgid "**Corners by sign.** The product of two intervals $[a_0, a_1] \\cdot [b_0, b_1]$ is no longer the minimum and maximum of four rounded products. With $a$ nonnegative, the smallest $a b$ over the box is $a_0 b_0$ if $b_0 \\ge 0$ and $a_1 b_0$ otherwise (take the smallest $b$, then the $a$ that suits its sign), and the largest is $a_1 b_1$ if $b_1 \\ge 0$ and $a_0 b_1$ otherwise; a nonpositive $a$ is $-|a|$ and a mixed $a$ with a sign-definite $b$ swaps the roles; two mixed intervals still take the four corners. The quotient by a positive interval $[d_0, d_1]$ has the lower end $n_0 / d_1$ if $n_0 \\ge 0$ and $n_0 / d_0$ otherwise, and the upper end $n_1 / d_0$ if $n_1 \\ge 0$ and $n_1 / d_1$ otherwise. Directed rounding is monotone, so the rounded exact extreme equals the extreme of the rounded corners. One thing is not monotone: the sign of a zero end depends on which of several equal candidates the old code kept, so when an end is zero the old four-candidate form is used and the results stay bit-identical."
msgstr "**按符号取角点。** 两个区间 $[a_0, a_1] \\cdot [b_0, b_1]$ 的乘积不再取四个舍入乘积的最小值和最大值。当 $a$ 非负时，$a b$ 在该矩形上的最小值为：$b_0 \\ge 0$ 时取 $a_0 b_0$，否则取 $a_1 b_0$（先取最小的 $b$，再取适合其符号的 $a$）；最大值为：$b_1 \\ge 0$ 时取 $a_1 b_1$，否则取 $a_0 b_1$；非正的 $a$ 即 $-|a|$，符号混合的 $a$ 与符号确定的 $b$ 则交换角色；两个混合区间仍取四个角点。除以正区间 $[d_0, d_1]$ 的商，下端为：$n_0 \\ge 0$ 时取 $n_0 / d_1$，否则取 $n_0 / d_0$；上端为：$n_1 \\ge 0$ 时取 $n_1 / d_0$，否则取 $n_1 / d_1$。带方向的舍入是单调的，所以先取精确极值再舍入，等于对舍入后的角点取极值。只有一点不单调：零端点的符号取决于旧代码在若干相等候选中保留了哪一个，所以端点为零时仍使用旧的四候选形式，结果保持逐位一致。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1151
msgid "**Trigonometric functions: no reduction near zero, one series for a point.** If both ends of the argument enclosure lie strictly inside $(-\\pi/4, \\pi/4)$ (the lower bound of $\\pi/4$ is half the lower bound of $\\pi/2$, exact), then $x / (\\pi/2) \\in (-\\tfrac12, \\tfrac12)$ at both ends, the nearest integer is $0$ for both, the product $0 \\cdot \\pi/2$ is $0$ and the reduced argument is the input itself; the division by $\\pi/2$ and the multiplication back are skipped, and the result is the one of the general path. When the reduced pair is a point (equal ends) the series is evaluated once and its two ends are used for both bounds, as evaluating twice gives the same value; `tan` takes the quotient corner by the sign of the cosine enclosure (a negative cosine uses $n / d = (-n) / (-d)$). The same point shortcut is used in `exp2`, `exp10`, `pow`, `rootn`, `log1p`, `asinh`, `acosh`, `atanh`, `expm1`-based `exp2m1` and `exp10m1`, and `compound`: `binary_bounds_at_ends` takes the lower end of the evaluation at the lower argument and the upper end of the evaluation at the upper argument, and evaluates once when the two arguments are equal."
msgstr "**三角函数：靠近零时不约简，单点只算一次级数。** 若参数包络的两个端点都严格位于 $(-\\pi/4, \\pi/4)$ 内（$\\pi/4$ 的下界是 $\\pi/2$ 下界的一半，精确），则两端的 $x / (\\pi/2) \\in (-\\tfrac12, \\tfrac12)$，两端的最近整数都是 $0$，乘积 $0 \\cdot \\pi/2$ 为 $0$，约简后的参数就是输入本身；于是跳过除以 $\\pi/2$ 与乘回去的两步，结果与通用路径相同。当约简后的区间是单点（两端相等）时，级数只求值一次，其两端分别用作上下界，因为求值两次得到同样的值；`tan` 按余弦包络的符号取商的角点（余弦为负时用 $n / d = (-n) / (-d)$）。同样的单点捷径用于 `exp2`、`exp10`、`pow`、`rootn`、`log1p`、`asinh`、`acosh`、`atanh`、基于 `expm1` 的 `exp2m1` 与 `exp10m1`，以及 `compound`：`binary_bounds_at_ends` 取下端参数处求值的下界和上端参数处求值的上界，两个参数相等时只求值一次。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1153
msgid "**Trigonometric functions: one series at the midpoint of a reduced interval.** When the argument needs the reduction, the reduced enclosure $[\\ell, u]$ of $x - n \\pi/2$ has two distinct ends (it comes from both bounds of $\\pi$), and the enclosure of the series used to be the lower end of the series at $\\ell$ and the upper end of the series at $u$: two series evaluations. Sine and cosine are 1-Lipschitz ($|\\sin'| = |\\cos| \\le 1$, $|\\cos'| = |\\sin| \\le 1$). Take any value $m$ (here the midpoint $(\\ell + u)/2$ rounded to nearest at the working precision) and $h = \\max(u - m,\\ m - \\ell)$ with both differences rounded upward; then every $x \\in [\\ell, u]$ has $|x - m| \\le h$, so $|f(x) - f(m)| \\le h$ and $f(x) \\in [f(m)_{\\mathrm{low}} - h,\\ f(m)_{\\mathrm{high}} + h]$ with the two sums rounded outward, where $[f(m)_{\\mathrm{low}}, f(m)_{\\mathrm{high}}]$ is the series enclosure at $m$. Soundness does not need $m$ to lie in $[\\ell, u]$, since $h$ covers both distances whatever $m$ is. The widened enclosure is then clamped to what is known of the function: the range bounds $-1$ and $1$ for both functions (and the cosine keeps its upper end $1$ when $0 \\in [\\ell, u]$), and, for a sine whose reduced interval has ends of one sign, the sign (the lower end is at least $0$ when $\\ell > 0$, the upper end at most $0$ when $u < 0$). The clamp matters by this rule: a widened end that crosses a bound the true value sits on, or within the directed-rounding unit of at every work precision, never converges, while one that crosses a bound the true value is strictly inside of converges as refinement shrinks $h$. The cosine of a tiny argument is $1 - x^2/2$, closer to $1$ than the work precision resolves, so the unclamped upper end $1 + h$ lies above the breakpoint $1$ for ever and a directed rounding never reaches one value (the first form of this change returned an error, a NaN from `cospi`, for such arguments). No other result is of that kind: the sine of a point interval is not widened (its upper end is the series' own), and for the distinct ends of `sinpi` and `tanpi` of a tiny argument the widened upper end exceeds the two-ended one by at most one unit of the work precision, which is the strictly inside kind. No two-ended fallback remains. The endpoint $1$ is then decided by `binary_inexact_inner_endpoint`, inside `binary_certified_inexact_target_rounding` (the step of every refinement loop of these functions): the result is known not to be representable, so an enclosure end that is a rounding breakpoint of the target format is moved strictly inside, and $[1 - d, 1]$ certifies a directed rounding; the end $1 + h$ of the first form has far more bits than a breakpoint, so that step did not apply to it. The same holds for $-1$, which only the quadrant maps produce (as the negation of the capped cosine upper end). Near the bottom of the exponent range the ends and $h$ are rounded to the quantum of the work precision (a value of width $w$ stores nothing below $2^{e_{\\min} - (w - 1)}$); while at least 64 bits of the product lie above the quantum, $h$ is a few quanta against a midpoint of many bits and the lower end of the sine stays positive, and where fewer remain (the smallest subnormal of a wide precision used at a narrow one) the widened lower end can reach $0$ or below and is clamped at $0$, as the two-ended lower end was at most the quantum. One series is evaluated instead of two, the half-width enters the radius as an upper bound, and nothing else changes: `tan` takes the quotient of the two enclosures as before, so it needs no derivative bound of its own, and the widened cosine enclosure still excludes $0$ wherever the two-ended one did (the reduced argument is within $\\pi/4$, so the cosine is at least $0.7071$ and $h$ is a few units of the working precision). The new enclosure contains the exact value and is at most $u - \\ell$ wider on each side than the two-ended one (where the derivative is small the two-ended enclosure was narrower than the interval); $u - \\ell$ is a few units of the working precision (for a huge argument the ends are first rounded outward to the series precision, so it is of the order of the series error already in the enclosure), so the uniqueness test of the final rounding and the refinement loop are unchanged and can only retry when the result lies within $u - \\ell$ of a rounding boundary. The tests keep the two-ended function and check that the new enclosure lies inside the old one widened by $2 (u - \\ell)$ plus a few units, that both contain the enclosure at a working precision 256 bits higher, that `tan` declines exactly where the old one does, and a named test of an argument with an exponent of a few thousand. A sweep of `sin`, `cos`, `tan`, `sinpi`, `cospi` and `tanpi` of $\\pm 2^e$ and $\\pm 3 \\cdot 2^e$ for $e$ from $-60$ down to the bottom of the range, of the smallest subnormals of each tested precision and the quanta above them, and of floats just above, at and below multiples of $\\pi/2$, in the five rounding directions at precisions $2$, $3$, $24$, $53$ and $113$, pins every value and flag to the two-ended form, requires no NaN, and fails if a case takes more refinement rounds than the two-ended form plus one. Why the first form passed its tests: the random operands (1.26 million) and the huge-argument test never ran a directed rounding on a result within one unit of the range bound, so the enclosure above $1$ never mattered; a reviewer of a change that widens an enclosure should ask for the directed-mode sweep at the range bounds first."
msgstr "**三角函数：对约化区间在中点做一次级数。** 当自变量需要约化时，$x - n \\pi/2$ 的约化包络 $[\\ell, u]$ 有两个不同的端点（它来自 $\\pi$ 的两个界），而级数的包络过去是 $\\ell$ 处级数的下端与 $u$ 处级数的上端：两次级数求值。正弦与余弦是 1-Lipschitz 的（$|\\sin'| = |\\cos| \\le 1$，$|\\cos'| = |\\sin| \\le 1$）。取任意值 $m$（这里是中点 $(\\ell + u)/2$ 在工作精度上舍入到最近），并取 $h = \\max(u - m,\\ m - \\ell)$，两个差都向上舍入；于是每个 $x \\in [\\ell, u]$ 都有 $|x - m| \\le h$，所以 $|f(x) - f(m)| \\le h$，$f(x) \\in [f(m)_{\\mathrm{low}} - h,\\ f(m)_{\\mathrm{high}} + h]$，两个和向外舍入，其中 $[f(m)_{\\mathrm{low}}, f(m)_{\\mathrm{high}}]$ 是 $m$ 处的级数包络。可靠性不要求 $m$ 位于 $[\\ell, u]$ 内，因为无论 $m$ 在哪里，$h$ 都覆盖了两个距离。随后把加宽的包络夹在函数已知的范围内：两个函数的值域界 $-1$ 与 $1$（当 $0 \\in [\\ell, u]$ 时余弦保持上端为 $1$），以及两端同号的约化区间上的正弦的符号（$\\ell > 0$ 时下端至少为 $0$，$u < 0$ 时上端至多为 $0$）。夹取的取舍依据是这条规则：加宽后的端点若越过真值恰好位于其上、或在每个工作精度上都落在其定向舍入单位之内的界，就永远不会收敛；若越过的是真值严格位于其内部的界，则随着细化使 $h$ 缩小而收敛。微小自变量的余弦是 $1 - x^2/2$，比工作精度所能分辨的更接近 $1$，所以未夹取的上端 $1 + h$ 永远位于断点 $1$ 之上，定向舍入永远得不到唯一值（这一改动的第一版对这样的自变量返回了错误，`cospi` 给出 NaN）。其他结果都不属于这一类：点区间的正弦不加宽（它的上端就是级数自己的上端），而对微小自变量的 `sinpi` 与 `tanpi` 的两个不同端点，加宽后的上端至多比两端形式的上端大工作精度的一个单位，属于严格位于内部的一类。不再保留两端形式的回退。端点 $1$ 由 `binary_inexact_inner_endpoint` 判定，它位于 `binary_certified_inexact_target_rounding` 之中（这些函数每个细化循环的一步）：结果已知不可表示，所以属于目标格式舍入断点的包络端点会被严格移到内部，$[1 - d, 1]$ 即可认证定向舍入；第一版的端点 $1 + h$ 的位数远多于断点，这一步对它不适用。$-1$ 同理，它只由象限映射产生（作为被夹取的余弦上端的相反数）。靠近指数范围底部时，端点和 $h$ 被舍入到工作精度的量子（宽度为 $w$ 的值在 $2^{e_{\\min} - (w - 1)}$ 之下什么都不存）；只要乘积在量子之上至少还有 64 位，$h$ 就是几个量子，而中点有许多位，正弦的下端保持为正；剩下的位更少时（宽精度的最小次正规数用在窄精度上），加宽后的下端可以达到 $0$ 或更小，会被夹在 $0$，两端形式的下端至多是量子。于是只求一次级数而不是两次，半宽度作为上界进入半径，其他都不变：`tan` 仍取两个包络的商，所以它不需要自己的导数界，并且加宽后的余弦包络在两端形式排除 $0$ 的地方仍然排除 $0$（约化自变量在 $\\pi/4$ 以内，所以余弦至少为 $0.7071$，而 $h$ 是工作精度的几个单位）。新包络包含精确值，并且在每一侧至多比两端形式宽 $u - \\ell$（导数较小处，两端形式比该区间更窄）；$u - \\ell$ 是工作精度的几个单位（对巨大自变量，两端先向外舍入到级数精度，所以它与包络中已有的级数误差同量级），因此最终舍入的唯一性检验和细化循环不变，只会在结果距舍入边界不到 $u - \\ell$ 时多重试一次。测试保留两端形式的函数，检查新包络位于旧包络加宽 $2 (u - \\ell)$ 再加几个单位之内，两者都包含工作精度高 256 位时的包络，`tan` 恰好在旧形式拒绝的地方拒绝，并且有一个针对指数为几千的自变量的命名测试。一个扫描对 $\\pm 2^e$ 与 $\\pm 3 \\cdot 2^e$（$e$ 从 $-60$ 直到范围的底部）、每个所测精度的最小次正规数及其上的量子，以及恰在 $\\pi/2$ 的倍数之上、之处与之下的浮点数，取 `sin`、`cos`、`tan`、`sinpi`、`cospi`、`tanpi`，在精度 $2$、$3$、$24$、$53$、$113$ 的五个舍入方向上，把每个值和每个标志钉到两端形式上，要求没有 NaN，并且若某个用例的细化轮数比两端形式多出一轮以上就失败。第一版为什么通过了它的测试：随机操作数（126 万个）和巨大自变量的测试从未在结果距值域界不到一个单位处运行过定向舍入，所以高于 $1$ 的包络从未起作用；评审一个加宽包络的改动的人应当首先要求在值域界处做定向模式的扫描。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1155
msgid "**`rootn` and `rsqrt` by one integer root.** For $2 \\le |n| \\le 32$ (within the gate described below) the result is rounded in one step, without a Ziv loop. For a positive $x = c 2^{e}$ with $2^t \\le x < 2^{t+1}$, the top bit of $x^{1/n}$ is $k = \\lfloor t/n \\rfloor$ ($t + 1 \\le n (k + 1)$ because $t < n (k + 1)$ are integers); the top bit of $x^{-1/n}$ is $-k - 1$, or $-\\lceil t/n \\rceil$ when $c = 1$ ($x = 2^t$ exactly), by the same inequality on $1/x$. With $T$ the exponent of the last place of the rounded result (the subnormal grid included), take $g = T - 1$ (half a unit) and the integer $y = \\lfloor x 2^{-n g} \\rfloor$ (for $x^{1/n}$) or $\\lfloor 2^{-n g} / x \\rfloor$ (for $x^{-1/n}$); since $\\lfloor v^{1/n} \\rfloor = \\lfloor \\lfloor v \\rfloor^{1/n} \\rfloor$ for real $v \\ge 0$ (an integer $r$ has $r^n \\le v$ exactly when $r^n \\le \\lfloor v \\rfloor$), $r_2 = \\lfloor y^{1/n} \\rfloor$ (the integer square root kernel for $n = 2$, the integer Newton root otherwise) is $\\lfloor |x|^{\\pm 1/n} / 2^{g} \\rfloor$. The retained part is $r_2 \\gg 1$, the round bit is the low bit of $r_2$, and the sticky bit is \"the root is not exactly $r_2 2^{g}$\", which holds unless $y$ was exact (no dropped bits, no remainder) and $y = r_2^n$: a boundary of any rounding direction is a multiple of half a unit, so a root strictly between $r_2$ and $r_2 + 1$ is on the same side of every boundary as $r_2$ with the sticky bit set. `binary_round_pack` then decides the result and the flags as for the square root, including the subnormal range and the tininess rule after rounding (a second root on the unbounded grid when it differs). The integer has about $n (p + 2)$ bits and the Newton steps of its root raise a number of that size to the power $n - 1$, so the path is used only where it is measurably faster than the certified `exp(ln(x) / n)` loop, which gets the fast `exp` and `ln` kernels from about 1500 bits on. Instructions retired, loop divided by integer root: for $n \\le 12$ the integer root wins at every precision measured (53 to 32768 bits) by 2.4 to 300 times; for $13 \\le n \\le 32$ it wins by 6.7 to 49 times up to 1024 bits, but at 2048 bits $n = 16$ gains only 1.6 times, $n = 20$ 1.1 times, and $n = 24$ and $n = 32$ are 1.3 and 2.2 times slower. The gate is therefore $|n| \\le 12$, or $|n| \\le 32$ with context precision at most 1024 bits, and the loop elsewhere; the tests compare the public result with the loop on both sides of each bound. The exact roots of perfect powers are still decided before either path. Instructions retired per call (53, 128, 512 bits): `rsqrt` 57, 23 and 35 times fewer, `rootn` with $n = 3$ 2.1, 3.6 and 11 times fewer."
msgstr "**用一次整数开方得到 `rootn` 与 `rsqrt`。** 当 $2 \\le |n| \\le 32$ 时（在下文所述的闸门之内），结果一步舍入，不需要 Ziv 循环。对正数 $x = c 2^{e}$，$2^t \\le x < 2^{t+1}$，$x^{1/n}$ 的最高位为 $k = \\lfloor t/n \\rfloor$（因为 $t < n (k + 1)$ 都是整数，所以 $t + 1 \\le n (k + 1)$）；$x^{-1/n}$ 的最高位为 $-k - 1$，当 $c = 1$（恰好 $x = 2^t$）时为 $-\\lceil t/n \\rceil$，对 $1/x$ 用同一个不等式即可。设 $T$ 为舍入结果末位的指数（包括次正规网格），取 $g = T - 1$（半个单位）和整数 $y = \\lfloor x 2^{-n g} \\rfloor$（对应 $x^{1/n}$）或 $\\lfloor 2^{-n g} / x \\rfloor$（对应 $x^{-1/n}$）；因为对实数 $v \\ge 0$ 有 $\\lfloor v^{1/n} \\rfloor = \\lfloor \\lfloor v \\rfloor^{1/n} \\rfloor$（整数 $r$ 满足 $r^n \\le v$ 当且仅当 $r^n \\le \\lfloor v \\rfloor$），所以 $r_2 = \\lfloor y^{1/n} \\rfloor$（$n = 2$ 用整数平方根内核，其余用整数 Newton 开方）就是 $\\lfloor |x|^{\\pm 1/n} / 2^{g} \\rfloor$。保留部分为 $r_2 \\gg 1$，舍入位是 $r_2$ 的最低位，粘滞位是“根并不恰好等于 $r_2 2^{g}$”，除非 $y$ 是精确的（没有丢弃的位、没有余数）且 $y = r_2^n$，否则它成立：任何舍入方向的边界都是半个单位的整数倍，所以严格位于 $r_2$ 与 $r_2 + 1$ 之间的根与置了粘滞位的 $r_2$ 在每个边界的同一侧。随后 `binary_round_pack` 像平方根那样决定结果和标志，包括次正规范围和舍入后的 tininess 规则（网格不同时在无界网格上再求一次根）。该整数约有 $n (p + 2)$ 位，其 Newton 步要把这么大的数乘到 $n - 1$ 次方，所以只在明显快于经认证的 `exp(ln(x) / n)` 循环的范围内使用，该循环从约 1500 位起可用快速的 `exp` 与 `ln` 内核。指令数，循环除以整数开方：$n \\le 12$ 时在所测的每个精度（53 到 32768 位）整数开方都更快，快 2.4 到 300 倍；$13 \\le n \\le 32$ 时在 1024 位以内快 6.7 到 49 倍，但在 2048 位，$n = 16$ 只快 1.6 倍，$n = 20$ 快 1.1 倍，$n = 24$ 与 $n = 32$ 反而慢 1.3 与 2.2 倍。因此闸门为 $|n| \\le 12$，或 $|n| \\le 32$ 且上下文精度不超过 1024 位，其余用循环；测试在每个界的两侧比较公开结果与循环。完全幂的精确根仍先于两条路径判定。每次调用的指令数（53、128、512 位）：`rsqrt` 少 57、23 和 35 倍，$n = 3$ 的 `rootn` 少 2.1、3.6 和 11 倍。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1159
msgid "Trigonometric functions of huge arguments"
msgstr "超大参数的三角函数"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1161
msgid "`sin`, `cos` and `tan` of an argument $x$ with $2^{k-1} \\le |x| < 2^k$ reduce $x$ modulo $\\pi/2$, which cancels the top $k$ bits of $x$: the reduction needs $\\pi$ to $p + k + 96$ bits for a result of $p$ bits. The reduced argument lies in $(-\\pi/4, \\pi/4)$ and the series needs only the precision of the result, so for $k > 256$ the enclosure of the reduced argument is rounded outward to $p + 96$ bits before the series (the reduction and the series are separate precisions). The working precision of the reduction is limited to 8,000,000 bits, so that every argument of the decimal operand range ($10^{999999} < 2^{3321929}$) is evaluated; a larger work size is a `ResourceLimit` certification failure. The `decimal` driver passes a huge integer operand to `BinFloat` exactly (an integer $c \\cdot 10^e$ is a dyadic rational) at the result precision, and `ball_float` evaluates a point interval by two directed evaluations without the rational index computation."
msgstr "对满足 $2^{k-1} \\le |x| < 2^k$ 的参数 $x$，`sin`、`cos` 和 `tan` 先对 $\\pi/2$ 取模归约 $x$，这会抵消 $x$ 的最高 $k$ 位：对 $p$ 位的结果，归约需要 $p + k + 96$ 位的 $\\pi$。归约后的参数落在 $(-\\pi/4, \\pi/4)$ 内，级数只需要结果的精度，因此当 $k > 256$ 时，归约后参数的包络先向外舍入到 $p + 96$ 位再做级数（归约与级数使用各自的精度）。归约的工作精度上限为 8,000,000 位，使十进制操作数范围内的每个参数（$10^{999999} < 2^{3321929}$）都能求值；更大的工作规模是 `ResourceLimit` 认证失败。`decimal` 驱动把巨大的整数操作数精确地交给 `BinFloat`（整数 $c \\cdot 10^e$ 是二进制有理数），以结果精度求值；`ball_float` 对点区间用两次定向求值，不做有理数下标计算。"

#: manual/design/bin_float.md:1175
msgid "The cost grows faster than linearly in $k$ because $\\pi$ at $k$ bits is computed by binary splitting with a quasi-linear product (a call recomputes $\\pi$: the cache keeps no entry above 65,536 bits). Native release build, one call of `Decimal::sin_ctx` in decimal64 (`cos` and `tan` cost the same), `p = 53` for the binary rows, on a quiet machine, measured at commit `bdba3fd` (2026-11-20; later multiplication work may lower the numbers by a few percent):"
msgstr "代价随 $k$ 的增长快于线性，因为 $k$ 位的 $\\pi$ 用二分拆分和拟线性乘法计算（每次调用都重新计算 $\\pi$：缓存不保留超过 65,536 位的条目）。原生 release 构建，decimal64 下一次 `Decimal::sin_ctx` 调用（`cos` 和 `tan` 代价相同），二进制行取 `p = 53`，在安静的机器上、于提交 `bdba3fd` 上测得（2026-11-20；之后的乘法优化可能使数字降低几个百分点）："

