#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:89
msgid "Build intervals"
msgstr "构造区间"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:91
msgid "Choose the constructor by what you know about the value."
msgstr "根据你对该值的了解选择构造器。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:115
msgid "`from_bounds` and `exact` abort on invalid input (a NaN endpoint, reversed bounds, a non-finite point); their `try_` forms return the same condition as an `ArithmeticError`, and so does `try_new(center, radius)` for a non-finite center or a negative or non-finite radius. `new(center, radius)` is a constructor view: the stored value is always the endpoint pair, and `midpoint()` / `radius()` read the midpoint–radius form back as IEEE 1788-2015 12.12.8 defines it. The whole real line and the empty set are `BallFloat::entire()` and `BallFloat::empty()`."
msgstr "`from_bounds` 和 `exact` 在输入无效时（NaN 端点、上下界颠倒、非有限的点）中止；它们的 `try_` 形式则把同样的情形作为 `ArithmeticError` 返回，非有限的中心或为负或非有限的半径对 `try_new(center, radius)` 也是如此。`new(center, radius)` 是一种构造视图：存储的值始终是端点对，`midpoint()` / `radius()` 按 IEEE 1788-2015 12.12.8 的定义把中点–半径形式读回来。整条实轴和空集分别是 `BallFloat::entire()` 和 `BallFloat::empty()`。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:123
msgid "Enclose a decimal constant"
msgstr "包络十进制常数"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:125
msgid "`BallFloat::from_double(0.1)` encloses the binary64 number nearest to $0.1$, which is not $0.1$. To enclose the decimal value itself, round the decimal string once down and once up, and use the two results as bounds."
msgstr "`BallFloat::from_double(0.1)` 包络的是最接近 $0.1$ 的 binary64 数，它并不是 $0.1$。要包络十进制值本身，应把十进制字符串分别向下和向上各舍入一次，并以这两个结果作为界。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:152
msgid "Do this at every boundary where data enters from decimal text or from a rounded computation; inside the interval domain the guarantee is then kept automatically."
msgstr "在数据从十进制文本或经舍入的计算进入的每个边界都这样做；进入区间域之后，保证便会自动维持。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:156
msgid "Compute and read the result"
msgstr "计算并读取结果"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:158
msgid "The arithmetic operators return an interval that contains every result of the operation applied to points of the operands."
msgstr "算术运算符返回的区间包含该运算作用于操作数中各点的所有结果。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:182
msgid "Read the result with `lower_bound()` / `upper_bound()` for the endpoints, `width()` for $\\overline{x} - \\underline{x}$ rounded up, `midpoint()` for a representative point, and `is_common_interval()` / `is_entire()` / `is_empty()` for the shape."
msgstr "用 `lower_bound()` / `upper_bound()` 读取端点，用 `width()` 读取向上舍入的 $\\overline{x} - \\underline{x}$，用 `midpoint()` 读取一个代表点，用 `is_common_interval()` / `is_entire()` / `is_empty()` 判断形状。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:187
msgid "Compare intervals"
msgstr "比较区间"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:189
msgid "An interval stands for an unknown point inside it, so \"is $x < y$?\" has three answers: certainly, possibly, or certainly not. The relations say which."
msgstr "区间代表其内部某个未知的点，因此“$x < y$ 吗？”有三种回答：一定是、可能是、一定不是。各种关系给出具体是哪一种。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:216
msgid "`is_member` tests a point; `subset`, `interior` and `==` (the `equal` of IEEE 1788) compare sets; `DefinitelyLt::definitely_lt` and `DefinitelyLe::definitely_le` of Luna-Flow/arithmetic hold only when the order holds for every pair of points; `MaybeEq::maybe_eq` (and `Overlaps::overlaps`) holds when some pair may be equal; `disjoint`, `precedes` and `strict_precedes` are the relations of IEEE 1788 and are true for an empty operand; `overlap` gives the full IEEE 1788 classification of two intervals."
msgstr "`is_member` 检验一个点；`subset`、`interior` 和 `==`（IEEE 1788 的 `equal`）比较集合；Luna-Flow/arithmetic 的 `DefinitelyLt::definitely_lt` 和 `DefinitelyLe::definitely_le` 仅当该序关系对每一对点都成立时才成立；`MaybeEq::maybe_eq`（以及 `Overlaps::overlaps`）在某对点可能相等时成立；`disjoint`、`precedes` 和 `strict_precedes` 是 IEEE 1788 的关系，对空操作数为真；`overlap` 给出两个区间完整的 IEEE 1788 分类。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:224
msgid "Evaluate elementary functions"
msgstr "求值初等函数"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:226
msgid "Functions are evaluated so that the result contains $f(\\xi)$ for every $\\xi$ in the argument where $f$ is defined. Extrema inside the interval and poles are taken into account."
msgstr "函数的求值保证结果对参数中每个使 $f$ 有定义的 $\\xi$ 都包含 $f(\\xi)$。区间内部的极值点和极点都会被考虑在内。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:254
msgid "Every `*_interval` function has a total form, which always returns a valid enclosure at any precision, and most also have a `try_*_interval` form. They use the same kernel and give the same interval whenever the certified evaluation succeeds. When it runs out of its work budget the total form widens to the range of the function (for example $[-1, 1]$ for `sin`), and the `try_` form returns an `ArithmeticError` describing the failure."
msgstr "每个 `*_interval` 函数都有全函数形式，它在任何精度下都总是返回有效的包络；大多数函数还有 `try_*_interval` 形式。它们使用同一个内核，只要认证求值成功，就给出相同的区间。当求值耗尽其工作预算时，全函数形式加宽到该函数的值域（例如 `sin` 为 $[-1, 1]$），而 `try_` 形式返回描述失败的 `ArithmeticError`。"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:261
msgid "Round to a target format"
msgstr "舍入到目标格式"

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:263
msgid "`BallContext` describes a binary format (precision and exponent range). `apply_ctx` rounds an interval outward into it and reports what happened in `BallFlags`; to round the result of an operation, apply the context to it."
msgstr "`BallContext` 描述一种二进制格式（精度和指数范围）。`apply_ctx` 把区间向外舍入到该格式，并在 `BallFlags` 中报告发生了什么；要舍入一次运算的结果，把上下文应用到它上面即可。"

