msgstr "[外部基线结果](../../performance/bench/external.md)"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:1
msgid "bin_float tutorial"
msgstr "bin_float 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:3
msgid "This tutorial teaches you to compute with `BinFloat`, the arbitrary-precision binary floating-point type of `floating`: build exact values, run a calculation in an IEEE 754 format such as binary32 with its status flags, read and write interchange bits and decimal text, and call correctly rounded elementary functions. Every example compiles and shows its output. The mathematics behind the rounding rules is on the [design page](../design/bin_float.md), and every function is listed in the [API reference](../api/bin_float.md)."
msgstr "本教程教你使用 `BinFloat`——`floating` 的任意精度二进制浮点类型——进行计算：构造精确值，在 binary32 等 IEEE 754 格式下连同其状态标志执行计算，读写交换位模式和十进制文本，以及调用正确舍入的初等函数。每个示例都能编译并展示其输出。舍入规则背后的数学见[设计页面](../design/bin_float.md)，所有函数都列在 [API 参考](../api/bin_float.md)中。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:14
msgid "build an exact binary value"
msgstr "构建精确的二进制值"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:15
msgid "read decimal text without double rounding"
msgstr "读取十进制文本且不发生二次舍入"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:16
msgid "compute in binary16/32/64/128 and see the IEEE flags"
msgstr "在 binary16/32/64/128 中计算并查看 IEEE 标志"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:16
msgid "[`add_ctx` and the other `*_ctx` methods](#compute-in-an-ieee-format-and-keep-the-flags)"
msgstr "[`add_ctx` 及其他 `*_ctx` 方法](#compute-in-an-ieee-format-and-keep-the-flags)"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:17
msgid "decode or encode interchange bit patterns"
msgstr "解码或编码交换格式的位模式"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:18
msgid "convert a value from one binary format to another, with flags"
msgstr "把一个值从一种二进制格式转换为另一种，并给出标志"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:18
msgid "`convert_format` ([Read and write interchange bits](#read-and-write-interchange-bits))"
msgstr "`convert_format`（[Read and write interchange bits](#read-and-write-interchange-bits)）"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:19
msgid "print the shortest or a fixed-digit decimal"
msgstr "打印最短或固定位数的十进制表示"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:20
msgid "evaluate a correctly rounded `exp`, `ln`, `sin`, …"
msgstr "求值正确舍入的 `exp`、`ln`、`sin`、…"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:20
msgid "[the elementary functions](#call-elementary-functions)"
msgstr "[初等函数](#call-elementary-functions)"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:21
msgid "bracket a real number from below and above"
msgstr "从下方和上方夹逼一个实数"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:21
msgid "[directed rounding](#enclose-a-real-number-with-directed-rounding)"
msgstr "[定向舍入](#enclose-a-real-number-with-directed-rounding)"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:22
msgid "recover the rounding error of a product"
msgstr "恢复乘积的舍入误差"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:23
msgid "choose how underflow is detected"
msgstr "选择下溢的检测方式"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:24
msgid "write code for every scalar core"
msgstr "为所有标量核心编写代码"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:24
msgid "[generic traits](#write-generic-code)"
msgstr "[泛型 trait](#write-generic-code)"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:34
msgid "Import the package in your `moon.pkg` (the examples also use `Luna-Flow/arithmetic` as `@lf_arith` and `Luna-Flow/floating/def` as `@def`):"
msgstr "在你的 `moon.pkg` 中导入该包（示例还以 `@lf_arith` 的名义使用 `Luna-Flow/arithmetic`，以 `@def` 的名义使用 `Luna-Flow/floating/def`）："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:43
msgid "The smallest useful program divides one by three, once with 53 bits and once in the binary32 format, and prints both results as the shortest decimal that reads back exactly:"
msgstr "最小的实用程序计算一除以三，一次用 53 位，一次用 binary32 格式，并把两个结果都打印为能精确读回的最短十进制形式："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:60
msgid "The operator `/` rounds to nearest-even at the precision of its operands (53 bits by default). `div_ctx` rounds under the binary32 context and also returns the IEEE flags; here `inexact` says that one third is not a binary number."
msgstr "运算符 `/` 在操作数的精度（默认 53 位）下就近舍入（偶数优先）。`div_ctx` 在 binary32 上下文下舍入，并同时返回 IEEE 标志；这里 `inexact` 表明三分之一不是二进制数。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:66
msgid "Build exact values"
msgstr "构造精确值"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:68
msgid "A finite `BinFloat` is $c \\cdot 2^{e}$ with an integer coefficient $c$ and an exponent $e$. `make` takes both plus a precision; `to_string` prints the stored form `c p e`, which is exact."
msgstr "有限的 `BinFloat` 是 $c \\cdot 2^{e}$，其中系数 $c$ 为整数，$e$ 为指数。`make` 接收这两者以及精度；`to_string` 打印存储形式 `c p e`，它是精确的。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:88
msgid "Read decimal input with `from_string`, which rounds the decimal value itself. Converting through a host `Double` rounds twice when you want a precision other than 53 bits, and `from_double` faithfully keeps the host's binary approximation:"
msgstr "用 `from_string` 读取十进制输入，它对十进制值本身进行舍入。当你想要 53 位以外的精度时，经由宿主 `Double` 转换会舍入两次，而 `from_double` 会如实保留宿主的二进制近似值："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:107
msgid "Compute in an IEEE format and keep the flags"
msgstr "在 IEEE 格式下计算并保留标志"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:109
msgid "A `BinaryContext` fixes the precision, exponent range, rounding direction and tininess rule of an operation. The `*_ctx` methods return the value and the flags of that one operation; combine flags yourself to accumulate them."
msgstr "`BinaryContext` 确定一个运算的精度、指数范围、舍入方向和微小性（tininess）规则。`*_ctx` 方法返回该次运算的值和标志；要累积标志，需要自己合并。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:132
msgid "$120000$ exceeds the largest binary16 value $65504$, so the sum overflows to infinity. The product $10^{-7}$ lies below the smallest normal binary16 number $2^{-14} \\approx 6.1 \\cdot 10^{-5}$, so it is rounded on the subnormal grid and raises underflow. The rounding direction changes the overflow result: toward zero it stays at the largest finite value."
msgstr "$120000$ 超过了 binary16 的最大值 $65504$，因此和上溢为无穷。积 $10^{-7}$ 小于 binary16 的最小正规数 $2^{-14} \\approx 6.1 \\cdot 10^{-5}$，因此它在次正规数网格上舍入并引发下溢。舍入方向会改变上溢的结果：向零舍入时，结果停留在最大有限值。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:152
msgid "Read and write interchange bits"
msgstr "读写交换位模式"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:154
msgid "Use `BinaryInterchange` when a file or protocol carries binary16, binary32, binary64 or binary128 bit patterns. It never goes through a host `Double`, so signaling NaNs, payloads and binary128 survive."
msgstr "当文件或协议携带 binary16、binary32、binary64 或 binary128 位模式时，请使用 `BinaryInterchange`。它从不经过宿主 `Double`，因此信号 NaN、载荷和 binary128 都能完整保留。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:173
msgid "Encoding rounds into the format, so it returns flags as well. Decoding is always exact."
msgstr "编码会舍入到目标格式，因此也会返回标志。解码总是精确的。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:176
msgid "Classify a value"
msgstr "对值分类"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:178
msgid "`class_of` returns the ten-valued class of IEEE 754-2019 clause 5.7.2. A `BinFloat` has no format of its own, so the context says where the subnormal range starts."
msgstr "`class_of` 返回 IEEE 754-2019 第 5.7.2 条的十值类别。`BinFloat` 自身没有格式，所以由上下文说明次正规范围从哪里开始。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:196
msgid "The same value is normal in a context with a lower `e_min`. `is_finite`, `is_infinite` and `is_nan` need no context."
msgstr "同一个值在 `e_min` 更低的上下文里是正规数。`is_finite`、`is_infinite` 和 `is_nan` 不需要上下文。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:199
msgid "Print decimal text"
msgstr "打印十进制文本"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:201
msgid "`to_shortest_string_ctx` gives the shortest decimal that reads back as the same value in a format; for binary64 it matches the host formatter. `to_decimal_string_ctx` gives a fixed number of significant digits, rounded in the context's direction, and reports whether digits were dropped."
msgstr "`to_shortest_string_ctx` 给出在某格式下能读回为同一值的最短十进制形式；对 binary64，它与宿主的格式化器一致。`to_decimal_string_ctx` 给出固定位数的有效数字，按上下文的方向舍入，并报告是否丢弃了数字。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:223
msgid "Every binary number has a finite decimal expansion, so 55 digits print the binary64 value of `0.1` exactly."
msgstr "每个二进制数都有有限的十进制展开，因此 55 位数字能精确打印 `0.1` 的 binary64 值。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:226
msgid "Call elementary functions"
msgstr "调用初等函数"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:228
msgid "Each elementary function has a plain form, a `*_ctx` form and a `try_*_ctx` form. All three return the correctly rounded result. They differ only in how a domain error or an exhausted refinement budget is reported: the plain and `*_ctx` forms return a quiet NaN with `invalid_operation`, while `try_*_ctx` returns an `@lf_arith.ArithmeticError` that says what went wrong. The budget is twelve refinement steps by default; `context.with_refinement_limit(Some(n))` changes the count and `with_refinement_limit(None)` removes it (the working precision then stops at a cap of at least 8,000,000 bits), for a rare input that sits very close to a rounding boundary."
msgstr "每个初等函数都有普通形式、`*_ctx` 形式和 `try_*_ctx` 形式。三者都返回正确舍入的结果，区别仅在于如何报告定义域错误或细化预算耗尽：普通形式和 `*_ctx` 形式返回带 `invalid_operation` 的静默 NaN，而 `try_*_ctx` 返回一个说明出错原因的 `@lf_arith.ArithmeticError`。预算默认为十二步细化；`context.with_refinement_limit(Some(n))` 更改步数，`with_refinement_limit(None)` 取消步数限制（此时工作精度在至少 8,000,000 位的上限处停止），用于极少数非常接近舍入边界的输入。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:258
msgid "`sinpi(0.5)` is exactly one, and the function knows it: exact results raise no `inexact` flag."
msgstr "`sinpi(0.5)` 恰好等于一，函数也知道这一点：精确结果不会引发 `inexact` 标志。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:263
msgid "Enclose a real number with directed rounding"
msgstr "用定向舍入包络实数"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:265
msgid "Rounding toward negative and toward positive infinity brackets the exact result. This is how you build a guaranteed enclosure without an interval library:"
msgstr "向负无穷和向正无穷舍入可以夹住精确结果。这就是在没有区间库的情况下构造有保证包络的方法："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:290
msgid "`ball_float` packages this idea as midpoint–radius arithmetic; see the [ball_float tutorial](ball_float.md)."
msgstr "`ball_float` 把这一思想封装为中点–半径算术；见 [ball_float 教程](ball_float.md)。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:293
msgid "Use fused and exact IEEE operations"
msgstr "使用融合运算与精确 IEEE 运算"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:295
msgid "`fma` rounds $x y + z$ once, so it recovers the rounding error of a product. `remainder` is always exact for operands of one precision."
msgstr "`fma` 对 $x y + z$ 只舍入一次，因此可以恢复乘积的舍入误差。对于精度相同的操作数，`remainder` 总是精确的。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:313
msgid "The two-product error term is the basis of compensated algorithms (Kahan summation, double-double arithmetic); the design page shows why it is exact."
msgstr "两数乘积的误差项是补偿算法（Kahan 求和、double-double 算术）的基础；设计页面说明了它为何是精确的。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:316
msgid "Watch underflow and tininess"
msgstr "留意下溢与微小性"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:318
msgid "IEEE 754 lets an implementation detect tininess before or after rounding, and the choice changes the underflow flag for values just below the smallest normal number. `BinaryContext` lets you choose:"
msgstr "IEEE 754 允许实现在舍入之前或之后检测微小性（tininess），这一选择会改变略小于最小正规数的值的下溢标志。`BinaryContext` 允许你自行选择："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:343
msgid "The value is the same; only the flag differs. Hardware differs too: x86 detects tininess after rounding and ARM before rounding, and TestFloat checks both rules."
msgstr "值是相同的，只有标志不同。硬件也各不相同：x86 在舍入之后检测微小性，ARM 在舍入之前检测，而 TestFloat 会检查这两种规则。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:347
msgid "Write generic code"
msgstr "编写泛型代码"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:349
msgid "`BinFloat` implements the `@def.Floating` trait shared by all scalar cores of `floating`, and the checked and contextual traits of `@lf_arith`. Code written against those traits runs on `BinFloat`, `Decimal` and the other cores:"
msgstr "`BinFloat` 实现了 `floating` 所有标量核心共享的 `@def.Floating` trait，以及 `@lf_arith` 的 checked 与 contextual trait。针对这些 trait 编写的代码可以在 `BinFloat`、`Decimal` 和其他核心上运行："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:380
msgid "The contextual traits turn the IEEE `division_by_zero` and `invalid_operation` flags into errors and report the other flags as diagnostics. For a whole pipeline that stops at the first error, use [`bin_float_checked`](bin_float_checked.md)."
msgstr "contextual trait 把 IEEE 的 `division_by_zero` 和 `invalid_operation` 标志转换为错误，并把其他标志作为诊断信息报告。若要一条在第一个错误处停止的完整流水线，请使用 [`bin_float_checked`](bin_float_checked.md)。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:385
msgid "Performance"
msgstr "性能"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:387
msgid "Precision costs time roughly like integer multiplication of that many bits. The coefficient kernel switches automatically from schoolbook to Karatsuba, Toom-3 and number-theoretic transforms, so thousands of bits are practical. Elementary functions refine their working precision until the result is certain, and the first attempt succeeds for almost every input. Pick one precision for an algorithm instead of widening and narrowing repeatedly. The [performance page](../performance/bin_float.md) records measurements."
msgstr "精度带来的时间代价大致相当于同等位数的整数乘法。系数内核会自动从教科书乘法切换到 Karatsuba、Toom-3 和数论变换，因此数千位的精度也切实可行。初等函数会逐步提高工作精度直到结果确定，几乎所有输入都在第一次尝试时成功。请为一个算法选定一个精度，而不要反复放宽和收窄。[性能页面](../performance/bin_float.md)记录了测量结果。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:397
msgid ""
"**`==` compares representations.** `BinFloat` derives `Eq`, so `1` at 53 bits is not `==` to `1` at 24 bits, $-0 \\n"
"e +0$, and a NaN equals an identical NaN. Use `compare(x, y) == 0` for numerical equality, or `compare_quiet_equal` for the IEEE predicate."
msgstr ""
"**`==` 比较的是表示。** `BinFloat` 派生了 `Eq`，因此 53 位的 `1` 与 24 位的 `1` 并不 `==`，$-0 \\n"
"e +0$，而一个 NaN 等于与之完全相同的 NaN。数值相等请用 `compare(x, y) == 0`，IEEE 谓词请用 `compare_quiet_equal`。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:401
msgid "**`compare` puts NaN last.** It never aborts: every NaN compares equal to every NaN and greater than every number, so `nan > x` is true. Use `compare_checked`, `compare_quiet` or `compare_quiet_less` when NaN must be unordered."
msgstr "**`compare` 把 NaN 排在最后。** 它从不中止：每个 NaN 都与每个 NaN 相等，且大于每个数，因此 `nan > x` 为真。当 NaN 必须无序时，请使用 `compare_checked`、`compare_quiet` 或 `compare_quiet_less`。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:405
msgid "**Plain operators ignore your format.** `x + y` works at the larger operand precision with an exponent range of about $2^{\\pm 2^{30}}$; it never overflows at binary32 limits. Use `add_ctx` with a format context."
msgstr "**普通运算符不理会你的格式。** `x + y` 以较大的操作数精度计算，指数范围约为 $2^{\\pm 2^{30}}$；它绝不会在 binary32 的界限处上溢。请配合格式上下文使用 `add_ctx`。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:408
msgid "**`from_double(0.1)` is not one tenth.** It is the binary64 value the host already rounded. Parse decimal text with `from_string`."
msgstr "**`from_double(0.1)` 不是十分之一。** 它是宿主已经舍入过的 binary64 值。请用 `from_string` 解析十进制文本。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:410
msgid "**`to_string` is not decimal.** It prints `3602879701896397p-55`. Use `to_shortest_string` or `to_decimal_string_ctx` for people."
msgstr "**`to_string` 不是十进制。** 它打印 `3602879701896397p-55`。给人阅读时请用 `to_shortest_string` 或 `to_decimal_string_ctx`。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:412
msgid "**`from_hex` needs the `p` exponent and reports no flags.** `0x1.8p0` and `0x3p-1` are both $1.5$, but `0x1.8` is rejected, and an inexact conversion looks like an exact one; use `from_hex_ctx` (or `from_string_ctx` for decimal text) when the rounding direction or the flags matter."
msgstr "**`from_hex` 需要 `p` 指数，且不报告标志。** `0x1.8p0` 和 `0x3p-1` 都是 $1.5$，但 `0x1.8` 会被拒绝；不精确的转换看起来与精确转换一样，需要舍入方向或标志时请用 `from_hex_ctx`（十进制文本用 `from_string_ctx`）。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:416
msgid "**`with_precision` hides flags.** Use `round_ctx` when you need to know that narrowing was inexact or overflowed."
msgstr "**`with_precision` 会隐藏标志。** 当你需要知道收窄是否不精确或上溢时，请使用 `round_ctx`。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:418
msgid "**The sign of a zero is an input.** IEEE 754 special cases read it: `atan2` of $(-0, -1)$ is $-\\pi$ but of $(+0, -1)$ is $+\\pi$, `tanpi(1)` is $-0$, and $(-0)^{-1}$ is $-\\infty$. Keep zeros as they come; normalising $-0$ to $+0$ changes these results."
msgstr "**零的符号是一种输入。** IEEE 754 的特殊情形会读取它：$(-0, -1)$ 的 `atan2` 是 $-\\pi$，而 $(+0, -1)$ 的是 $+\\pi$；`tanpi(1)` 是 $-0$；$(-0)^{-1}$ 是 $-\\infty$。请按原样保留零；把 $-0$ 规范化为 $+0$ 会改变这些结果。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:425
msgid "[bin_float design](../design/bin_float.md): the error model, how correct rounding is decided, overflow and tininess, certified elementary functions."
msgstr "[bin_float 设计](../design/bin_float.md)：误差模型、如何判定正确舍入、上溢与微小性、认证初等函数。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:427
