#~ msgid "The derived `Eq` is structural, not numerical. Two values are `==` when sign, class, coefficient, exponent, precision and NaN state all agree, so `one(precision=53) != one(precision=24)`, `-0 != +0`, and a NaN is `==` to an identical NaN. Use `compare`, `compare_quiet` or `total_order` for numerical questions."
#~ msgstr "派生的 `Eq` 是结构相等，而不是数值相等。只有当符号、类别、系数、指数、精度和 NaN 状态全部一致时，两个值才 `==`，因此 `one(precision=53) != one(precision=24)`，`-0 != +0`，而一个 NaN 与完全相同的 NaN `==`。数值问题请使用 `compare`、`compare_quiet` 或 `total_order`。"

#~ msgid "Equality follows the type. `Decimal`'s `==` is numeric for finite values (`-0 == 0.00`) and treats two NaNs as equal. `BinFloat` and `BallFloat` derive `Eq`, so their `==` compares representations, including the sign of zero and the precision: `-0 == +0` is false there, while `compare` returns `0`. Use `compare(...) == 0` or `compare_quiet_equal` for numeric equality of binary values."
#~ msgstr "相等性取决于类型。`Decimal` 的 `==` 对有限值按数值比较（`-0 == 0.00`），并将两个 NaN 视为相等。`BinFloat` 与 `BallFloat` 派生了 `Eq`，因此它们的 `==` 比较的是表示，包括零的符号和精度：在这里 `-0 == +0` 为假，而 `compare` 返回 `0`。比较二进制值的数值相等性请使用 `compare(...) == 0` 或 `compare_quiet_equal`。"

