#~ msgid "*AGM alternative.* $\\ln s = \\pi / (2\\, \\mathrm{AGM}(1, 4/s)) - m \\ln 2$ for $s = v\\, 2^{m} > 2^{w/2}$ costs about $\\log_2 w$ iterations of one product and one square root. With today's kernels (`sqrt_ctx` 128 µs, product 43 µs at 8192 bits) this is 2.7 to 3.2 ms, no better than the Newton step within the model's error, because our square root is 29 times and our product 13 times slower than MPFR's (4.4 and 3.2 µs on the same machine, secondary evidence). It also needs a rigorous bound for the truncation error of the formula (the $O(s^{-2})$ term, derived from the theta-function formula $\\ln(1/q) = \\pi / \\mathrm{AGM}(\\theta_2^2(q), \\theta_3^2(q))$, attributed to Sasaki and Kanada, see the evidence note at the end of this section[^brent-agm]), which this page does not yet provide. It is therefore the second choice, taken up only if the Newton step measures slower than the projection."
#~ msgstr "*AGM 方案。* 对 $s = v\\, 2^{m} > 2^{w/2}$，$\\ln s = \\pi / (2\\, \\mathrm{AGM}(1, 4/s)) - m \\ln 2$ 约需 $\\log_2 w$ 次迭代，每次一个乘积和一个平方根。用现在的内核（8192 位下 `sqrt_ctx` 128 µs，乘积 43 µs），耗时 2.7 到 3.2 ms，在模型误差范围内并不比牛顿步更好，因为我们的平方根比 MPFR 慢 29 倍、乘积慢 13 倍（同一台机器上 MPFR 为 4.4 和 3.2 µs，二手证据）。它还需要该公式截断误差（$O(s^{-2})$ 项）的严格界，这个界由 theta 函数公式 $\\ln(1/q) = \\pi / \\mathrm{AGM}(\\theta_2^2(q), \\theta_3^2(q))$ 推出，该公式归于 Sasaki 与 Kanada，见本节末尾的证据说明[^brent-agm]，本页尚未给出。因此它是第二选择，只有在牛顿步的实测比预测更慢时才会采用。"

