#~ msgstr "`BallFloat` 的 `@def.Floating`"

#~ msgid "`BallFloat` implements the `Floating` trait of [`def`](def.md) with `classify`, `sign`, `precision`, `with_precision` and `normalized` as described above, so the generic predicates `@def.is_finite` (bounded), `@def.is_infinite` (unbounded), `@def.is_nan` (Empty) and `@def.is_zero` (sign `Zero`, that is, contains 0) apply to intervals."
#~ msgstr "`BallFloat` 实现了 [`def`](def.md) 的 `Floating` trait，其中 `classify`、`sign`、`precision`、`with_precision` 和 `normalized` 如上文所述，因此通用谓词 `@def.is_finite`（有界）、`@def.is_infinite`（无界）、`@def.is_nan`（Empty）和 `@def.is_zero`（符号为 `Zero`，即包含 0）也适用于区间。"

#~ msgid "The laws of `Floating` that speak of keeping a value hold only as enclosures: `with_precision` and `normalized` return supersets of the input (see the warning under [`BallFloat::with_precision`](#ballfloatwith_precision))."
#~ msgstr "`Floating` 中关于保持值不变的定律只在包络意义下成立：`with_precision` 和 `normalized` 返回输入的超集（参见 [`BallFloat::with_precision`](#ballfloatwith_precision) 下的警告）。"

#~ msgid "`Contains::contains(x, y)` is `y.subset(x)` (set inclusion, not the point-taking method); the others call the methods of the same name."
#~ msgstr "`Contains::contains(x, y)` 即 `y.subset(x)`（集合包含，而不是接受点的那个方法）；其他方法调用同名方法。"

#~ msgid "`flat_map` is the former name of `bind`. Replace `r.flat_map(f)` with `r.bind(f)`."
#~ msgstr "`flat_map` 是 `bind` 的旧名称。请将 `r.flat_map(f)` 替换为 `r.bind(f)`。"

#~ msgid "For the scalar types this is the IEEE class with signalling and quiet NaNs merged. For `BallFloat` it is `Finite` for a bounded non-empty interval, `Infinity` for an interval with an infinite endpoint (including the entire line), and `NaN` for the empty interval. Total; never aborts."
#~ msgstr "对于标量类型，这是将信号 NaN 与静默 NaN 合并后的 IEEE 类别。对于 `BallFloat`，有界非空区间为 `Finite`，带有无穷端点的区间（包括整条实数线）为 `Infinity`，空区间为 `NaN`。全函数；从不中止。"

#~ msgid "The interval rule also applies to unbounded intervals: $[-\\infty, -1]$ is `Negative`."
#~ msgstr "区间规则同样适用于无界区间：$[-\\infty, -1]$ 为 `Negative`。"

#~ msgid "[!WARNING] `BallFloat::sign` aborts on the empty interval, which has no sign. Test `@def.is_nan(x)` (true exactly for the empty interval) before calling `sign` on an interval."
#~ msgstr "[!WARNING] `BallFloat::sign` 在空区间上会中止，因为空区间没有符号。在对区间调用 `sign` 之前，请先检测 `@def.is_nan(x)`（当且仅当为空区间时为真）。"

#~ msgid "For `BallFloat` the endpoints are rounded outward (the lower one toward $-\\infty$, the upper one toward $+\\infty$), so the result is the tightest enclosure of `x` at the new precision. An interval whose endpoints are already representable at `p` bits is returned unchanged."
#~ msgstr "对 `BallFloat`，端点向外舍入（下端点朝 $-\\infty$，上端点朝 $+\\infty$），因此结果都是 `x` 在新精度下的最紧包络。端点在 `p` 位下已可表示的区间原样返回。"

#~ msgid "`BallFloat::normalized` normalizes the two endpoints and keeps them at the stored precision, so the interval denotes the same set: at 53 bits, $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ stays $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$."
#~ msgstr "`BallFloat::normalized` 规范化两个端点并将其保持在存储精度上，因此区间表示的集合不变：在 53 位下，$[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ 仍为 $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$。"

#~ msgid "Exactly one of the first three is true for every value. For scalars `is_zero` is true for both signed zeros. For a `BallFloat`, `is_zero` is true for every bounded interval that *contains* zero (for example $[-1, 1]$), not only for $[0, 0]$; use `BallFloat::contains_zero` or compare the bounds when you mean something else. `is_zero` never calls `sign` on an empty interval, because the conjunction stops at `classify`."
#~ msgstr "对每个值，前三者中恰有一个为真。对于标量，`is_zero` 对两种带符号零都为真。对于 `BallFloat`，`is_zero` 对每个*包含*零的有界区间（例如 $[-1, 1]$）都为真，而不仅限于 $[0, 0]$；若你指的是其他含义，请使用 `BallFloat::contains_zero` 或比较区间端点。`is_zero` 从不在空区间上调用 `sign`，因为合取在 `classify` 处即短路停止。"

#~ msgid "For an interval $X = [\\ell, u]$ the same question has three honest answers, and `BallFloat::sign` returns them as follows:"
#~ msgstr "对于区间 $X = [\\ell, u]$，同一问题有三个诚实的答案，`BallFloat::sign` 按如下方式返回："

#~ msgid "The three cases are exhaustive and disjoint for non-empty $X$ because $\\ell \\le u$: if neither $\\ell > 0$ nor $u < 0$, then $\\ell \\le 0 \\le u$. So `Zero` on an interval means \"contains zero\", and `is_zero`, which is defined through `sign`, inherits that meaning."
#~ msgstr "由于 $\\ell \\le u$，对非空 $X$ 这三种情形是穷尽且互斥的：若既非 $\\ell > 0$ 也非 $u < 0$，则 $\\ell \\le 0 \\le u$。因此区间上的 `Zero` 意味着“包含零”，而通过 `sign` 定义的 `is_zero` 也继承了这一含义。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Why (F6) holds for `BallFloat`.** A `BallFloat` stores its endpoints $\\ell \\le u$. `with_precision` rounds the lower endpoint toward $-\\infty$ and the upper one toward $+\\infty$ at $q$ bits, so $\\n"
#~ "abla_q(\\ell) \\le \\ell \\le t \\le u \\le \\Delta_q(u)$ for every member $t$, whatever $m$ is; the direction $m$ is not used. Infinite endpoints stay infinite, an endpoint that leaves the `BinFloat` range is rounded in its own direction as in IEEE 754, which still encloses, and the empty interval maps to the empty interval. $[\\n"
#~ "abla_q(\\ell), \\Delta_q(u)]$ is also the smallest interval with $q$-bit endpoints that contains $[\\ell, u]$, so the result is the tightest enclosure, and by the consequences of (F5) below it is the identity when $\\ell$ and $u$ are already $q$-bit numbers."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "**为什么 (F6) 对 `BallFloat` 成立。** `BallFloat` 存储端点 $\\ell \\le u$。`with_precision` 在 $q$ 位下将下端点朝 $-\\infty$、上端点朝 $+\\infty$ 舍入，因此对每个成员 $t$ 都有 $\\n"
#~ "abla_q(\\ell) \\le \\ell \\le t \\le u \\le \\Delta_q(u)$，与 $m$ 无关；方向 $m$ 不被使用。无穷端点保持无穷，超出 `BinFloat` 范围的端点按 IEEE 754 沿其自身方向舍入，仍然构成包络，空区间映射为空区间。$[\\n"
#~ "abla_q(\\ell), \\Delta_q(u)]$ 也是包含 $[\\ell, u]$ 的、端点为 $q$ 位数的最小区间，因此结果是最紧包络；并且由下文 (F5) 的推论，当 $\\ell$ 和 $u$ 已是 $q$ 位数时它是恒等的。"

#~ msgid "**Why (F7′) holds for `BallFloat`.** `normalized` normalizes the two stored endpoints, which changes their representation but not their values, and stores them at the interval's own precision $q$ by rounding the lower one down and the upper one up. Both are already in $\\mathbb{F}_{2,q}$, and rounding is the identity on its target set (see the consequences of (F5) below), so the result denotes the same set: with $q = 53$, $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ stays $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$. Rebuilding the interval from its centre and radius would not keep it: the centre $1 + 2^{-53}$ needs 54 bits, and rounding it to 1 and adding the error to the radius gives $[1 - 2^{-52}, 1 + 2^{-52}]$. The endpoint form also makes `normalized` idempotent on the set."
#~ msgstr "**为什么 (F7′) 对 `BallFloat` 成立。** `normalized` 规范化两个存储的端点，这只改变其表示而不改变其值，并以区间自身的精度 $q$ 存储它们，下端点向下舍入、上端点向上舍入。两者都已属于 $\\mathbb{F}_{2,q}$，而舍入在其目标集合上是恒等的（参见下文 (F5) 的推论），因此结果表示同一个集合：在 $q = 53$ 时，$[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$ 仍为 $[1, 1 + 2^{-52}]$。若从中心和半径重建区间则无法保持：中心 $1 + 2^{-53}$ 需要 54 位，将其舍入为 1 并把误差加到半径上，得到 $[1 - 2^{-52}, 1 + 2^{-52}]$。端点形式也使 `normalized` 在集合意义上是幂等的。"

#~ msgid "`normalized` keeps the representation-independent value: the number on scalars (F7) and the set on intervals (F7′)."
#~ msgstr "`normalized` 保持与表示无关的值：对标量是数值 (F7)，对区间是集合 (F7′)。"

#~ msgid "**`flat_map` is deprecated.** Use `bind`."
#~ msgstr "**`flat_map` 已弃用。** 请使用 `bind`。"

#~ msgid "The interval case shows why the NaN test comes first: the empty interval classifies as `NaN`, and `BallFloat::sign` aborts on it."
#~ msgstr "区间的情形说明了为什么要先检验 NaN：空区间被分类为 `NaN`，而 `BallFloat::sign` 在其上会中止。"

#~ msgid "`@def.is_zero` on a `BallFloat` is true for $[-1, 1]$: the predicate is defined through `sign`, which for an interval means \"contains zero\"."
#~ msgstr "对 `BallFloat` 而言，`@def.is_zero` 在 $[-1, 1]$ 上为真：该谓词通过 `sign` 定义，而它对区间的含义是“包含零”。"

#~ msgid "On a `BallFloat`, `with_precision` returns the tightest enclosure of the input at the new precision (the endpoints rounded outward), and `normalized` returns the same set. Neither changes an interval that is already representable at the target precision."
#~ msgstr "对 `BallFloat`，`with_precision` 返回输入在新精度下的最紧包络（端点向外舍入），`normalized` 返回同一个集合。两者都不会改变在目标精度下已可表示的区间。"

#~ msgid "A context holds a precision $p$, one rounding-direction attribute (`rounding`, a `DecimalRoundingMode`, the one the arithmetic uses), the adjusted-exponent limits $e_{\\min} \\le e_{\\max}$, the `clamp` switch, the `extended` switch and a tininess rule. No operation reads ambient state: every context operation receives its context as an argument."
#~ msgstr "上下文包含精度 $p$、一个舍入方向属性（`rounding`，类型为 `DecimalRoundingMode`，即算术实际使用的那一个）、调整后指数的限制 $e_{\\min} \\le e_{\\max}$、`clamp` 开关、`extended` 开关以及微小性规则。任何运算都不读取环境状态：每个上下文运算都以参数形式接收其上下文。"

#~ msgid "adjusted-exponent range"
#~ msgstr "调整后指数的范围"

#~ msgid "fold large exponents down to $e_{\\max}-p+1$"
#~ msgstr "将大指数折叠到 $e_{\\max}-p+1$"

#~ msgid "IEEE/extended arithmetic; `false` selects the GDA subset"
#~ msgstr "IEEE/扩展算术；`false` 选择 GDA 子集"

#~ msgid "when a result counts as tiny"
#~ msgstr "结果何时算作微小"

#~ msgid "`precision` must be in `1..=999,999,999`, `e_min` in `-999,999,999..=0`, and `e_max` in `0..=999,999,999`. `try_new` returns `Err(domain_error)` naming the invalid field; `new` aborts with a message that names it, like `BinaryContext::new`, so use `try_new` for parameters that come from outside. These bounds adopt decNumber's `decContext.h` limits and keep Etiny, Etop and context exponent arithmetic within `Int`. GDA 1.70 specifies no fixed exponent limit and requires a balanced range; this library does not enforce that balance rule."
#~ msgstr "`precision` 必须在 `1..=999,999,999` 范围内，`e_min` 在 `-999,999,999..=0` 范围内，`e_max` 在 `0..=999,999,999` 范围内。`try_new` 会返回指出无效字段的 `Err(domain_error)`；`new` 则以指出该字段的消息中止（与 `BinaryContext::new` 相同），因此来自外部的参数应使用 `try_new`。这些边界采用 decNumber `decContext.h` 的限制，并确保 Etiny、Etop 和上下文指数运算都在 `Int` 范围内。GDA 1.70 未规定固定的指数上限，并要求指数范围平衡；本库不强制该平衡规则。"

#~ msgid "The subset mode (`extended=false`) reproduces the classic decNumber subset: operands longer than $p$ digits are rounded first (raising `lost_digits`), zero results lose their sign and exponent, and special-value text is rejected. It exists for General Decimal Arithmetic test compatibility."
#~ msgstr "子集模式（`extended=false`）重现经典的 decNumber 子集：长于 $p$ 位的操作数先被舍入（引发 `lost_digits`），零结果丢失其符号和指数，特殊值文本被拒绝。它是为了兼容 General Decimal Arithmetic 测试而存在的。"

#~ msgid "These constructors return the interchange-format contexts and an exact working context."
#~ msgstr "这些构造函数返回交换格式的上下文以及一个精确的工作上下文。"

#~ msgid "All three use `RoundTiesToEven` by default (pass `rounding~` for another attribute), extended arithmetic and before-rounding tininess. `exact()` has precision 0, which means \"unlimited\": results keep every digit and no rounding by precision happens; its exponent range is the default one. It is the only way to obtain precision 0."
#~ msgstr "三者默认都使用 `RoundTiesToEven`（可用 `rounding~` 指定其他属性）、扩展算术以及舍入前微小性判定。`exact()` 的精度为 0，表示“无限”：结果保留所有数字，不按精度进行舍入；其指数范围为默认范围。这是获得精度 0 的唯一途径。"

#~ msgid "Precision, rounding and clamp are copied; a missing `e_min` or `e_max` becomes $\\mp 999\\,999\\,999$. The result is extended and uses before-rounding tininess. The conversion returns `Err(domain_error)` if precision is outside `1..=999,999,999`, `e_min` outside `-999,999,999..=0`, or `e_max` outside `0..=999,999,999`. These are the adopted decNumber `decContext.h` limits; GDA 1.70 itself sets no fixed limits and its separate balanced-range rule is not enforced here."
#~ msgstr "精度、舍入模式和 clamp 会被复制；缺少 `e_min` 或 `e_max` 时分别使用 $\\mp 999\\,999\\,999$。结果是扩展上下文，并采用舍入前微小性判定。若 precision 不在 `1..=999,999,999`、`e_min` 不在 `-999,999,999..=0` 或 `e_max` 不在 `0..=999,999,999`，转换会返回 `Err(domain_error)`。这些是本库采用的 decNumber `decContext.h` 限制；GDA 1.70 本身没有固定限制，本库也不强制其单独规定的平衡范围规则。上下文 trait 和 checked trait 实现均使用此转换。"

#~ msgid "`precision` is 0 only for `exact()`."
#~ msgstr "只有 `exact()` 的 `precision` 为 0。"

#~ msgid "Read and set the opt-in fold-down of a zero `quantize_ctx` result."
#~ msgstr "读取和设置零 `quantize_ctx` 结果的可选折叠。"

#~ msgid "Under `clamp` the largest encodable exponent is $e_{\\max} - p + 1$ (369 in decimal64). IEEE 754-2019 §5.3.2 says nothing about a `quantize_ctx` result that is zero and whose requested exponent lies above it (the target must not exceed $e_{\\max}$): by default the exponent asked for is returned and nothing is raised, as before (`quantize_ctx(0, 1E+380)` is `0E+380`). With `with_clamp_fold(true)` that zero is folded down to $e_{\\max} - p + 1$ and `clamped` is raised (`0E+369`), which is what decNumber does (`decQuantizeOp` calls `decFinalize` for a zero operand). `rescale_ctx` shares the path. The option is `false` by default and in every preset, has no effect without `clamp`, does not change a non-zero result, and takes part in `==`; every other operation that produces such a zero already folds, with or without it."
#~ msgstr "在 `clamp` 下，最大可编码指数是 $e_{\\max} - p + 1$（decimal64 中为 369）。IEEE 754-2019 §5.3.2 对结果为零且所请求的指数高于它的 `quantize_ctx`（目标指数不得超过 $e_{\\max}$）没有任何规定：默认返回所请求的指数且不引发任何标志，和以前一样（`quantize_ctx(0, 1E+380)` 是 `0E+380`）。使用 `with_clamp_fold(true)` 时，该零被折叠到 $e_{\\max} - p + 1$ 并引发 `clamped`（`0E+369`），这正是 decNumber 的做法（`decQuantizeOp` 对零操作数调用 `decFinalize`）。`rescale_ctx` 共用这条路径。该选项默认以及在每个预设中都是 `false`，没有 `clamp` 时无效，不改变非零结果，并参与 `==`；其他产生这种零的运算本来就会折叠，无论有无该选项。"

#~ msgid "`with_precision` replaces the precision (it aborts outside `1..=decimal_precision_max`, like `new`). `with_rounding` replaces the rounding-direction attribute. `with_tininess` replaces the tininess rule. `ieee754` returns the context unchanged: every context already follows the IEEE 754-2019 semantics of this package. `is754version2019` always returns `true`."
#~ msgstr "`with_precision` 替换精度（超出 `1..=decimal_precision_max` 时与 `new` 一样中止）。`with_rounding` 替换舍入方向属性。`with_tininess` 替换微小性规则。`ieee754` 原样返回上下文：每个上下文都已遵循本包的 IEEE 754-2019 语义。`is754version2019` 总是返回 `true`。"

#~ msgid "Rounding modes and tininess"
#~ msgstr "舍入模式与微小性"

#~ msgid "`DecimalTininessDetection` chooses when a non-zero result is tiny."
#~ msgstr "`DecimalTininessDetection` 决定非零结果何时为微小。"

#~ msgid "`BeforeRounding` (the default) calls a result tiny when the adjusted exponent of the exact result is below $e_{\\min}$, as IEEE 754-2019 §7.5 requires for decimal formats; `AfterRounding` uses the result rounded to $p$ digits with unbounded exponent and is a non-standard option for callers who want the binary-style rule. A tiny result raises `subnormal`, and also `underflow` when it is inexact."
#~ msgstr "`BeforeRounding`（默认）在精确结果的调整后指数小于 $e_{\\min}$ 时判定结果微小，这是 IEEE 754-2019 §7.5 对十进制格式的要求；`AfterRounding` 则使用在无界指数下舍入到 $p$ 位后的结果进行判定，是为想要二进制式规则的调用者提供的非标准选项。微小结果会引发 `subnormal`，若同时不精确还会引发 `underflow`。"

#~ msgid "The two rules differ only for results just below $10^{e_{\\min}}$. With $p = 3$, $e_{\\min} = 0$ and `HalfEven`, `plus_ctx` of `0.9951` and of `0.99951` are both tiny by default and raise `underflow`, `subnormal` and `inexact`. Under `AfterRounding` only `0.9951` is (its rounding to three digits is $0.995 < 1$); `0.99951` rounds to $1.00$ and raises only `inexact`."
#~ msgstr "两条规则仅对略低于 $10^{e_{\\min}}$ 的结果有所不同。取 $p = 3$、$e_{\\min} = 0$ 和 `HalfEven`，`0.9951` 与 `0.99951` 的 `plus_ctx` 默认都是微小的，并引发 `underflow`、`subnormal` 和 `inexact`。在 `AfterRounding` 下只有 `0.9951` 如此（它舍入到三位是 $0.995 < 1$）；`0.99951` 舍入为 $1.00$，只引发 `inexact`。"

#~ msgid "a subset-mode operand longer than $p$ lost non-zero digits"
#~ msgstr "子集模式下长于 $p$ 位的操作数丢失了非零数字"

#~ msgid "`DecimalContext::new` (precision up to 999,999,999)"
#~ msgstr "`DecimalContext::new` （精度最高 999,999,999）"

#~ msgid "conforming (the default is before rounding; `AfterRounding` is a non-standard option)"
#~ msgstr "符合（默认是舍入前检测；`AfterRounding` 是非标准选项）"

#~ msgid "the same, or $\\mp 999\\,999\\,999$ when absent"
#~ msgstr "相同；缺省时为 $\\mp 999\\,999\\,999$"

#~ msgid "with `extended = true` and before-rounding tininess detection (IEEE 754-2019 §7.5). So the predefined `ArithmeticContext::decimal64()` maps exactly to `DecimalContext::decimal64()`. The constructors pass the context through `DecimalContext::ieee754()`, the hook that selects the IEEE profile; on the current branch it returns the context unchanged."
#~ msgstr "并采用 `extended = true` 以及舍入前的微小性检测（IEEE 754-2019 §7.5）。因此预定义的 `ArithmeticContext::decimal64()` 恰好映射为 `DecimalContext::decimal64()`。各构造函数让上下文经过 `DecimalContext::ieee754()`，这是选择 IEEE 配置的钩子；在当前分支上它原样返回上下文。"

#~ msgid "`make(c, e, p)` returns $c \\cdot 10^{e}$ rounded to `p` significant digits and with trailing zeros removed."
#~ msgstr "`make(c, e, p)` 返回舍入到 `p` 位有效数字并去除尾随零的 $c \\cdot 10^{e}$。"

#~ msgid "The sign comes from the sign of `c`. Rounding uses `rounding` (default `HalfEven`), one of the eight modes of the context. Because trailing zeros are removed, `make(1200, 0, 34)` is `1.2E+3`; build from a string when the quantum matters. No flags are reported."
#~ msgstr "符号取自 `c` 的符号。舍入使用 `rounding`（默认 `HalfEven`），即上下文的八种模式之一。由于尾随零会被去除，`make(1200, 0, 34)` 为 `1.2E+3`；当量子重要时，请从字符串构建。不报告任何标志。"

