#~ msgid "Operands that both fit in four 32-bit limbs use the binary (Stein) algorithm. Larger operands use Lehmer rounds: each runs Euclid on the leading 63 bits of the larger operand and the bits of the smaller one in the same window, and takes one plain division step instead when the smaller operand has no bits in that window or the cofactors would not shrink the pair. A long operand is therefore reduced modulo a much shorter one in one step, and operands of any lengths finish. Below eight limbs of the smaller operand the loop continues with plain Euclid. JavaScript uses the host `BigInt`."
#~ msgstr "两个操作数都能放入四个 32 位 limb 时，使用二进制（Stein）算法。更大的操作数使用 Lehmer 轮：每一轮对较大操作数的前 63 位以及较小操作数在同一窗口中的位运行欧几里得算法；当较小操作数在该窗口中没有任何位，或余因子不会使这对操作数缩小时，则改为执行一次普通除法步骤。因此，长操作数会在一步之内对短得多的操作数取模约简，任意长度的操作数都能终止。当较小操作数少于八个 limb 时，循环改用普通欧几里得算法继续。JavaScript 使用宿主的 `BigInt`。"

