#~ msgid "On Native and LLVM squaring runs a word-range Karatsuba square from 36 64-bit limbs (three half-size squares $a_0^2$, $a_1^2$ and $(a_0 - a_1)^2$ instead of three products) and keeps the NTT square for 7168 32-bit limbs and above (measured crossover)."
