#~ msgid "[!WARNING] The BID encoder does not store the payload as an integer. It writes the payload with $p_{\\text{value}}-1$ digits, where $p_{\\text{value}}$ is the precision field of the `Decimal`, and keeps the *leading* $p-1$ of those digits (padding with zeros on the right when there are fewer). The payload survives only when $p_{\\text{value}}$ equals the format precision. For example, `NaN7` parsed with the default precision 34 encodes to decimal64 BID as `#7C00000000000000` (payload 0) while DPD gives `#7C00000000000007`, and a NaN with payload 7 and precision 7 encodes to BID payload 7000000000. Build NaNs with `Decimal::quiet_nan(payload=..., precision=p)` using the format precision before encoding them in BID. Tracked in [#54](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/floating/issues/54); no fix yet."
#~ msgstr "[!WARNING] BID 编码器并不把载荷作为整数存储。它以 $p_{\\text{value}}-1$ 位书写载荷（其中 $p_{\\text{value}}$ 是 `Decimal` 的精度字段），并保留这些数字中的*前* $p-1$ 位（不足时在右侧补零）。只有当 $p_{\\text{value}}$ 等于格式精度时，载荷才能保留下来。例如，以默认精度 34 解析的 `NaN7` 编码为 decimal64 BID 得到 `#7C00000000000000`（载荷为 0），而 DPD 得到 `#7C00000000000007`；载荷为 7、精度为 7 的 NaN 编码为 BID 后载荷为 7000000000。在以 BID 编码之前，请以格式精度使用 `Decimal::quiet_nan(payload=..., precision=p)` 构造 NaN。由 [#54](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/floating/issues/54) 跟踪；尚无修复。"

